{"level":30,"time":1778188588534,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24RPZ401PKSFH058JKR1EB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have the grouping file (EL-MD-EXP 1.md), the README with the site plan document list, and the facts.md. \n\nLet me understand the grouping:\n- This is about \"Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\"\n- The checklist has 47 items (EL-1.1 through EL-1.47)\n- It covers clearance requirements between overhead electric facilities and site features\n- Key clearance thresholds:\n  - 7.5 feet horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from primary, neutral, and secondary conductors\n  - 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors\n  - 16 feet vertical clearance for driveways (no truck traffic)\n  - 18 feet vertical clearance for roads with truck traffic\n  - 10 lateral feet from overhead distribution conductors for trees\n  - 50 lateral feet from overhead transmission conductors for trees\n\nThe project is \"Valley View Townhomes\" - a 39-unit multi-family townhome development at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check if this grouping is applicable to the project\n2. Gather evidence from site plan sheets\n3. Evaluate each checklist item\n\n**Step 2: Check Applicability**\n\nFrom the README and facts.md, I can see:\n- The project is a townhome development (39 units in 8 buildings)\n- The site area is 2.16 acres\n- There are site plans including electrical design (Sheet 21: Preliminary Electrical Design Plan)\n- There are landscape plans (Sheets 31, 35)\n- There are grading and utility plans\n\nThe key question is: Are there overhead electric facilities on or adjacent to the site? Let me check the electrical design plan sheet and utility information.\n\nLet me read Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) to see if