{"level":30,"time":1778188600723,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24SDWHPSV9BT0H02FQYETH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I can see from the blocks that:\n\nSheet 21 (Electrical Plan):\n- Shows transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters\n- All electrical is UNDERGROUND according to the description\n\nSheet 31 (Landscape Plan):\n- Shows utility lines including \"overhead electric (OHE)\"\n- This indicates there IS overhead electric on or near the site\n\nSo the key finding here is:\n1. The electrical design plan shows UNDERGROUND electric infrastructure for the development\n2. BUT the landscape plan indicates \"overhead electric (OHE)\" which could be existing facilities on or near the site\n\nNow, the critical question for applicability is: Are there existing OVERHEAD electric facilities on or adjacent to the site that the development must maintain clearances from?\n\nLet me look at the site plan blocks more carefully to understand if overhead electric is shown.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3251e5e3-3f03-4e85-9bab-d2e9039fdd51","uuid":"80969f51-d638-4ddf-bf6f-a38db22efc58"}
