{"level":30,"time":1778188609386,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Identify all transformer pad locations on this electrical design plan. For each transformer pad, provide: 1) Location on the site (relative to buildings), 2) Any clearance dimensions or labels shown, 3) Proximity to buildings, structures, trees, utilities, sidewalks, or other site features. Note the scale (1\" = 20') and indicate what measurements or dimensions are visible for transformer pad location, size, and spacing from other features. Are there any transformer pad detail callouts or specifications visible?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here is the detailed information regarding the electrical transformer pads.\n\n### General Observations\n*   **Scale:** The plan indicates a scale of **Scale 1\" = 20'** in the top right corner.\n*   **Dimensions/Spacing:** There are **no explicit numeric dimensions, setback distances, or clearance distances** written on this plan regarding the size of the transformer pads or their specific spacing from buildings, trees, or other features. Any measurements would have to be physically scaled off a full-size printed plan using the provided 1\" = 20' scale.\n*   **Specifications/Details:** There are **no detail callouts** (e.g., \"See Sheet XX for details\") or printed construction specifications for the transformer pads visible on this specific sheet.\n\n### Transformer Pad Locations\nI have identified four (4) distinct locations labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" on the site plan.\n\n**1. Transformer Pad 1 (Northwest Area)**\n*   **Label:** Identified by a callout box reading \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   **Location relative to buildings:** Located in the northwest corner of the site, directly west of **Bldg. 1** (near Unit 101/102).\n*   **Clearance Dimensions:** None shown.\n*   **Proximity to site features:**\n    *   Situated between the west elevation of Bldg. 1 and the western property line.\n    *   Very close proximity to a \"Sidewalk Easement\" (dashed lines indicating a sidewalk).\n    *   Adjacent to an \"Electrical Pull Box\".\n    *   Located near the drip line/canopy of an existing tree symbol.\n\n**2. Transformer Pad 2 (West-Central Area)**\n*   **Label:** Identified by a callout box reading \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   **Location relative to buildings:** Located directly west of **Bldg. 2** (near Unit 201).\n*   **Clearance Dimensions:** None shown.\n*   **Proximity to site features:**\n    *   Situated between the west elevation of Bldg. 2 and the western property line/Sidewalk Easement.\n    *   Adjacent to an \"Electrical Pull Box\".\n    *   Directly adjacent to an \"Underground Electric Line\".\n    *   Located very close to the canopies of several large existing trees near the entrance drive.\n\n**3. Transformer Pad 3 (Northeast-Central Area)**\n*   **Label:** Identified by a callout box reading \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   **Location relative to buildings:** Located between **Bldg. 5** (south of Unit 504) and **Bldg. 4** (northeast of Unit 404).\n*   **Clearance Dimensions:** None shown.\n*   **Proximity to site features:**\n    *   Situated in an island/median area separating the internal drive aisles and parking spaces.\n    *   Adjacent to an \"Electrical Pull Box\" and \"Electrical Meters\" panel location.\n    *   Directly adjacent to the curb line of the internal drive.\n    *   Located under/near the canopy of a large tree symbol.\n\n**4. Transformer Pad 4 (Southeast-Central Area)**\n*   **Label:** Identified by a callout box reading \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   **Location relative to buildings:** Located directly east of **Bldg. 7** (near Unit 704) and south of **Bldg. 6** (near Unit 601).\n*   **Clearance Dimensions:** None shown.\n*   **Proximity to site features:**\n    *   Situated in a landscape/median area at the corner of an internal drive aisle.\n    *   Adjacent to an \"Electrical Pull Box\".\n    *   Near \"Electrical Meters\" panel locations on adjacent buildings.\n    *   Directly adjacent to the curb line.\n    *   Located under/near the canopy of a large tree symbol.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1416,"outputTokens":856,"totalTokens":3924,"reasoningTokens":1652},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Identify all transformer pad locations on this electrical design pl