{"level":30,"time":1778188615410,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify:\n1. The location of overhead electric utilities (OHE) - show any lines, poles, or infrastructure marked as overhead electric\n2. The location of all proposed trees - identify each tree by symbol and location on the site plan\n3. The proximity between proposed trees and overhead electric infrastructure - note any trees that appear to be within critical clearance zones (typically within 15-50 feet of distribution/transmission conductors)\n4. Whether conductors or poles are clearly marked and dimensioned\n5. Any tree symbols with labels indicating species or type (SY=street yard, PL=parking lot, P=buffer, M=mitigation)\n\nProvide specific spatial relationships and approximate distances where observable.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
