{"level":30,"time":1778188628353,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Analyze the electrical design plan and identify: (1) All utility pole locations shown on the sheet; (2) Underground electric lines (trenches, duct banks, pull boxes) - their routes and locations; (3) Transformer pads or pad-mounted equipment locations; (4) Any reference to overhead electric lines; (5) Conductor positions or cross-arm configurations. Note whether this shows underground service only or if overhead lines are also depicted.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (21)"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188629109,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24T9SE22Y447FH56AZYWWF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! Now I have the tree list. I can see all the trees and their species. Many trees are marked \"Y\" for utility-compatible (Appendix F), but I also see several invasive trees (I) and non-utility-compatible trees (N). \n\nNow I need to look at the site plan visually to understand the proximity of trees to transformer pads. Let me use the vision tool to look at the site plans and electrical plan more carefully to measure the distances.\n\nSince the transformer pad locations are visual and the tree locations are also visual, I should measure the distances between specific transformer pads and nearby trees. Let me first visually examine the site plan and electrical plan to see which trees are near which transformer pads.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ee23800-1891-4c6c-9860-87ab169d6f67","uuid":"2c3cc7c1-48a2-4c58-a0d8-7bcd9316ead4"}
