{"level":30,"time":1778188630379,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine this electrical design plan and identify:\n1. Are there any overhead electric lines shown on this plan? If yes, describe their locations and routing across the site.\n2. Are there any electrical transformer pads shown? If yes, where are they located?\n3. Are there any utility poles shown? If yes, how many and where?\n4. Are there any pad-mounted electrical equipment visible?\n5. Are there any underground electric facilities marked or labeled?\n6. Generally describe the electrical infrastructure layout relative to the building locations and the overall site.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here are the detailed findings regarding the electrical infrastructure:\n\n**1. Are there any overhead electric lines shown on this plan? If yes, describe their locations and routing across the site.**\nYes. There is a dashed line labeled exactly **\"-OHE-\"** running north-south. This line is located just outside the western (left) property boundary line of the site. It does not appear to cross internally over the proposed townhome buildings.\n\n**2. Are there any electrical transformer pads shown? If yes, where are they located?**\nYes, there are four specific locations marked with blue rectangular boxes and labeled exactly **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. They are located as follows:\n*   On the west side of the site, in the landscaped area west of Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 2.\n*   On the west side of the site, in the landscaped area west of Bldg. 8.\n*   On the east side of the site, between the parking area and the eastern property line, located roughly between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 5.\n*   On the east side of the site, between the parking area and the eastern property line, located roughly between Bldg. 6 and Bldg. 7.\n\n**3. Are there any utility poles shown? If yes, how many and where?**\nAlong the **\"-OHE-\"** (overhead electric) line running outside the western boundary, there are at least three small circular symbols containing a crosshair pattern, which is standard symbology for utility poles.\n*   One is located near the northwest corner of the property boundary.\n*   One is located near the midpoint of the western property boundary.\n*   One is located near the southwest corner of the property boundary.\n\n**4. Are there any pad-mounted electrical equipment visible?**\nYes. The primary pieces of pad-mounted equipment explicitly labeled as such are the four **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** locations detailed in the answer to question 2. *(Note: The plan also shows \"Electrical Pull Box\" locations and \"Electrical Meters,\" but pull boxes are typically flush with grade rather than pad-mounted, and the meters appear to be wall-mounted to the buildings).*\n\n**5. Are there any underground electric facilities marked or labeled?**\nYes, the primary electrical distribution throughout the interior of the site is routed underground, represented by thick, solid blue lines. There are two specific instances where leader lines point to these blue lines with the exact label **\"Underground Electric Line\"**:\n*   One label points to the blue line routing near the northwest corner of the inner driveway loop, north of Bldg. 1.\n*   A second label points to the blue line routing on the east side of the site, between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 6.\n*   Additionally, the underground system includes numerous points labeled exactly **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** (represented by blue circles containing the letter 'E'), which are underground access points.\n\n**6. Generally describe the electrical infrastructure layout relative to the building locations and the overall site.**\nThe electrical infrastructure (highlighted in blue) forms a distribution network that generally follows the interior driveways and parking areas to service the eight residential buildings.\n*   **Routing:** A main underground electric line (solid blue line) loops through the site, seemingly originating near the southern boundary and routing northwards along both the western and eastern sides of the central building clusters.\n*   **Step-Down:** This main line connects to the four designated **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** locations, which are strategically placed on the outer perimeters of the building clusters (two on the west, two on the east).\n*   **Access:** Numerous **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** locations are situated along the underground lines, primarily at corners, junctions, or near transformer pads to allow for cable pulling and routing.\n*   **Service Delivery:** From the main distribution lines or transformers, connections are routed directly to **\"Electrical Meters\"** (marked as blue rectangles). There is a designated meter bank attached to the exterior of every single building (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) to provide service to the individual units.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1428,"outputTokens":882,"totalTokens":4875,"reasoningTokens":2565},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, loo