{"level":30,"time":1778188641036,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Examine the existing conditions survey drawing and identify: 1) Are there any overhead utility lines shown on this sheet? If yes, where are they located (north, south, east, west side of property)? 2) Are there utility poles shown? 3) What are the electric easement locations? 4) Are there any transformers or other electric equipment shown? Describe all overhead electric facilities visible on this existing conditions survey.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided existing conditions survey drawing, here are the details regarding the electrical utilities requested:\n\n**1) Are there any overhead utility lines shown on this sheet? If yes, where are they located (north, south, east, west side of property)?**\n*   **Yes**, there are overhead utility lines shown.\n*   **Locations:**\n    *   **West Side:** There is a continuous overhead line running North-South along the western boundary of the property, adjacent to and partially within the right-of-way for Valley View Road. The linetype includes \"- OHE -\" and is also explicitly labeled with the text \"OVERHEAD ELECTRIC\".\n    *   **South Side:** An overhead line branches off from the southwest corner and runs East-West along or very near the southern property boundary. This line is also labeled \"OVERHEAD ELECTRIC\".\n\n**2) Are there utility poles shown?**\n*   **Yes**, utility poles are shown and indicated by the symbol \"U.P.\" as defined in the legend.\n*   They are located along the overhead electric lines described above:\n    *   Near the northwest corner of the property along Valley View Road.\n    *   Midway along the western boundary along Valley View Road.\n    *   Near the southwest corner of the property.\n    *   Further east along the southern property boundary line.\n\n**3) What are the electric easement locations?**\n*   Specific electric easements are explicitly labeled on the drawing in the following locations:\n    *   **North boundary:** Labeled exactly as `\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 9116, PG. 734 P.R.T.C.TX.\"` running along the top/northern property line.\n    *   **South boundary:** Labeled exactly as `\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 9116, PG. 734 P.R.T.C.TX.\"` running along the bottom/southern property line.\n    *   **East boundary (partial):** The same label `\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 9116, PG. 734 P.R.T.C.TX.\"` appears near the southeast corner, indicating the easement likely follows that eastern property line segment as well.\n\n**4) Are there any transformers or other electric equipment shown?**\n*   **No**. Based on a scan of the drawing for the \"TRANSFORMER ON PAD\" (a rectangle with a 'T') and \"ELECTRIC METER\" (a circle with 'EM') symbols defined in the legend, there are no transformers or electric meters visibly marked on this specific sheet.\n\n**Summary Description of Visible Overhead Electric Facilities:**\nThe visible overhead electric facilities consist of an \"OVERHEAD ELECTRIC\" line (- OHE -) that enters the site plan area from the north, running south along the western property boundary parallel to Valley View Road. This line is supported by several utility poles (\"U.P.\"), some of which are shown with attached guy wires. Near the southwest corner of the site, the overhead line connects to a pole and continues eastward, running along the southern boundary of the property. There are dedicated 5-foot electric easements mapped along the north, south, and portions of the east property lines to accommodate utility infrastructure, though no surface-level equipment like transformers are drawn within them on this survey.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1398,"outputTokens":714,"totalTokens":6672,"reasoningTokens":4560},