slands:** At least one tree is shown in a landscape island within the northern parking row.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** A few scattered trees near the northeastern corner and southeastern corner.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** A row of trees planted along the property line, directly adjacent to the OHE line.\n\n**3. Proximity between proposed trees and overhead electric infrastructure**\nThere is a direct and close spatial relationship between proposed trees and the OHE line on the southern boundary.\n*   There are three distinct tree symbols planted in the landscape buffer along the southern property line.\n*   The graphical representation of the tree canopies (the outer circles of the symbols) for all three of these trees physically overlaps or directly touches the line marked **\"OHE\"**.\n*   Based on the scale provided (\"SCALE IN FEET 1\"=20'-0\"\"), the center points (trunks) of these trees appear to be located very close to the OHE line—visually appearing to be well within a 15 to 50-foot critical clearance zone, likely within 10-15 feet horizontally.\n\n**4. Marking and dimensioning of conductors or poles**\n*   **Conductors/Lines:** The general path is marked with a line and the text **\"OHE\"**.\n*   **Poles:** There are no distinct, standard symbols clearly identifiable as utility poles along the OHE line.\n*   **Dimensions:** There are **no dimensions**, height callouts, voltage markers, or specific clearance requirements noted or attached to the OHE line on this specific landscape plan sheet.\n\n**5. Tree symbols with labels indicating species or type**\nBased on the definitions located below the \"KEY NOTES\" section (SY, PL, P, M), specific labels are found inside or adjacent to the tree symbols on the plan:\n*   **Western Boundary (Street Yard):** The large trees in the shaded area contain the label **\"SY/M\"**. A smaller circular symbol contains the label **\"P\"**.\n*   **Northern Boundary:** The cluster of trees along the top edge contains multiple 