{"level":30,"time":1778188649622,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24TWBPC2RYNNWZJ9K1FG6K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014rauLZu3FWAkffB51iV8Ar","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the Site Plan drawing and determine: 1) Are the overhead electric lines and utility poles from the existing conditions (shown on Sheet 4) depicted on this proposed site plan? 2) What is the proximity of the proposed buildings (particularly Buildings 1-8) to any overhead electric lines? 3) Are there any clearance dimension annotations shown from overhead utilities to buildings, driveways, or other features? 4) Are there any notes regarding overhead electric line relocation, adjustments, or clearances? Please describe what you observe about the relationship between the proposed development and any overhead electric facilities that may still be present."}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4476681c-aa5e-420f-bcfe-9f06ce103f91","uuid":"768c83e4-d3b2-4875-aa4f-f12681abc38a"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188649677,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the Site Plan drawing and determine: 1) Are the overhead electric lines and utility poles from the existing conditions (shown on Sheet 4) depicted on this proposed site plan? 2) What is the proximity of the proposed buildings (particularly Buildings 1-8) to any overhead electric lines? 3) Are there any clearance dimension annotations shown from overhead utilities to buildings, driveways, or other features? 4) Are there any notes regarding overhead electric line relocation, adjustments, or clearances? Please describe what you observe about the relationship between the proposed development and any overhead electric facilities that may still be present.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (9)"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188652621,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24TTGV4RMM50055BHX46R0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very important! The vision report shows that:\n\n1. Overhead electric (OHE) runs along the entire southern boundary of the site\n2. There are trees planted along the southern property line that are directly adjacent to the OHE line\n3. The tree canopies appear to physically overlap the OHE line on the drawing\n4. No poles or dimensions are clearly marked\n5. The three trees near the OHE are mitigation trees (M symbol)\n6. There are no clearance dimensions or notes on the landscape plan\n\nThis suggests potential violations of EL-2.14 (trees not shown in relation to facilities preventing verification) and possibly other clearance violations. However, I need more information:\n\n1. What are the species of these southern boundary trees?\n2. Are they utility-compatible?\n3. What is the actual distance?\n4. Is there overhead electric infrastructure on the plan - is it a transmission or distribution line?\n5. Where are the poles?\n\nLet me check the landscape blocks more carefully to see if there's a legend showing which trees are which species. Let me also check if the plant list in Sheet 35 matches the symbols.\n\nActually, looking back at the vision report, it says the scale is 1\" = 20' (which I confirmed in the guides). And it says the center points appear to be within 10-15 feet horizontally of the OHE line.\n\nBut I need to know:\n1. What are the species of those southern boundary trees?\n2. Are they utility-compatible?\n\nThe vision report only tells me they are labeled \"M\" (mitigation) but doesn't tell me what species. Let me check if there's a key or legend in the landscape plan that shows which symbols correspond to which species.\n\nLooking back at Sheet 31 blocks.md, I saw Block 5 which has the key notes:\n- SY - STREET YARD TREE\n\n\n- PL - PARKING LOT TREE\n- P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n- M - MITIGATION TREE\n\nThis identifies the tree categories but not the actual species. I need to cross-reference Sheet 35 to find what species are assigned to the M symbol. Checking Block 11 and 17 on that sheet, I can see shade trees like Live Oak and Cedar Elm, plus ornamental varieties like Texas Mountain Laurel and Mexican Redbud, each with their own symbols. I need to determine which of these species are the mitigation trees planted along the southern boundary.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c5d1be6-7d35-4fa2-8909-ba4ff47d7c41","uuid":"c99564d0-cc43-4ca4-ad34-f280b9120beb"}
