{"level":30,"time":1778188661978,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine this site plan carefully for overhead electric utility infrastructure. Look for overhead electric lines, poles, conductors, or guy wires labeled \"OHE,\" \"overhead electric,\" or similar. Identify their routing, location relative to buildings and site features, and any dimensions or clearance annotations showing distances from buildings, driveways, parking areas, or other site improvements. Note the southern boundary area carefully. Also check if there are any easement boundaries or notes indicating electric facility locations or required clearances.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding overhead electric utility infrastructure:\n\n**Overhead Electric Lines (OHE) Routing & Location:**\n*   A utility line clearly labeled with repeating **\"- OHE -\"** text and dashed lines runs horizontally across the entire southern boundary of the site plan.\n*   This line runs east-west, parallel to and just inside or along the southern property line (which is marked with the bearing and distance `N88° 30' 57\" W  414.24'`).\n*   There are no other overhead electric lines visible crossing the interior of the site or running along the northern, western, or eastern boundaries.\n\n**Poles and Guy Wires:**\n*   There are utility poles (represented by circular symbols) situated along this southern `- OHE -` line. \n*   One pole is located at the far southwest corner of the site near the \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" note.\n*   Another pole is located roughly midway along the southern boundary.\n*   A third pole is located near the southeast corner of the site plan. Extending from this easternmost pole is a line explicitly labeled **\"guy\"**, indicating a guy wire anchoring the pole to the southeast.\n\n**Clearance Annotations and Dimensions:**\n*   While Building 7 and Building 8 are the closest structures to this southern OHE line, there are **no explicit clearance annotations**, radial clearance arcs, or dimension lines specifically denoting required distances or clearances from the OHE line/poles to the buildings, driveways, or other site improvements on this particular page.\n\n**Easements and Related Electric Facilities:**\n*   **Southeast Corner:** Near the easternmost pole on the southern boundary, there is a callout for an easement pointing toward the property line labeled exactly: **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5168, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** Along the eastern property line (adjacent to \"Existing Apartment Building\"), there is a callout pointing to the boundary labeled exactly: **\"3' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Western Area:** On the western side of the site, adjacent to Building 1 and near the driveway, there is a rectangular feature labeled exactly: **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** and just below it, **\"need to look up approp. detail\"**.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1407,"outputTokens":552,"totalTokens":3694,"reasoningTokens":1735},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this site plan carefully for overhead electric utility infrastructure. Look for overhead electric lines, poles, conductors, or guy wires labeled \"OHE,\" \"overhead electric,\" or similar. Identify their routing, location relative to buildings and site features, and any dimensions or clearance annotations showing distances from buildings, driveways, parking areas, or other site improvements. Note the southern boundary area carefully. Also check if there are any easement boundaries or notes indicating electric facility locations or required clearances."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-Ami62w12r79S5UIDn1B27U57","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anth