{"level":30,"time":1778188666433,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the main Site Plan and identify:\n1. Fire hydrant locations on the site\n2. Building footprints and their spatial relationship to driveways and parking areas\n3. Retaining walls and their locations\n4. Any visible utility easement boundaries or annotations\n5. Sidewalk/pedestrian areas and their separation from buildings\n6. The location and extent of the detention pond\n7. Property lines and right-of-way areas\n8. Any fences, bollards, or protective barriers shown\nProvide compass directions and specific building references.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Site Plan, here are the details corresponding to your requested points.\n\n**1. Fire Hydrant Locations on the Site**\nFire hydrants (denoted by \"FH\" and standard cross-circle symbols) are located in the following areas:\n*   **Northwest Corner (Off-site/ROW):** Near the northernmost driveway entrance, off the main road, labeled with \"FH (Out): 682.03\" and \"FH (In): 682.33\".\n*   **Southwest Corner:** Just east of the property line, north of the southern driveway entrance, an \"FH\" symbol is visible with a leader line pointing to it.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** Midway down the eastern property line, east of Building 6, an \"FH\" symbol is explicitly labeled near the 5' Electric Easement.\n\n**2. Building Footprints and Spatial Relationships**\nThe site features 8 rectangular building footprints, with internal drives and surface parking (garages/driveways) looping around them:\n*   **Bldg. 1 (3,290 sf):** Northwest corner, north of the northern entrance drive.\n*   **Bldg. 2 (4,830 sf):** West side, directly south of the northern entrance drive.\n*   **Bldg. 3 (4,144 sf):** North-central area, east of Bldg. 1, connected by a central pedestrian area.\n*   **Bldg. 4 (4,144 sf):** Central area, south of Bldg. 3.\n*   **Bldg. 5 (3,290 sf):** Northeast side, south of the detention pond area.\n*   **Bldg. 6 (3,290 sf):** Southeast side, directly south of Bldg. 5.\n*   **Bldg. 7 (4,144 sf):** South-central area, east of Bldg. 8.\n*   **Bldg. 8 (4,997 sf):** Southwest area, north of the southern entrance drive.\n*   **Spatial Relationship to Parking/Drives:** The buildings are arranged around a continuous looping internal drive. Driveways (\"Construct Type II Driveway\") enter from the west, forming a primary north-south lane that branches east between Bldgs 1/2 and 8, looping around the central buildings (Bldgs 3, 4, 7) to provide access to Bldgs 5 and 6 on the east. Standard perpendicular parking stalls and parallel spots are distributed along these internal drives.\n\n**3. Retaining Walls and Locations**\nExtensive retaining wall systems run along the perimeter of the property:\n*   **North Boundary:** A \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" runs east-west along the northern edge, turning south around the detention pond.\n*   **East Boundary:** The wall continues south along the eastern edge, with two segments labeled \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\" behind Buildings 5 and 6.\n*   **South Boundary:** The wall continues west along the southern boundary, labeled \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" at the southeast corner. Near the southwest driveway entrance, annotations state \"End Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n*   **Detention Pond Area:** An internal \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" loop bounds the detention pond in the northeast.\n\n**4. Visible Utility Easement Boundaries/Annotations**\n*   **Western Edge (Street Frontage):** Includes a \"Wastewater Easement Doc# [text unclear]\", \"Sidewalk Easement Doc# [text unclear]\", and a \"15' Exclusive Water and Wastewater Vault Easement\".\n*   **Northern Edge:** Contains a \"5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n*   **Eastern Edge:** Includes a \"25' Drainage Easement\", \"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\", and a \"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14\".\n*   **Southern Edge:** An annotation for \"10' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76\" is visible near the southeast corner.\n*   **General Utilities:** Underground lines are marked with \"- W -\" (Water), \"- WW -\" (Wastewater), and \"- SD -\" (Storm Drain) throughout the drives. Several \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" boxes are shown next to buildings.\n\n**5. Sidewalk/Pedestrian Areas and Separation**\n*   **Concrete Sidewalks:** A 5-foot pedestrian path labeled \"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ) See Dtl 432S-1\" loops through the site. It runs between the buildings, borders the \"Common Open Space\", and connects building fronts to the public ROW on the west.\n*   **Decomposed Granite Walkway:** A \"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\" is featured along the north, connecting Building 1 and Building 3 to the detention pond area.\n*   **Separation:** Sidewalks are largely separated from vehicular drives by small landscaped buffers, except where they cross the driveways at designated striped pedestrian crosswalks (e.g., east of Bldg. 4 and east of Bldg. 7).\n\n**6. Detention Pond Location and Extent**\n*   **Location:** Northeast corner of the site.\n*   **Details:** It is labeled \"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\".\n*   **Extent/Access:** It occupies a large rectangular area bound by concrete retaining walls. It features a \"15' Pond Maintenance Drive\" on its western edge, accessed via \"20' Pond Access Gates\" from the main drive.\n\n**7. Property Lines and Right-of-Way Areas**\n*   **Property Lines:** Marked by a thick, dark dashed-and-dotted line traversing the perimeter. Metes and bounds bearings are noted (e.g., \"N 89° 36' 57\" W 414.24'\" along the south).\n*   **Right-of-Way (ROW):** The western property line borders a public road (Valley View Road). Existing pavement and the ROW boundary are clearly defined. The area outside the western property boundary includes a \"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 432S-1\" paralleling the road, alongside an \"Existing Water Manhole\". Adjacent properties to the East and South are noted as \"Existing Apartment Building\" and \"Existing Stone Retaining Wall\".\n\n**8. Fences, Bollards, or Protective Barriers**\n*   **Fences:** A \"Pond Perimeter Fence\" fully encloses the detention pond in the northeast. A \"Wood Fence\" is annotated along the southern property line and portions of the eastern property line.\n*   **Bollards:** \"Bollard (Typ)\" is explicitly labeled in multiple key vehicular areas to protect structures or pedestrians, including:\n    *   Southeast corner of Building 4.\n    *   Northeast corner of Building 7.\n    *   Along the driveways near Buildings 5 and 6.\n*   **Retaining Walls as Barriers:** The aforementioned \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" functions as a substantial perimeter barrier on the North, East, and South sides.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1422,"outputTokens":1598,"totalTokens":6184,"reasoningTokens":3164},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the main Site Plan and identify:\n1. Fire hydrant locations on the site\n2. Building footprints and their spatial relationship to driveways and parking areas\n3. Retaining walls and their locations\n4. Any visible utility easement boundaries or annotations\n5. Sidewalk/pedestrian areas and their separation from buildings\n6. The location and extent of the detention pond\n7. Property lines and right-of-way areas\n8. Any fences, bollards, or protective barriers shown\nProvide compass directions and specific building references."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-nANZuTytfGdrc9DT6Q1gIGV9","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","conte