{"level":30,"time":1778188674417,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24VMC1G319EA8VMETARS1N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very important. The vision tool has confirmed that:\n- There are NO dimension lines showing clearance distances from transformer pads to buildings\n- There are NO callout notes for pad dimensions or clearances\n- There are NO detail reference symbols for pad specifications\n- There are NO callouts for bollards or protective barriers\n- There are NO notes about parking or fire lane distances\n\nThe pads are only labeled as \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" with no further specifications.\n\nThis is a significant deficiency. According to the grouping's regulatory overview and the code requirements, transformer pads must:\n- Have minimum 5-foot clearance from buildings (or 3 feet with written AE Design approval)\n- Have minimum 5-foot clearance from various site features\n- If within 4 feet of parking areas, require 4-inch bollards\n- Have specific dimensions matching AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets\n\nThe fact that there are NO dimensions, NO clearances marked, and NO detail references suggests that:\n1. The transformer pad dimensions are not specified on this plan\n2. The clearances to buildings and other features are not documented\n3. The plan does not reference Austin Energy Design-approved pad details\n4. No bollard details are provided\n\nThis could mean the plan is incomplete and doesn't show the required transformer pad specifications. However, I should check if there are detail sheets elsewhere in the plan set. Let me check the detail sheets (22-28) to see if there are transformer pad details there.\n\nLet me also check the site plan sheet (9) more carefully to see if transformer information is shown there, and check the utility plan sheets to see if there's any 