{"level":30,"time":1778188674446,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Analyze the electrical design plan and identify: (1) All utility pole locations shown on the sheet; (2) Underground electric lines (trenches, duct banks, pull boxes) - their routes and locations; (3) Transformer pads or pad-mounted equipment locations; (4) Any reference to overhead electric lines; (5) Conductor positions or cross-arm configurations. Note whether this shows underground service only or if overhead lines are also depicted.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here are the findings regarding the requested electrical infrastructure elements.\n\n**General Symbology Note:** Electrical infrastructure is predominantly denoted using solid blue lines and blue symbols with associated callout boxes containing specific text.\n\n### (1) Utility Pole Locations\nThere are no explicit utility pole locations labeled or clearly symbolized with specific callouts on this sheet. The origin point of the new electrical service on the left (west) side of the property connects near an existing line, but no specific pole symbol or label (e.g., \"Utility Pole\") is present at that connection point or elsewhere on the drawing.\n\n### (2) Underground Electric Lines (Routes and Locations)\nThe plan heavily details an underground electrical network serving the proposed buildings. The routing is indicated by solid blue lines that form a network along the internal driveways, branching off to individual buildings.\n\n**Routes:**\n*   The primary feed enters the site from the far left (west) edge, passing between \"Bldg. 1\" and \"Bldg. 8\".\n*   The line branches to create a circuitous route generally following the internal drive aisles, passing between the northern 