ng off to individual buildings.\n\n**Routes:**\n*   The primary feed enters the site from the far left (west) edge, passing between \"Bldg. 1\" and \"Bldg. 8\".\n*   The line branches to create a circuitous route generally following the internal drive aisles, passing between the northern buildings (Bldg. 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6) and southern buildings (Bldg. 8, 7).\n*   From the main blue routing lines, smaller branches extend directly to transformer pads and meter locations adjacent to the buildings.\n\n**Labeled Locations (Trenches, Pull Boxes, Lines):**\nThe following exact text labels in callout boxes pointing to the blue underground infrastructure are present:\n\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**\n    *   Callout pointing to the main incoming line on the far-left side of the drawing, near the property boundary.\n    *   Callout pointing to a segment of the blue line located centrally between \"Bldg. 4\" and \"Bldg. 6\".\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** (These point to small blue square symbols with an 'E' inside, located along the blue routing lines)\n    *   Located near the southwest corner of \"Bldg. 1\".\n    *   Located near the southwest corner of \"Bldg. 2\".\n    *   Located near the southwest corner of \"Bldg. 8\".\n    *   Located centrally between \"Bldg. 3\" and \"Bldg. 7\".\n    *   Located east of \"Bldg. 3\", near the property line.\n    *   Located east of \"Bldg. 7\" / west of \"Bldg. 6\".\n    *   Located southeast of \"Bldg. 7\", near the curving southern driveway.\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"** (These designate the termination points of the underground lines at the buildings)\n    *   Labeled multiple times pointing to grouped symbols attached to the exterior walls of Bldg. 1, Bldg. 2, Bldg. 3, Bldg. 4, Bldg. 6, Bldg. 7, and Bldg. 8.\n\n### (3) Transformer Pads or Pad-Mounted Equipment Locations\nThere are five distinct locations labeled as transformer pads. They are depicted as blue square/rectangular symbols attached to the underground electric lines. The exact text in the callout boxes for all five is: **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n\nTheir locations relative to the buildings are:\n1.  Located near the west side/northwest corner of \"Bldg. 1\".\n2.  Located near the west side of \"Bldg. 2\".\n3.  Located near the northwest corner of \"Bldg. 8\".\n4.  Located on the west side of \"Bldg. 6\" (east of Bldg. 4).\n5.  Located on the east side of \"Bldg. 7\".\n\n### (4) Reference to Overhead Electric Lines\nThere is a reference to overhead lines located outside the main property boundary on the far-left (west) side of the drawing, running parallel to the edge of the sheet.\n*   It is depicted as a dashed line running north-south.\n*   Embedded within this dashed line is the exact text: **\"OHE\"** (which standardly denotes Overhead Electric).\n\n### (5) Conductor Positions or Cross-Arm Configurations\nThere are no detail drawings, cross-sections, or text notes on this sheet that describe or show conductor positions or cross-arm configurations.\n\n***\n\n### Conclusion regarding Underground vs. Overhead\nThis sheet depicts **both** underground and overhead lines.\nHowever, there is a clear distinction: an existing overhead line (**\"OHE\"**) runs along the perimeter right-of-way (left side of the page), while the entirety of the newly designed distribution network serving the proposed development on the site itself is explicitly labeled and depicted as **\"Underground Electric Line\"** utilizing pad-mounted transformers and pull boxes."}]}
