{"level":30,"time":1778188676802,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the Site Plan drawing and determine: 1) Are the overhead electric lines and utility poles from the existing conditions (shown on Sheet 4) depicted on this proposed site plan? 2) What is the proximity of the proposed buildings (particularly Buildings 1-8) to any overhead electric lines? 3) Are there any clearance dimension annotations shown from overhead utilities to buildings, driveways, or other features? 4) Are there any notes regarding overhead electric line relocation, adjustments, or clearances? Please describe what you observe about the relationship between the proposed development and any overhead electric facilities that may still be present.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Site Plan (Sheet 9 of 39), here are the findings regarding the overhead electric lines and utility poles:\n\n**1) Depiction of overhead electric lines and utility poles:**\nYes, overhead electric lines and utility poles are depicted on this proposed site plan. \n*   A line type designated as **\"- OHE -\"** (Overhead Electric) is visible running along the outer perimeter of the site. Specifically, it runs horizontally along the southern (bottom) property boundary.\n*   Another segment of the **\"- OHE -\"** line is visible on the far left (western) side near the main driveway entrance, crossing near a label that reads \"Wastewater Service Connection.\"\n*   Utility poles are also depicted; for example, in the upper-left corner near the site entrance, there is a specific callout for an **\"AT&T Pole\"** with an associated \"Guy Wire\". Small circles indicative of utility poles appear intermittently along the \"- OHE -\" lines.\n\n**2) Proximity of the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) to overhead electric lines:**\nNone of the proposed Buildings (Bldg 1 through Bldg 8) are located directly underneath the depicted overhead electric lines. The \"- OHE -\" lines are routed exclusively along the perimeter/boundaries of the property. The buildings are grouped centrally within the site, maintaining a visual setback from the southern and western boundaries where these lines run. However, there are no specific dimensions provided on this sheet that quantify the exact distance (proximity) from the building footprints to the \"- OHE -\" lines.\n\n**3) Clearance dimension annotations:**\nThere are **no** clearance dimension annotations shown on this sheet denoting the distance or required clearance from the overhead utilities to any of the proposed buildings, driveways, or other site features. \n\n**4) Notes regarding overhead electric line relocation, adjustments, or clearances:**\nThere are **no** notes explicitly addressing the relocation, adjustment, or clearance requirements of existing overhead electric lines. \n*   A review of the \"Site Plan Release Notes\" yielded no instructions for the contractor regarding overhead line safety or relocation. Note 'd' states, *\"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date,\"* but it does not address the existing overhead infrastructure.\n*   There are notes calling out existing easements near the lines (e.g., *\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14, P.R.T.C.Tx.\"* near the bottom right), but no instructions on handling the physical lines themselves.\n\n**Summary of the Relationship:**\nBased solely on this sheet, the relationship between the proposed development and the overhead electric facilities appears to be one of avoidance by design; the proposed structures (Bldgs 1-8) and primary internal driveways are placed within the interior of the lot, while the overhead lines remain on the outer perimeter (south and west edges). However, because there are no clearance dimensions or utility adjustment notes provided on this page, it is impossible to verify from this sheet alone if the current proximity meets safety code clearances or if utility pole relocations will be necessary during construction.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1438,"outputTokens":661,"totalTokens":4453,"reasoningTokens":2354},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Site Plan drawing and determine: 1) Are the overhead electric lines and utility poles from the existing conditions (shown on Sheet 4) depicted on this proposed site plan? 2) What is the proximity of the proposed buildings (particularly Buil