{"level":30,"time":1778188683312,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Existing Conditions Survey: Are there any overhead electric lines, poles, or other overhead electric utility facilities shown on the existing conditions survey? Describe any utility infrastructure visible on the site or in adjacent areas.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Existing Conditions Survey\" site plan, here is the information regarding utility infrastructure:\n\n**Overhead Electric Facilities**\nYes, overhead electric lines and utility poles are clearly shown on the survey. \n*   **Overhead Lines:** Lines specifically labeled with the text **`OHE`** (breaking the line, e.g., `— OHE —`) are visible. \n    *   One primary `OHE` line runs along the entire left side of the property, adjacent to the right-of-way for **\"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\"**.\n    *   Another `OHE` line runs generally parallel to the bottom property boundary line.\n*   **Utility Poles:** The legend defines a circle with a dot/cross symbol as **\"U.P. UTILITY POLE\"**. Several of these symbols are present along the `OHE` lines:\n    *   One is located near the top-left curve of Valley View Road.\n    *   One is located roughly midway down the Valley View Road frontage.\n    *   One is located at the bottom-left corner of the property. A guy wire symbol (line with an arrowhead and cross) is shown extending from this pole.\n    *   Another utility pole is visible near the bottom-right property corner area.\n\n**Other Visible Utility Infrastructure**\nVarious other utility features and easements are documented on the site and adjacent areas:\n\n*   **Electric/Power:**\n    *   An **\"ELEC. BOX\"** is indicated by a small square near the bottom property boundary, roughly south of the main building slab.\n    *   Another **\"ELEC. BOX\"** is indicated near the right (eastern) property boundary.\n*   **Water:** A symbol specifically labeled **\"WATER METER\"** is located near the left property boundary, fronting Valley View Road.\n*   **Wastewater:** A circle symbol labeled **\"CLEAN-OUT\"** is located near the top-left (northwest) corner of the existing central **\"SLAB\"**.\n*   **Gas:** A rectangular symbol labeled **\"GAS METER\"** is located near the top (north) edge of the existing central **\"SLAB\"**. \n*   **HVAC:** An **\"A/C CONDENSER\"** is labeled adjacent to the top edge of the main building slab.\n*   **Utility Easements:** The plan delineates several public utility easements around the perimeter to accommodate infrastructure:\n    *   **\"5' P.U.E.\"** is noted running along the left property boundary (adjacent to Valley View Road).\n    *   **\"5' P.U.E.\"** is noted running along the right property boundary.\n    *   A **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT\"** is shown running parallel to a portion of the top property boundary.\n    *   A utility easement (partially obscured but appears to read **\"5' P.U.E.\"** based on surrounding text context like Vol/Pg references) runs along the bottom property boundary.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1350,"outputTokens":652,"totalTokens":5903,"reasoningTokens":3901},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Existing Conditions Survey: Are there any overhead electric lines, poles, or other overhead electric utility facilities shown on the existing conditions survey? Describe any utility infrastructure visible on the site or in adjacent areas."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-jFZwBAt0pV67MASXFEUKort5","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 07 May 2026 21:18:03 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"m