{"level":30,"time":1778188699864,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the landscape plan legend and key notes (Block 5). Identify:\n1. The legend symbols used for different tree types (EXISTING, SY, PL, P, M)\n2. Whether each symbol is associated with a specific species or if there's a separate legend showing which species corresponds to which symbol\n3. For the MITIGATION TREES (M symbols), identify if there's any indication of what species they are\n4. Look for any notes, schedule references, or symbols that indicate what species are planted in different zones\n5. Check if there are cross-references to other sheets (plant schedule) that identify the species\n\nProvide details on what you can discern about the identity and species of trees marked with \"M\" (mitigation).","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the details regarding the legend, key notes, and tree symbols, with a specific focus on the \"M\" (mitigation) trees:\n\n**1. Legend Symbols for Tree Types (EXISTING, SY, PL, P, M)**\nThe \"KEY NOTES\" section on the right side of the document contains a list of hexagonal callouts (H-1 through H-7) for various site elements (e.g., paving, fencing). Directly below this list, there is a text block that defines abbreviations for specific tree classifications used on the plan. \n\nThere are no distinct graphical symbols shown next to these abbreviations in the legend itself. Instead, the letters are used as labels next to or inside tree circles on the main plan drawing. \n\nThe text block exactly reads:\n*   `SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)`\n*   `PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)`\n*   `P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE`\n*   `M - MITIGATION TREE`\n\n*Note: There is no definition or legend entry for \"EXISTING\" trees in this specific key notes section.*\n\n**2. Association with Specific Species**\nThe abbreviations (SY, PL, P, M) do **not** associate with specific botanical species on this sheet. Instead, they classify the trees based on their regulatory or functional purpose within the development (e.g., fulfilling Street Yard requirements, Parking Lot shading, or Mitigation requirements). There is no separate species legend on this page.\n\n**3. Mitigation Trees (M symbols) Identification**\nThe only definition provided on this sheet for the \"M\" symbol is:\n`M - MITIGATION TREE`\n\nLooking at the main drawing, the \"M\" symbols appear as circles with a crosshair/plus sign inside them, accompanied by the letter \"M\". \n**There is absolutely no indication on this sheet of what specific biological species the \"M\" (Mitigation) trees are.** \n\n**4 & 5. Notes, Schedules, and Cross-References for Species**\n*   **Plant Schedule:** There is no Plant Schedule or Planting Legend present on this sheet. \n*   **Notes:** The \"IRRIGATION NOTES\" and general \"NOTE\" sections do not contain any information regarding plant species. \n*   **Cross-references:** There are no explicit text notes on this page (such as \"See Sheet XX for Plant Schedule\") directing the viewer to another sheet for species identification. \n\n**Summary regarding \"M\" (Mitigation) Trees:**\nFrom this sheet alone, you can discern that trees marked with \"M\" are legally or functionally classified as \"MITIGATION TREE[s]\" for the project. However, their specific species, size (caliper/gallon), and other botanical identifying details are completely absent from this page. Because this is Sheet 28 of 35, standard architectural and landscaping practices heavily imply that a detailed Plant Schedule containing this missing species information is located on a different sheet within the broader plan set.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1469,"outputTokens":674,"totalTokens":4086,"reasoningTokens":1943},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Focus on the landscape plan legend and key notes (Block 5). Identify:\n1. The legend symbols used for different tree types (EXISTING, SY, PL, P, M)\n2. Whether each symbol is associated with a specific species or if there's a separate legend showing which species corresponds to which symbol\n3. For the MITIGATION TREES (M symbols), identify if there's any indication of what species they are\n4. Look for any notes, schedule references, or symbols that indicate what species are planted in different zones\n5. Check if there are cross-references to other sheets (plant schedule) that identify the species\n\nProvide details on what you can discern about the identity and species of trees marked with \"M\" (mitigation)."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-PX7CfNmeYbSAATiGSEaz5tZ7","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 07 May 2026 21:18:19 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::d6x62-1778188670609-6d4c910c7df2"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the details regarding the legend, key notes, and tree symbols, with a specific focus on the \"M\" (mitigation) trees:\n\n**1. Legend Symbols for Tree Types (EXISTING, SY, PL, P, M)**\nThe \"KEY NOTES\" section on the right side of the document contains a list of hexagonal callouts (H-1 through H-7) for various site elements (e.g., paving, fe