{"level":30,"time":1778188716751,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine the Grading Plan drawing and look for: 1) Are overhead electric lines shown on this grading plan? 2) Are there any utilities or easements labeled? 3) Are there section views or cross-sections shown that depict clearances from driveways or other features to overhead utilities? 4) Are there elevation callouts or spot elevations that might be relevant to vertical clearances from overhead lines? 5) Are there any notes about overhead utilities, clearances, or relocation of existing poles? Please describe what overhead utility information is shown on this grading plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Grading Plan, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1) Are overhead electric lines shown on this grading plan?**\nNo overhead electric lines are explicitly drawn or labeled as such on this plan. There are no linetypes indicating overhead wires crossing the site or running along the right-of-way (Valley View Road).\n\n**2) Are there any utilities or easements labeled?**\nYes, several underground utilities and various easements are labeled on the plan. \n*Utilities shown include:*\n*   **Water/Wastewater:** Along Valley View Road, there are labels for \"8\" W.L.A.C.\", \"8\" W.L. (P)\", and \"8\" WW. (P)\". Near the top left, there is a callout for \"Existing 8\" W.L. Wastewater MH...\" and \"Existing Water Meter\".\n*   **Storm Drain:** Proposed storm drain lines are indicated by lines labeled \"SD\" running between buildings, connecting to inlets.\n\n*Easements shown include:*\n*   **Electric Easements:** \n    *   Bottom middle/right: \"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 66, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n    *   Bottom right edge: \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 885 D.R.T.C.T.s.\"\n    *   Right side (near Bldg 6): \"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n*   **Public Utility Easements (P.U.E.):**\n    *   Top middle: \"5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n    *   Top right: \"7.5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"\n*   **Drainage Easements:**\n    *   Top right: \"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n*   **Other Easements/Setbacks:**\n    *   Left side (near Bldg 2): \"25' Building Setback Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.T.s\"\n    *   Left side (top and bottom): \"Sidewalk Easement Doc#\" (document numbers are unclear).\n    *   Right side (near Bldg 5/6): \"Greenbelt Access & P.U.E. Easement Doc. 2010130721 O.R.P.T.C.T.\"\n\n**3) Are there section views or cross-sections shown that depict clearances from driveways or other features to overhead utilities?**\nNo. This document provides a top-down plan view only. There are no section cut lines, cross-sections, or profile views depicted on this sheet.\n\n**4) Are there elevation callouts or spot elevations that might be relevant to vertical clearances from overhead lines?**\nWhile the plan is covered in hundreds of proposed grading spot elevations (e.g., \"687.00\", \"684.39\"), Finished Floor Elevations (e.g., \"FFE = 687.50\"), and Top of Wall elevations (e.g., \"TW 681.00\"), none of these can be determined as relevant to vertical clearances from overhead lines on this sheet, because no overhead lines are depicted.\n\n**5) Are there any notes about overhead utilities, clearances, or relocation of existing poles?**\nNo. A review of all text blocks, including the Legend, Benchmarks, Curb Note, and the Texas 811 information box, reveals no specific notes regarding overhead utilities, vertical clearances, or the relocation of existing utility poles. There are no symbols for utility poles shown on the plan.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1424,"outputTokens":911,"totalToke