{"level":30,"time":1778188720810,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan and identify:\n1. All trees shown on the plan - mark their locations with compass directions relative to buildings\n2. Any vegetation or shrubs near transformer pad locations (note: transformers are shown on electrical plan Sheet 21 as: west side near Bldg 2, east central area, and other interior courtyard locations)\n3. Species identification or plant list reference - are trees labeled by type or species?\n4. Distance markings or dimensions showing tree setbacks from utilities or structures\n5. Root barrier details if shown\n6. Shrub or vegetation placement relative to buildings\n7. Mitigation trees or special planting requirements\nProvide specific locations using building references and compass directions.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35 for Valley View Townhomes), here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**1. All trees shown on the plan - mark their locations with compass directions relative to buildings**\nTrees are indicated by circular symbols (some with crosses or dots in the center) and are distributed across the site:\n*   **West Side (Street Frontage, West of westernmost buildings):** A prominent row of seven trees runs north-to-south along the western edge within the shaded street yard area.\n*   **North Side (North of northern building wings):** A row of approximately eight trees runs west-to-east along the northern property boundary.\n*   **East Side (East of eastern building wings):** Approximately four trees are clustered near the northeast corner (near the \"FILTRATION BASIN\"), and a row of roughly six trees runs along the eastern property line to the southeast corner.\n*   **South Side (South of southern building wings):** A row of approximately seven trees runs west-to-east along the southern property line.\n*   **Interior/Central (Between building wings):** One tree is located in a landscape island in the north-central parking/drive aisle. Another tree is located centrally, south of the main drive aisle.\n\n**2. Any vegetation or shrubs near transformer pad locations**\n*Note: Transformer pads are not explicitly drawn or labeled on this landscape sheet.* Based on the locations you provided from Sheet 21:\n*   **West side near Bldg 2 (Western edge):** This entire area is heavily landscaped. It falls within the shaded zone labeled \"H-3\" which the KEY NOTES define as \"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\". It also contains a row of large trees labeled \"SY/M\".\n*   **East central area:** The east central area immediately adjacent to the building primarily shows \"H-1\" (\"PROPOSED PAVING\") and narrow strips of \"H-7\" (\"SOD\"). No dense shrubbery or landscaping islands are denoted in the immediate east-central courtyard area.\n*   **Interior courtyard locations:** The spaces between the building \"fingers\" are generally marked with \"H-7\" (\"SOD\") and \"H-5\" (\"PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\"). There are no specific shrub hatchings or plantings indicated in these interior courtyards other than sod.\n\n**3. Species identification or plant list reference**\nTrees are **not** labeled by botanical species or type on this specific plan sheet, nor is there a plant schedule provided on this page. They are identified only by their categorical function as defined in the \"KEY NOTES\":\n*   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n**4. Distance markings or dimensions showing tree setbacks from utilities or structures**\nThere are **no** dimension lines or distance markings showing tree setbacks from buildings, utilities, or property lines visible on this sheet.\n\n**5. Root barrier details if shown**\nThere are **no** root barriers shown, labeled, or detailed anywhere on this plan sheet or in the provided notes.\n\n**6. Shrub or vegetation placement relative to buildings**\nVegetation placement is primarily indicated by hatching and key notes rather than individual shrub symbols:\n*   **West of Buildings:** The most significant vegetation is concentrated on the west side (street yard), indicated by the grey shaded area \"H-3\" (\"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\"). This zone buffers the entire western facade of the westernmost buildings.\n*   **Parking/Drive Aisles:** Landscaped islands within the central paved areas (north of the central buildings) are indicated by diagonal hatching labeled \"H-4\" (\"PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\").\n*   **Courtyards and Perimeters:** The immediate perimeters of the north, east, and south buildings, as well as the interior courtyards between building wings, are designated primarily as \"H-7\" (\"SOD\").\n*   **Basins:** A \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\" are located northeast of the buildings, showing hatched areas but no specific shrub notations.\n\n**7. Mitigation trees or special planting requirements**\nMitigation trees are heavily utilized and explicitly marked across the site:\n*   **West Side:** Three trees are labeled \"SY/M\" (Street Yard / Mitigation), and two are labeled \"M\" (Mitigation).\n*   **North Side:** Four trees along the north property line are labeled \"M\".\n*   **Interior:** One tree in the north-central parking island is labeled \"PL/M\" (Parking Lot / Mitigation).\n*   **South/Southeast Side:** At least four trees along the south/southeast property line are labeled \"M\".\n*   **Special Planting Requirements:** A \"NOTE\" at the top center of the page specifies a grading requirement for specific landscape areas: *\"FOR PARKING LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7]\"*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1452,"outputTokens":1160,"totalTokens":5286,"reasoningTokens":2674},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Landscape Plan and identify:\n1. All trees shown on the plan - mark their locations with compass directions relative to buildings\n2. Any vegetation or shrubs near transformer pad locations (note: transformers are shown on e