{"level":30,"time":1778188725625,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Examine this general notes sheet carefully and identify all notes, requirements, and specifications related to electric utilities, overhead electric lines, electric transmission lines, Austin Energy requirements, electric easements, and clearances from electric facilities. Look for any text mentioning \"electric,\" \"transmission,\" \"distribution,\" \"conductor,\" \"pole,\" \"Austin Energy,\" \"clearance,\" \"easement,\" or similar terms. Read the exact language of any electric-related notes, transmission facility requirements, clearance specifications, and Austin Energy coordination requirements.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a precise visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are all the notes, requirements, and specifications related to electric utilities, transmission lines, overhead lines, Austin Energy, easements, and clearances. \n\nThe information has been transcribed exactly as it appears on the sheet.\n\n### **Electric Notes**\nThis section appears in the first column, middle of the page:\n\n> \"1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n> \n> \"2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n> \n> \"3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n> \n> \"4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n> \n> \"5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n***\n\n### **Electric Transmission Notes**\nThis section appears in the top-middle portion of the page:\n\n> \"1. **No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement.** No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n> \n> \"2. **Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.** Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n> \n> \"3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512 505 7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (alt 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n> \n> \"4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\"\n> \n> \"5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n> \n> \"6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\"\n> \n> \"7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n> \n> \"8. 24 hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\"\n> \n> \"9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\"\n> \n> \"10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n> \n> \"11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be inverted curbing.\"\n> \n> \"12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\"\n> \n> \"13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n> \n> \"14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\"\n> \n> \"15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors).\"\n> \n> \"16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n>     - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n>     - any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, no;\n>     - any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n\n***\n\n### **Unnumbered Paragraphs Below Transmission Notes**\n*Note: Directly below the numbered \"Electric Transmission Notes\" section, the document contains five paragraphs of text. These paragraphs are exact duplicates of the five numbered items found in the \"Electric Notes\" section, repeated here as solid blocks of text without numbering.*\n\n> \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n> \n> \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n> \n> \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n> \n> \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n> \n> \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n***\n\n### **Electric Utility Mentions in Other Sections**\n\n**General Construction Notes:**\n> \"2. Contractor shall call Texas 811 (811 or 1-800-344-8377) for utility locations prior to any work in City easements or street R.O.W.\"\n> \n> \"6. Upon completion of the project and prior to the following, the engineer shall certify in writing that the proposed drainage, filtration and detention facilities were constructed in conformance with the approved plans:\n>     - Release of the Certificate of Occupancy by the Development Services Department (inside the City Limits);\n>       or\n>     - Installation of an electric or water meter (in the five mile ETJ).\"\n\n**Site Plan Release Notes:**\n> \"4. The owner is responsible for all costs of relocation of, or damage to, utilities.\"\n\n**Legend:**\nThe legend contains the following symbols and labels explicitly referencing electrical or utility items:\n*   `— PUE —` : **Public Utility Easement**\n*   *[Dashed rectangle symbol]* : **Electric Easement**\n*   *[Circle with an 'X' symbol]* : **Existing Power Pole & Down Guy**\n*   *[Square with an 'E' symbol]* : **Existing Electric Meter**\n*   `[ T ]` : **Existing Transformer Pad**\n*   `— OHE —` : **Existing Overhead Electric Line**\n*   `— OHE —` : **Overhead Electric Line**","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1413,"outputTokens":2031,"totalTokens":6821,"reasoningTokens":3377},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this general notes sheet carefully and identify all notes, requirements, and specifications related to electric utilities, overhead electric lines, electric transmission lines, Austin Energy requirements, electric easements, and clearances from electric facilities. Look for any text mentioning \"electric,\" \"transmission,\" \"distribution,\" \"conductor,\" \"pole,\" \"Austin Energy,\" \"clearance,\" \"easement,\" or similar terms. Read the exact language of any electric-related notes, transmission facility requirements, clearance specifications, and Austin Energy coordination requirements."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-o5c6hYrsO5m3Gv1AkaOEWAzA","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 07 May 2026 21:18:45 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::p7wp8-1778188682513-f3c