{"level":30,"time":1778188740265,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UYuHdficzqXGjGF4T9WMaY","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 7: text_block — Notice stating the applicant's responsibility for determining ADA compliance.\n     4→\n     5→Americans with Disabilities Act\n     6→The City of Austin has reviewed this plans for compliance with City development regulations only. The applicant, property owner, and occupant of the premises are responsible for determining whether the plan complies with all other laws, regulations , and restrictions which may be applicable to the property and its use.\n     7→\n     8→## Block 11: text_block — Legal description of the property for the site plan.\n     9→\n    10→Legal Description\n    11→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    12→\n    13→## Block 12: text_block — List of 10 site plan release notes outlining requirements and conditions for the approved site plan, including building codes, relocation costs, demolition permits, and utility service providers.\n    14→\n    15→Site Plan Release Notes\n    16→1. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require a site plan amendment and approval from the Development Services Department.\n    17→2. Approval of this site plan does not include Building Code and Fire Code approval; or building, demolition, or relocation permits approval. A City demolition or relocation permit can only be issued once the historic review process is completed.\n    18→3. All signs must comply with the requirements of the Land Development Code.(Chapter 25-10)\n    19→4. The owner is responsible for all costs of relocation of, or damage to, utilities.\n    20→5. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\n    21→6. A Site Development Permit must be issued prior to an application for building permit for non-consolidated or Land Use Commission approved site plans.\n    22→8. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\n    23→9. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n    24→10. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin).\n    25→\n    26→## Block 15: text_block — List of 7 requirements from the Austin Fire Department regarding pavement, hydrants, installation timing, paving standards, dumpster placement, fire lanes, and vertical clearances.\n    27→\n    28→Fire Department\n    29→1. The Austin Fire Department requires asphalt or concrete pavement prior to construction as an \"all-weather driving surface.\"\n    30→2. Hydrants must be installed with the center of the four-inch opening at least 18 inches above finished grade. The four-inch opening must face the driveway or street with three- to six-foot setbacks from the curbline(s). No obstruction is allowed within three feet of any hydrant and the four-inch opening must be totally unobstructed from the street.\n    31→3. TIMING OF INSTALLATION: When fire protection facilities are installed by the developer, such facilities shall include all surface access roads which shall be installed and made serviceable prior to and during the time of construction. Where alternative methods of protection, as approved by the Fire Chief, are provided, the above may be modified or waived.\n    32→4. All pervious/decorative paving shall be engineered and installed for 80,000 lb. live-vehicle loads. Any pervious/decorative paving within 100 feet of any building must be approved by the Fire Department.\n    33→5. Commercial dumpsters and containers with an individual capacity of 1.5 cubic yards or greater shall not be stored or placed within ten feet of openings, combustible walls, or combustible eave lines.\n    34→6. Fire lanes designated on site plan shall be registered with City of Austin Fire Marshal's office and inspected for final approval.\n    35→7. Vertical clearance required for fire apparatus is 14 feet for full width of access drive.\n    36→\n    37→## Block 18: text_block — Locations and elevations for two benchmarks used in the project.\n    38→\n    39→Benchmarks\n    40→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    41→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    42→\n    43→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    44→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    45→\n    46→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce5a084e-a0f7-4302-9557-5dc167da4ff6","uuid":"b8e5f5fe-b6f3-4005-b3f6-5c68825897d5","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 7: text_block — Notice stating the applicant's responsibility for determining ADA compliance.\n\nAmericans with Disabilities Act\nThe City of Austin has reviewed this plans for compliance with City development regulations only. The applicant, property owner, and occupant of the premises are responsible for determining whether the plan complies with all other laws, regulations , and restrictions which may be applicable to the property and its use.\n\n## Block 11: text_block — Legal description of the property for the site plan.\n\nLegal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 12: text_block — List of 10 site plan release notes outlining requirements and conditions for the approved site plan, including building codes, relocation costs, demolition permits, and utility service providers.\n\nSite Plan Release Notes\n1. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require a site plan amendment and approval from the Development Services Department.\n2. Approval of this site plan does not include Building Code and Fire Code approval; or building, demolition, or relocation permits approval. A City demolition or relocation permit can only be issued once the historic review process is completed.\n3. All signs must comply with the requirements of the Land Development Code.(Chapter 25-10)\n4. The owner is responsible for all costs of relocation of, or damage to, utilities.\n5. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\n6. A Site Development Permit must be issued prior to an application for building permit for non-consolidated or Land Use Commission approved site plans.\n8. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\n9. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n10. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin).\n\n## Block 15: text_block — List of 7 requirements from the Austin Fire Department regarding pavement, hydrants, installation timing, paving standards, dumpster placement, fire lanes, and vertical clearances.\n\nFire Department\n1. The Austin Fire Department requires asphalt or concrete pavement prior to construction as an \"all-weather driving surface.\"\n2. Hydrants must be installed with the center of the four-inch opening at least 18 inches above finished grade. The four-inch opening must face the driveway or street with three- to six-foot setbacks from the curbline(s). No obstruction is allowed within three feet of any hydrant and the four-inch opening must be totally unobstructed from the street.\n3. TIMING OF INSTALLATION: When fire protection facilities are installed by the developer, such facilities shall include all surface access roads which shall be installed and made serviceable prior to and during the time of construction. Where alternative methods of protection, as approved by the Fire Chief, are provided, the above may be modified or waived.\n4. All pervious/decorative paving shall be engineered and installed for 80,000 lb. live-vehicle loads. Any pervious/decorative paving within 100 feet of any building must be approved by the Fire Department.\n5. Commercial dumpsters and containers with an individual capacity of 1.5 cubic yards or greater shall not be stored or placed within ten feet of openings, combustible walls, or combustible eave lines.\n6. Fire lanes designated on site plan shall be registered with City of Austin Fire Marshal's office and inspected for final approval.\n7. Vertical clearance required for fire apparatus is 14 feet for full width of access drive.\n\n## Block 18: text_block — Locations and elevations for two benchmarks used in the project.\n\nBenchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778188740540,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24XBEN2QS1D21KHK56C64Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"EXCELLENT! Now I have the critical information from Sheet 3. The Electric Transmission Notes are very important and note that:\n\n1. No trees within transmission easement or within 25 feet of transmission structures\n2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of transmission structures\n3. Pre-construction safety meeting required with Austin Energy 48 hours before\n4. Barricades 10 feet from transmission structures during construction\n5. 20-foot clearance from energized transmission lines during construction (OSHA)\n6. Aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging NOT permitted within 20 feet of transmission wire\n7. Roads/driveways/parking should support 46,000 lb tandem axle if within easement\n8. Fire hydrants minimum 20 feet from transmission structure\n9. Sprinklers prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles\n10. Owner responsible for maintaining clearances required by NESC, OSHA, City of Austin, and Texas laws\n\nAnd the Electric Notes state:\n1. Austin Energy can prune/remove trees in easements\n2. Owner must provide easements for overhead and underground facilities\n3. Owner responsible for tree pruning/removal within 10 feet of centerline of proposed overhead electric facilities\n4. **Owner responsible for maintaining clearances per NESC, OSHA, City rules, and Texas law - Austin Energy will not render service unless clearances maintained**\n\nNow the critical question is: Are there transmission structures on this site or within the immediate adjacent area? The vision analysis of Sheet 9 suggested there is an overhead electric line along the southern boundary. I need to determine if this is a transmission line (≥60kV) or distribution line (<60kV).\n\nFrom the facts.md I read earlier, the easements mentioned were:\n- \"5' Electric Easements (×2)\" - documented as dedicated easements (Easement 7 & 8)\n- These are small widths (5 feet) which suggest distribution, not transmission\n\n\n- Sheet 9 also shows \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5168, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\" and \"3' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n\nThe narrow easement widths of 3-5 feet are characteristic of distribution lines rather than transmission lines, which typically require 25-50+ foot easements. I need to verify whether the overhead line visible on the southern boundary has any documented specifications that would clarify its voltage classification.\n\nI should also examine if any structures encroach on required clearance zones, and look for section or profile views that might illustrate vertical clearances between buildings and the line. Sheet 21 references a profile on Sheet 19, so I'll check there for any cross-sectional details showing how the line relates to the site's built features.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3251e5e3-3f03-4e85-9bab-d2e9039fdd51","uuid":"a8a952b7-739a-46b9-921a-de08ac864c93"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188740942,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine the site plan drawing (Sheet 9) and identify:\n1. Are there any transformer pads, electrical equipment, or electrical callouts shown on this site plan?\n2. If transformers are shown, what are their locations relative to buildings (north/south/east/west of which buildings)?\n3. Are there any dimension lines or notes showing clearances from transformer locations to buildings, parking areas, or other site features?\n4. Are there any detail reference callouts or symbols that reference electrical equipment details?\n5. What electrical or utility-related symbols, notes, or labels appear on this sheet?\n6. Are there any notes about compliance with Austin Energy Design requirements or electrical clearances?\n7. How close are any electrical facilities to parking areas, driveways, or building entrances?\n\nPlease be specific about spatial relationships and any text visible on the drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 9 of the Valley View Townhomes site plan, here are the findings regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Are there any transformer pads, electrical equipment, or electrical callouts shown on this site plan?**\nYes. There is a transformer pad and various electrical utility lines and easements explicitly labeled on this sheet.\n\n**2. If transformers are shown, what are their locations relative to buildings (north/south/east/west of which buildings)?**\nThere is one labeled transformer pad on this sheet.\n*   **Label:** \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"\n*   **Location:** It is located on the far mid-western edge of the site. It is situated **West** of the southern portion of **\"Bldg. 1\"** and **Northwest** of **\"Bldg. 8\"**. It sits directly adjacent to the main western property line and just west of the main entrance driveway.\n\n**3. Are there any dimension lines or notes showing clearances from transformer locations to buildings, parking areas, or other site features?**\nNo. There are no dimension lines indicating specific clearance radii or exact distances from the \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" to the buildings, parking stalls, or driveways. There is a dimension line showing \"26.1'\" nearby, but it denotes the distance from the face of Bldg. 1 to the back of the curb/sidewalk, not to the transformer pad.\n\n**4. Are there any detail reference callouts or symbols that reference electrical equipment details?**\nNo. There are no detail bubbles, section cuts, or reference callouts pointing to the \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" or the electrical lines to direct the reader to an electrical equipment detail on another sheet.\n\n**5. What electrical or utility-related symbols, notes, or labels appear on this sheet?**\nThe following utility-related labels and line types appear exactly as written below:\n*   **Electrical Specific:**\n    *   \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" (Located mid-west property line)\n    *   Line Type: **\"— OHE —\"** (Overhead Electric line running along the southern and eastern property boundaries)\n    *   Line Type: **\"— E —\"** (Underground electric line entering the site from the west near the transformer pad)\n    *   \"5' Electric Easement / Vol. 69, Pg. 14 / Vol. 73, Pg. 76 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located on the middle-right eastern property line)\n    *   \"5' Elec. & Tele Easement / Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 / D.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Located on the bottom-right southeastern corner)\n*   **Other Utility Labels:**\n    *   Line Types: **\"— W —\"** (Water), **\"— WW —\"** (Wastewater), **\"— SD —\"** (Storm Drain)\n    *   \"Wastewater Service Connection\" (Top left)\n    *   \"Existing Water Manhole\" (Top left)\n    *   \"Wastewater Easement Dock\" (Top left)\n    *   \"Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin...\" (Located in \"Site Plan Release Notes\", note 'e')\n    *   \"Wastewater Easement / Vol. 73, Pg. 76 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Top middle)\n    *   \"25' Drainage Easement / Vol. 73, Pg. 76 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Top right)\n    *   \"Water Meter\" (Top left, near the street)\n\n**6. Are there any notes about compliance with Austin Energy Design requirements or electrical clearances?**\nNo. A thorough review of all text blocks on the sheet—including \"Site Plan Release Notes,\" \"Accessibility Notes,\" \"Lighting Note,\" and general notes—reveals no mention of Austin Energy, Austin Energy Design requirements, or specific electrical clearance requirements. (The \"Lighting Note\" does mention compliance with \"Subchapter E 2.5\", but this pertains to shielded lighting, not electrical equipment clearances).\n\n**7. How close are any electrical facilities to parking areas, driveways, or building entrances?**\nBecause no specific dimensions are provided for these relationships, proximity can only be described visually based on the line work:\n*   **Transformer Pad:** Visually, it sits immediately adjacent to the western edge of the main entrance driveway (\"Construct Type III Driveway\"). It is separated from the parking spaces located east of the driveway by the width of the driveway itself. It is separated from building entrances for Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 8 by a retaining wall, a sidewalk, and a landscaped area.\n*   **Overhead Electric (— OHE —):** The overhead electric lines running along the southern property line pass visually extremely close to, or directly over, the rear edges of the parking stalls located south of Bldg. 8, Bldg. 7, and Bldg. 6.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1491,"outputTokens":1085,"totalTokens":4785,"reasoningTokens":2209},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Y