{"level":30,"time":1778188749226,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus specifically on the southern boundary of the property (bottom edge of the drawing):\n1. Trace the \"OHE\" (Overhead Electric) line - is it within the property boundary or outside (on/near Valley View Road)?\n2. Count and describe the specific tree symbols positioned along the southern boundary - are they within the LOC (Limit of Construction)?\n3. Measure visually: what is the approximate distance between tree symbols and the OHE line?\n4. Are there any tree symbols that appear to be directly under or within a few feet of the OHE line?\n5. Is the OHE line shown on Sheet 31 marked with poles or other infrastructure that would help determine its exact location?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided document, which is labeled as **Sheet 28 of 35 (LANDSCAPE PLAN)**, here are the precise observations regarding the southern boundary:\n\n**1. Trace the \"OHE\" (Overhead Electric) line - is it within the property boundary or outside?**\nThe line denoted with \"---OHE---\" runs horizontally along the southern portion of the site. It is located **within** (north of) the heavy line marked with \"x\" symbols labeled \"LOC\" (Limit of Construction) that runs along the very bottom edge of the drawing. Note that \"Valley View Road\" is labeled on the western (left) edge of the plan, not the southern boundary. Therefore, the OHE line appears to be inside the construction limits/property boundary, not on Valley View Road.\n\n**2. Count and describe the specific tree symbols positioned along the southern boundary - are they within the LOC?**\nThere are approximately **5 distinct tree symbols** (circular shapes representing tree canopies with a center mark) positioned along the immediate path of the OHE line on the so