{"level":30,"time":1778188757087,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan drawing and determine: 1) Are overhead electric lines shown on this landscape plan? If yes, where are they located? 2) Are there trees or shrubs planted that are within 10 lateral feet of the overhead electric lines? 3) Are the species of trees within these clearance zones identified and verified as \"Utility Compatible\" from ECM Appendix F (typically mature height ≤20 feet)? 4) Are there any clearance annotations or notes indicating distances from trees to overhead utilities? 5) What landscape features are shown in the vicinity of the overhead electric lines (utilities shown as running along the perimeter)? Please provide specific observations about tree placement relative to any overhead electric facilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan document, here are the determinations regarding your questions:\n\n**1) Are overhead electric lines shown on this landscape plan? If yes, where are they located?**\nYes, overhead electric lines are shown on this plan. They are identified by a line labeled \"**OHE**\" running horizontally along the bottom (southern) edge of the site plan, just outside the Limit of Construction (\"LOC\") line.\n\n**2) Are there trees or shrubs planted that are within 10 lateral feet of the overhead electric lines?**\nYes. Based on the provided scale (1\" = 20'-0\"), there are multiple trees planted along the bottom boundary that appear to be within 10 lateral feet of the \"**OHE**\" line. The center points of the tree symbols (indicating trunk placement) are drawn very close to this line, and their graphical canopies overlap it.\n\n**3) Are the species of trees within these clearance zones identified and verified as \"Utility Compatible\" from ECM Appendix F (typically mature height ≤20 feet)?**\nNo, the species cannot be identified or verified from this document alone. There is no Plant Schedule or list of botanical names on this specific page. The trees are only identified by tags relating to their code function (e.g., \"**M**\" for \"MITIGATION TREE\", \"**SY**\" for \"STREET YARD TREE\"), as defined in the legend under \"KEY NOTES:\". Because the species are unknown, their mature height and utility compatibility cannot be verified here.\n\n**4) Are there any clearance annotations or notes indicating distances from trees to overhead utilities?**\nNo. There are no dimension lines, callouts, or specific notes on this drawing indicating required clearance distances between the planted trees and the overhead electric lines.\n\n**5) What landscape features are shown in the vicinity of the overhead electric lines (utilities shown as running along the perimeter)? Please provide specific observations about tree placement relative to any overhead electric facilities.**\n*   **Landscape Features:** The area immediately adjacent to the \"**OHE**\" line features newly planted trees (some labeled \"**M**\"), a Limit of Construction boundary (\"**LOC**\"), and areas designated for sod (indicated by Key Note bubble \"**H.7**\" pointing to the ground area). There is also a line type indicating a fence running parallel in the vicinity.\n*   **Tree Placement Observations:** The trees along the bottom boundary are planted in a linear arrangement in a narrow landscape strip between the paved site area/storm drain (\"**SD**\") and the property edge. They are placed directly adjacent to the overhead utility corridor, to the extent that the circular symbols representing the mature or drawn tree canopies physically intersect and overlap the \"**OHE**\" line on the plan.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1454,"outputTokens":585,"totalTokens":4239,"reason