{"level":30,"time":1778188762541,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan and identify:\n1. Whether there are any overhead electric utilities or lines shown on this sheet\n2. If overhead lines are shown, identify their location, voltage classification (if labeled), and type (distribution vs. transmission)\n3. The locations of transformers, pad-mounted equipment, pull boxes, and underground electric lines\n4. Any notes or callouts that indicate pole locations or conductor positions\n5. Any reference to the landscape plan or tree placement relative to electrical infrastructure\n6. Whether the electrical infrastructure shown is primarily underground or overhead\n\nProvide specific locations and details on the extent and type of electrical infrastructure.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here are the details regarding the electrical infrastructure:\n\n**1. Presence of Overhead Electric Utilities**\nYes, overhead electric utilities are shown on this sheet.\n\n**2. Overhead Line Location, Voltage, and Type**\n*   **Location:** Overhead lines, denoted by the line type \"- OHE -\", run along the western property boundary parallel to \"Valley View Road\". Another \"- OHE -\" line runs along the southern property boundary.\n*   **Voltage Classification & Type:** There are no explicit labels indicating the specific voltage classification (e.g., 12kV, 34.5kV) or type (distribution vs. transmission) for these overhead lines. They are simply labeled \"- OHE -\". \n\n**3. Locations of Transformers, Pad-Mounted Equipment, Pull Boxes, and Underground Lines**\n*   **Underground Electric Lines:** Shown as a network of dashed blue lines routing throughout the interior of the site. A leader line on the western side of the property explicitly points to this blue dashed line with the label \"**Underground Electric Line**\", showing it transitioning from the overhead line on Valley View Road into the site.\n*   **Electrical Transformer Pads:** Three main pad-mounted transformer locations are labeled \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\":\n    1.  Near the western entrance, adjacent to Bldg. 2 (Unit 201) and Bldg. 8 (Unit 801).\n    2.  In the eastern-central portion of the site, between Bldg. 6 (Unit 602) and Bldg. 4 (Unit 404/704 area).\n    3.  A third is located just north of Bldg 2 (Unit 201) / near the upper site entrance.\n*   **Electrical Pull Boxes:** Several boxes labeled \"**Electrical Pull Box**\" are placed along the underground routes. Locations include:\n    1.  Near Bldg. 1 (Unit 102)\n    2.  Near Bldg. 8 (Unit 801)\n    3.  Near Bldg. 4 (Unit 404)\n    4.  Near the eastern boundary by Unit 603\n    5.  Along the southern routing near the center-south property line.\n*   **Electrical Meters:** Banks of \"**Electrical Meters**\" are noted at the sides or rears of the buildings (e.g., between Bldg. 1 and 3, near Bldg. 2, Bldg. 4, Bldg. 6, and Bldg. 8).\n\n**4. Notes or Callouts for Pole Locations/Conductor Positions**\nThere are no specific textual callouts or notes labeling \"poles,\" \"guy wires,\" or specific conductor heights/positions. The \"- OHE -\" lines show the path of the overhead conductors, and while there are circular symbols along these lines that typically represent utility poles, they lack explicit text labels identifying them as such.\n\n**5. Reference to Landscape Plan or Tree Placement**\nAt the bottom center of the sheet, there is a \"**Tree List**\" box containing the text: \"**Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.**\" There are no notes on this specific sheet dictating clearance requirements or tree placement relative to the electrical infrastructure.\n\n**6. Primary Electrical Infrastructure (Underground vs. Overhead)**\nThe proposed on-site electrical infrastructure servicing the townhome units is primarily **underground**. While existing overhead lines (\"- OHE -\") border the west and south perimeters, the entirety of the internal distribution network connecting to the buildings consists of underground electric lines, pad-mounted transformers, and at-grade pull boxes.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1444,"outputTokens":780,"totalTokens":4182,"reasoningTokens":1958},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan and identify:\n1. Whether there are any o