es or Callouts for Pole Locations/Conductor Positions**\nThere are no specific textual callouts or notes labeling \"poles,\" \"guy wires,\" or specific conductor heights/positions. The \"- OHE -\" lines show the path of the overhead conductors, and while there are circular symbols along these lines that typically represent utility poles, they lack explicit text labels identifying them as such.\n\n**5. Reference to Landscape Plan or Tree Placement**\nAt the bottom center of the sheet, there is a \"**Tree List**\" box containing the text: \"**Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.**\" There are no notes on this specific sheet dictating clearance requirements or tree placement relative to the electrical infrastructure.\n\n**6. Primary Electrical Infrastructure (Underground vs. Overhead)**\nThe proposed on-site electrical infrastructure servicing the townhome units is primarily **underground**. While existing overhead lines (\"- OHE -\") border the west and south perimeters, the entirety of the internal distribution network connecting to the buildings consists of underground electric lines, pad-mounted transformers, and at-grade pull boxes."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778188762995,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24XTD9V96C9VDWFA4KHA8S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me now create a comprehensive summary of my research findings before evaluating the checklist items.\n\nFrom my research:\n\n1. **Grouping Overview**: EL-13 covers transformer pad clearances and location requirements under UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 and related sections. This is a comprehensive grouping covering 39 checklist items.\n\n2. **Project Information**:\n   - Valley View Townhomes - 39 townhome units across 8 buildings\n   - MF-2 Zoning (Multi-Family Medium Density)\n   - Site area: 2.16 acres\n   - No overhead distribution lines shown in the immediate vicinity of transformer pads\n   - Electrical infrastructure shown on Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan)\n\n3. **Transformer Pads Found**:\n   - Sheet 21 shows 4 transformer pads (labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\")\n   - Sheet 9 shows \"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\" label but only 1 pad is clearly called out\n   - The vision analysis indicated 4 pads on Sheet 21:\n     * Pad 1: Northwest near Building 1\n     * Pad 2: West-central, west of Building 2\n     * Pad 3: East-central, near Buildings 4 and 5\n     * Pad 4: South-central, east of Building 7\n\n4. **KEY FINDING - CRITICAL DEFICIENCY**: \n   - NO SPECIFIC DIMENSIONS OR CLEARANCES ARE SHOWN ON THE ELECTRICAL PLAN (Sheet 21)\n   - NO DETAIL REFERENCES FOR TRANSFORMER PAD SPECIFICATIONS\n   - NO CALLOUTS FOR PAD DIMENSIONS OR PROTECTION DETAILS\n   - NO DIMENSION LINES SHOWING CLEARANCES TO BUILDINGS\n   - The vision analysis explicitly stated: \"This specific sheet ('Preliminary Electrical Design Plan') appears to only show the schematic locations of the transformer pads and routing of the electrical lines. \n\nThe plan lacks the specific dimensional clearances, detail references, and protective barrier specifications required by code. No detail sheets containing transformer pad specifications were found—Sheets 22-23 only cover water, fire hydrant, and pavement details. The supplementary documents (Engineer's Summary Letter, Master Comment Report) also don't include transformer pad specifications, and the Electric Review section in the Master Comment Report only provides a Bluebeam link for comments that I cannot access.\n\n5. **No Evidence of Applicability Exclusions**:\n   - There ARE transformer pads on the site plan\n   - The site IS applicable to Austin Energy design requirements per the Master Comment Report\n\n6. **Critical Missing Elements**:\n   - Transformer pad dimensions (length x width) are not documented\n   - Clearances from pads to buildings, parking areas, and retaining walls are not shown\n   - Detail references to AE Design-approved transformer pad details are absent\n   - No bollard or protective barrier specifications provided\n   - Transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) not specified\n   - No documentation of any approved reduced clearances (such as the 3-foot to buildings exception)\n   - Fire rating documentation for walls adjacent to transformer pads is missing\n   - Grading and drainage direction relative to pads not indicated\n   - Transformer easements and pad locations not confirmed on the plans\n   - Electrical routing details absent from site plan\n\n**Analysis of Applicability**:\n\nSince transformer pads are shown on these plans for a residential multi-family project, the clearance requirements under UCM § 1.10.4 apply. Most of the 39 checklist items warrant evaluation.\n\n**Key Determination - FAIL vs NOT-VERIFIABLE**:\n\nThe critical distinction: a FAIL occurs when inadequate clearance exists or required information is missing from the plans, while NOT-VERIFIABLE means the requirement cannot be assessed from available evidence. Here, the applicant must demonstrate compliance through dimensioned drawings and specifications. When this information is absent from the plans, the items cannot be verified.\n\nLooking at specific items: EL-13.1 shows transformer pads without clearance dimensions to buildings—the required measurements aren't provided. EL-13.10 lacks identification of the access door side and any clearance dimensions. EL-13.37 doesn't reference whether the transformer pad dimensions match Austin Energy Design-approved detail sheets.\n\nFor EL-13.38, there's no indication of bollards or protective barriers around equipment pads near parking areas. EL-13.4 is difficult to assess since no clearance dimensions appear on the plans at all, making it impossible to determine if reduced clearances were intended or if standard 5-foot clearances apply.\n\nMy evaluation strategy is to categorize each item by what's actually verifiable: dimensional requirements need visible measurements on the plans, specification items require detail sheet references, physical features like bollards must be shown, conditional requirements depend on whether I can confirm the triggering condition exists, and universal requirements apply regardless. I'll work through all 39 checklist items using these criteria to determine which are clear failures, which cannot be verified from available documentation, and which pass.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f2fc17a-22f3-4791-8627-5877b81951c5","uuid":"1f55c239-d7db-4c1c-8ca5-2c0447d6096e"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188763027,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24XTD9V96C9VDWFA4KHA8S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me now check the fire protection plan to see if any fire escape or fire lane distances are shown relative to transformer locations."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f2fc17a-22f3-4791-8627-5877b81951c5","uuid":"5d4e84ed-4acf-4c61-beee-1a57a289e668"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188764682,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Provide detailed measurements and distances. Focus on the three Mitigation Trees (M) in the southeast corner of the site and their distances from the overhead electric line (OHE) running along the southern boundary. Estimate the lateral distance from each tree trunk to the OHE line based on the grid scale (1\"=20'). Also identify any trees along the western boundary and estimate their distances to any overhead lines shown there. Include any utility poles or infrastructure shown. Be as specific as possible with distance estimates based on the scale provided.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the detailed observations and measurements regarding the trees, overhead electric (OHE) lines, and infrastructure.\n\n**Reference Scale**\nAll distance estimates are based on the graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner of the document, where the first major segment represents 20 feet (1\" = 20'-0\").\n\n### 1. Southeast Corner Mitigation Trees (M) and Southern OHE Line\nAn overhead electric line, labeled \"**OHE**\", runs parallel to the southern boundary property line. In the southeast corner of the site, there is a cluster of three trees designated with the symbol for a Mitigation Tree (a circle with a crosshair inside) and labeled \"**M**\". \n\nMeasuring laterally from the center of each tree trunk (the center crosshair of the symbol) south to the OHE line:\n*   **Easternmost Mitigation Tree (M):** The trunk is located approximately **8 to 10 feet** north of the OHE line. The southern edge of its drawn canopy extends over the OHE line.\n*   **Middle Mitigation Tree (M):** The trunk is located approximately **12 to 15 feet** north of the OHE line.\n*   **Westernmost Mitigation Tree (M) (of this SE group):** The trunk is located approximately **18 to 20 feet** north of the OHE line.\n\n### 2. Western Boundary Trees and Western OHE Line\nAnother overhead electric line, also labeled \"**OHE**\", runs vertically along the entire western boundary of the site. Several trees are planted along this boundary.\n\n*   **Southwest Corner Tree:** There is one Mitigation Tree (\"**M**\") located in the extreme southwest corner. Its trunk is positioned very close to the western OHE line, estimated at approximately **3 to 5 feet** east of the line. The OHE line passes directly through its indicated canopy.\n*   **Western Buffer Area Trees:** Moving north along the western boundary, there is a shaded buffer/street yard area (marked with H-1/H-3 notes). This area contains a row of five primary trees. While the labels are overlapping (appearing to be combinations of \"**SY**\" for Street Yard Tree and \"**M**\" for Mitigation Tree), their distances from the western OHE line can be estimated:\n    *   The southernmost tree in this shaded row is approximately **15 feet** east of the OHE line.\n    *   The remaining four trees continuing north to the northwest corner are set further back, with their trunks located roughly **20 to 25 feet** east of the western OHE line.\n\n### 3. Utility Poles and Other Infrastructure\nSeveral utility poles and infrastructure elements are identifiable on the plan:\n\n*   **Utility Poles (OHE Line):** Small circular symbols indicating utility poles are present along the OHE lines.\n    *   One pole is located at the intersection of the southern and western OHE lines in the southwest corner.\n    *   One pole is located on the southern OHE line, roughly halfway along the southern boundary (directly south of the westernmost edge of the building structure).\n    *   One pole is located on the southern OHE line near the southeast corner, just left of the easternmost \"OHE\" text label.\n    *   One pole is visible on the western OHE line, roughly midway up the western property line.\n*   **Drainage/Water Infrastructure:** \n    *   A \"**SEDIMENTATION BASIN**\" and a \"**FILTRATION BASIN**\" are explicitly labeled in the northeast quadrant of the site.\n    *   Storm drain lines, marked with \"**SD**\", run horizontally through the center of the site (driveway/parking area) from west to east.\n*   **Fencing:** A wooden privacy fence, denoted by a line with alternating 'x' marks and labeled \"**H-6**\" in the Key Notes, runs along the eastern boundary.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1416,"outputTokens":858,"totalTokens":6844,"reasoningTokens":4570},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Provide detailed measurements and distances. Focus on the three Mitigation Trees (M) in the southeast corner of the site and their distances from the overhead electric line (OHE) running along the southern boundary. Estimate the lateral distance from each tree trunk to the OHE line based on the grid scale (1\"=20'). Also identify any trees along the western boundary and estimate their distances to any overhead lines shown there. Include any utility poles or infrastructure shown. Be as specific as possible with distance estimates based on the scale provided."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-Qa2QtO6pb76JYWcP56VIx5TJ","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 07 May 2026 21:19:24 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::pv5dr-1778188708438-0a26f503ebe7"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ba