{"level":30,"time":1778188773190,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":32,"prompt":"Examine the Tree List table and identify:\n1. All tree species proposed on the site with their common names\n2. The caliper sizes and quantity of each species\n3. Whether each species is marked as utility-compatible (should reference ECM Appendix F \"UC\" column notation)\n4. Any heritage trees (24\" and up caliper)\n5. Tree tag numbers and their proposed/removed status\n6. Total quantities of each species\n7. Any notation about utility compatibility or restriction\nFocus on identifying which proposed species have \"UC\" designation for utility compatibility, as required by UCM § 1.10.10.4.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided document, here is the detailed analysis addressing your specific requests. \n\n**CRITICAL OBSERVATION:** The document provided is titled **\"SURVEYED TREES\"** and represents an inventory of *existing* trees on the site. It is **not** a proposed tree planting list. Therefore, it evaluates existing trees for \"Remain\" or \"Remove\" status rather than listing newly proposed plantings. \n\nBelow is the exact data extracted from the table as it appears:\n\n### 1, 2, & 6. Tree Species, Caliper Sizes, and Total Quantities\nThe following summarizes all surveyed tree species on the site, their total quantities, and the specific caliper sizes (in inches) recorded for each:\n\n*   **Live Oak (Total: 17 trees)**\n    *   Sizes: 12\", 14\", 14\", 15\", 15\", 16\", 18\", 18\", 19\", 20\", 20\", 20.5\", 24\", 27\", 32\", 36\", 42\"\n*   **China Berry (Total: 8 trees, 1 multi-trunk)** *Note: Listed as Invasive*\n    *   Sizes: 9 & 14\" (multi-trunk), 10\", 12\", 12\", 15\", 20\", 24\", 30\"\n*   **Hackberry (Total: 8 trees)**\n    *   Sizes: 8\", 9\", 10\", 11\", 13\", 14\", 16\", 18\"\n*   **Arizona Ash (Total: 4 trees)**\n    *   Sizes: 11\", 11\", 13\", 15\"\n*   **Cedar Elm (Total: 3 trees)**\n    *   Sizes: 14\", 17\", 19.5\"\n*   **Pecan (Total: 2 trees)**\n    *   Sizes: 10\", 24\"\n*   **Poplar (Total: 2 trees)**\n    *   Sizes: 9\", 11\"\n*   **American Elm (Total: 1 tree)**\n    *   Size: 27\"\n*   **Bradford Pear (Total: 1 tree)**\n    *   Size: 14\"\n*   **Pine (Total: 1 tree)**\n    *   Size: 16\"\n*   **Unknown (Total: 1 tree)**\n    *   Size: 13\"\n\n### 3 & 7. Utility-Compatible Designation (ECM Appendix F \"UC\" Notation)\n*   **Notation Found:** None. \n*   **Analysis:** Because this is an existing tree survey and not a proposed planting schedule, there is **no \"UC\" (Utility Compatible) designation** anywhere on this document. The table includes a column labeled exacty as `\"APPENDIX F (Y/N) OR INVASIVE (I)\"`, which categorizes existing trees (using 'Y', 'N', or 'I'), but it does not specify which, if any, are utility-compatible for planting purposes under UCM § 1.10.10.4.\n\n### 4. Heritage Trees (24\" and up caliper)\nThe following trees are explicitly marked `\"Yes\"` in the `\"HERITAGE TREE\"` column (all are 24\" & up):\n*   **Tree No. 4015:** 24\" Pecan (Remain)\n*   **Tree No. 4018:** 32\" Live Oak (Remain)\n*   **Tree No. 4019:** 42\" Live Oak (Remain)\n*   **Tree No. 4022:** 27\" American Elm (Remove)\n*   **Tree No. 4026:** 36\" Live Oak (Remain)\n*   **Tree No. 4027:** 27\" Live Oak (Remain)\n*   **Tree No. 4038:** 24\" Live Oak (Remain)\n*(Note: Tree No. 4014 (30\" China Berry) and 4035 (24\" China Berry) meet the size threshold but are marked \"No\" for Heritage, likely because China Berry is noted as an invasive species).*\n\n### 5. Tree Tag Numbers and Proposed/Removed Status\nHere is the exact character-by-character transcription of the tree numbers, species, sizes, and their proposed status from the table:\n\n| TREE NO. | TREE INCHES | TREE SPECIES | STATUS |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 143 | 12 | Live Oak | Remain |\n| 144 | 14 | L