{"level":30,"time":1778188793790,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24Z7CJZ7JCB0W56KD32AN7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The measurement tool failed because it couldn't find the plan_set_version. This is a technical issue with the tool itself. However, based on my vision analysis of the site plans, I have enough information to make a determination on the clearances.\n\nLet me assess the evidence I've gathered:\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY - FINDINGS:**\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Present:**\n- OHE line runs horizontally (east-west) along southern property boundary\n- At least 3 utility poles visible: SW corner, midway, SE corner\n- Guy wire extends from SE corner pole\n- Easements are 5-feet wide (indicating distribution lines, not transmission)\n- Conductors are described as \"OHE\" (Overhead Electric)\n\n**Evidence of Missing Clearance Verification:**\n\nFrom all sheets reviewed:\n1. Sheet 9 (Site Plan): Shows OHE line and buildings but NO clearance dimensions\n2. Sheet 11 (Grading Plan): Shows electrical easements but NO clearance dimensions\n3. Sheet 21 (Electrical Design): Shows underground electrical infrastructure, NOT overhead coordination\n4. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan): Shows OHE line but NO clearance dimensions\n5. Sheet 3 (General Notes): Requires owner to maintain clearances per NESC/OSHA but provides no verification\n\n**Building Proximity to OHE:**\n- Buildings 7 and 8 are closest to the southern OHE line based on site plan layout\n- From the vision analysis: \"Building 7 and Building 8 are the closest structures to this southern OHE line\"\n- No horizontal or vertical clearance annotations shown for these buildings\n\n**Missing Required Documentation:**\n- NO surveyed elevations of overhead conductors\n- NO section views showing clearances\n- NO registered surveyor mid-span clearance data\n- NO clearance dimension lines shown from conductor to buildings\n- NO 48-hour notification note visible on general notes\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item systematically.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3251e5e3-3f03-4e85-9bab-d2e9039fdd51","uuid":"2403a28b-b7a5-492f-9649-74b6c9c1d6cb"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188796849,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Examine the general notes on this sheet. Are there any notes regarding:\n1. Electric transmission line clearances or safety requirements?\n2. Austin Energy easement requirements or overhead electric facility requirements?\n3. 48-hour notification requirements for work near electric lines?\n4. Tree pruning or maintenance near overhead lines?\n5. Construction staging areas near overhead electric facilities?\nPlease provide the exact text of any such notes found.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful examination of the provided site plan document, there are several notes addressing your specific questions. Below are the exact quotes found in the **Electric Notes** and **Electric Transmission Notes** sections (Note: The text from the *Electric Notes* section is also duplicated in an unnumbered block of text directly below the *Fire Department* section).\n\n**1. Electric transmission line clearances or safety requirements?**\nYes, there are multiple notes regarding clearances and safety:\n\nFrom the **Electric Transmission Notes** section:\n*   \"2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n*   \"3. ...OSHA requires a 20’ clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n*   \"4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\"\n*   \"6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\"\n*   \"15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors).\"\n*   \"16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    *   any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n    *   any structure of any kind in such proximity to transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected...\"\n\nFrom the **Electric Notes** section:\n*   \"4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n\n**2. Austin Energy easement requirements or overhead electric facility requirements?**\nYes, these requirements are detailed extensively:\n\nFrom the **Electric Notes** section:\n*   \"2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   \"5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner’s/developer’s expense.\"\n\nFrom the **Electric Transmission Notes** section:\n*   \"5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n*   \"8. 24 hour access to electric facilities must be maintained.\"\n*   \"9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\"\n*   \"11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structure/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be mountable curbing.\"\n*   \"12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\"\n*   \"13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n\n**3. 48-hour notification requirements for work near electric lines?**\nYes, there is a requirement for a pre-construction meeting 48 hours in advance:\n\nFrom the **Electric Transmission Notes** section:\n*   \"3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (alt 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20’ clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n\n**4. Tree pruning or maintenance near overhead lines?**\nYes, tree pruning, planting, and maintenance are addressed:\n\nFrom the **Electric Notes** section:\n*   \"1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n*   \"3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy’s work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n\nFrom the **Electric Transmission Notes** section:\n*   \"1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n\n**5. Construction staging areas near overhead electric facilities?**\nYes, there is a specific restriction regarding staging areas:\n\nFrom the **Electric Transmission Notes** section:\n*   \"7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1400,"outputTokens":1331,"totalTokens":7077,"reasoningTokens":4346},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the general notes on this sheet. Are there any notes regarding:\n1. Electric transmission line clearances or safety requirements?\n2. Austin Energy easement requirements or overhead electric facility requirements?\n3. 48-hour notification requirements for work near electric lines?\n4. Tree pruning or maintenance near overhead lines?\n5. Construction staging areas near overhead electric facilities?\nPlease provide the exact text of any such notes found."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-Qdy80CrCtCHiOgX9pEM6i1gf","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT,