{"level":30,"time":1778188812071,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24YXN6DYSHKV7B2SZZYG52","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TpC5Mf8wyXAkRwFubKb1SA","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan southern boundary trees near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Sheet 35 - Landscape Calculations"}],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees marked with 'M' symbols along the southern boundary near overhead electric utilities, but the plant schedule (Sheet 35) does not specify which proposed tree species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, or Mexican Redbud) are located at these positions. The plant legend defines 'M' as 'MITIGATION TREE' without species identification. Provide species identification for all trees shown on the landscape plan, particularly those in proximity to overhead and underground utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows 'M' labeled trees near OHE line; Sheet 35 lists proposed species but does not correlate them to landscape plan symbols or locations.","reasoning":"Per UCM and City of Austin standards, plant schedules must identify species for all trees proposed near utilities to enable verification of utility compatibility and clearance compliance. The present plan fails to make this correlation, preventing verification that the species selected meet clearance requirements.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary trees; western boundary along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While trees and overhead electric (OHE) lines are both shown on the landscape plan, no dimensions, callouts, or measurements relate tree locations to the OHE infrastructure. The OHE line path is indicated but conductor position, pole locations, and clearance distances from proposed tree trunk centers to conductors are not specified. The vision analysis of Sheet 31 indicated tree canopies appearing to physically overlap the OHE line at drawing scale (1\"=20'), but without dimensioned clearances on the plan, exact compliance with clearance requirements (15 feet distribution, 50 feet transmission) cannot be verified from the submitted documents.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows both trees and OHE line; Sheet 21 shows OHE but no specific conductor or pole positions; no dimension lines or notes correlate tree locations to electric infrastructure.","reasoning":"To verify clearance compliance, the landscape plan must show explicit measurements from tree trunk centers to the outside electric conductor, with pole and conductor locations clearly marked. The absence of these dimensions prevents verification of compliance with lateral clearance requirements.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c5d1be6-7d35-4fa2-8909-ba4ff47d7c41","uuid":"cfad0f60-759d-40da-a763-bcc2785ab9dd"}
