{"level":30,"time":1778188816030,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":10,"prompt":"Please examine the Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) and identify:\n1. The location of the fire hydrant(s) shown on the plan\n2. Any fire escapes, fire exit stairs, or emergency exit structures\n3. Any fire lanes marked with dashed or colored lines\n4. The location of any transformer pads or electrical equipment if shown on this sheet\n5. Any dimension lines or distances marked on the plan\n6. Any callouts or notes related to electrical equipment clearances from fire features\n\nPlease be specific about locations, using building numbers and cardinal directions (north, south, east, west).","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10), here are the findings for each of your specific requests. \n\n*(Note: For clarity, cardinal directions in the descriptions below assume standard sheet orientation where the top of the page is North, though the official North Arrow on the plan points to the top-left corner).*\n\n**1. The location of the fire hydrant(s) shown on the plan**\nThere are three fire hydrants explicitly called out on this sheet, indicated by text boxes pointing to a symbol:\n*   **\"Existing Fire Hydrant\"**: Located in the top-left (northwest) corner of the drawing, outside the main property lines, near the curved \"Existing R.O.W.\" and north of the main site entrance.\n*   **\"Proposed Fire Hydrant\"**: Located in the bottom-left (southwest) area of the site. It is positioned on the south side of the main entrance drive aisle, near the beginning of the looped fire lane.\n*   **\"Proposed Fire Hydrant\"**: Located on the right (east) side of the property. It is situated adjacent to the eastern curve of the fire lane, positioned southeast of \"Bldg. 7\" and southwest of \"Bldg. 6\".\n\n**2. Any fire escapes, fire exit stairs, or emergency exit structures**\n*   There are no features explicitly labeled as fire escapes, fire exit stairs, or emergency exit structures visible on the building footprints (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) or the surrounding areas on this site plan. \n\n**3. Any fire lanes marked with dashed or colored lines**\n*   **Location:** The main looped drive aisle navigating through the center and around the perimeter of the buildings is designated as the fire lane. It is explicitly labeled with the text **\"Fire Lane\"** in multiple locations (e.g., between Bldg 1/3 and Bldg 2/4, and running horizontally south of Bldg 8).\n*   **Markings:** Because the plan is black and white, colored lines are not visible. The physical boundaries of the fire lane appear to be defined by solid lines representing the curbs. \n*   **Signage/Color details:** The plan includes a detail block titled **\"RESTRICTED, ZONE SIGNS, TYPE II\"** (bottom left) and **\"Fire Zone Notes\"**. Note 3 specifies: *\"Signs stating 'FIRE ZONE- TOW-AWAY ZONE' shall be posted on both ends of a fire zone and at each entry and exit point which constitutes a portion of the fire zone or fire lane. Signs shall comply with Standard City of Austin Detail 801S-6.\"* Note 5 specifies: *\"All private hydrants shall be painted red.\"*\n\n**4. The location of any transformer pads or electrical equipment if shown on this sheet**\n*   There are no explicit labels for transformer pads or specific electrical equipment units (such as \"Transformer\" or \"XFMR\") visible on this sheet.\n*   The plan does show designated electrical areas, specifically a **\"5' Elec. Easement\"** in the bottom-right (southeast) corner and an **\"Electric Easement\"** along the far right (east) property boundary, but no equipment is drawn or labeled within them.\n\n**5. Any dimension lines or distances marked on the plan**\nNumerous dimensions are provided, primarily to detail the fire lane and site boundaries. Examples include:\n*   **Fire Lane Widths:** Marked prominently as **\"26'\"** across the drive aisles in multiple locations (e.g., west of Bldg 2, north of Bldg 2, south of Bldg 4) and **\"24'\"** at the entrance aisle (bottom left).\n*   **Turning Radii:** Marked at the corners of the fire lanes with dimensions such as **\"R25'\"**, **\"R40'\"**, and **\"R45'\"**.\n*   **Building/Lane Clearances:** A dimension of **\"27.3'\"** is marked between the east side of Bldg 4 and the fire lane; **\"25'\"** is marked between the west side of Bldg 6 and the fire lane.\n*   **Setbacks:** A dashed perimeter line is labeled **\"25' Building Setback\"**.\n*   **Property Lines:** Boundary dimensions are provided, such as **\"S63° 02' 25\" E 419.96'\"** along the top property line.\n\n**6. Any callouts or notes related to electrical equipment clearances from fire features**\n*   A thorough review of the \"Notes\", \"Fire Zone Notes\", and other text blocks on the sheet reveals **no** callouts or notes specifically addressing electrical equipment clearances from fire hydrants or other fire features.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1436,"outputTokens":1016,"totalTokens":6437,"reasoningTokens":3985},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2043616]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine the Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) and identify:\n1. The location of the fire hydrant(s) shown on the plan\n2. Any fire escapes, fire exit stairs, or emergency exit structures\n3. Any fire lanes marked with dashed or colored lines\n4. The location of any transformer pads or electrical equipment if shown on this sheet\n5. Any dimension lines or distances marked on the plan\n6. Any callouts or notes related to electrical equipment clearances from fire features\n\nPlease be specific about locations, using building numbers and cardinal directions (north, south, east, west)."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-YkehoI1JgRim3FDKbmkW8d6G","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 07 May 2026 21:20:16 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::cdt7c-1778188771552-ceafd0785ca1"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10), here are the findings for each of your specific requests. \n\n*(Note: For clarity, cardinal directions in the descriptions below assume standard sheet orientation where the top of the page is North, though the official North Arrow on the plan points to the top-left corner).*\n\n**1. The location of the fire hydrant(s) shown on the plan**\nThere are three fire hydrants explicitly called out on this sheet, indicated by text boxes pointing to a symbol:\n*   **\"Existing Fire Hydrant\"**: Located in the top-left (northwest) corner of the drawing, outside the main property lines, near the curved \"Existing R.O.W.\" and north of the main site entrance.\n*   **\"Proposed Fire Hydrant\"**: Located in the bottom-left (southwest) area of the site. It is positioned on the south side of the main entrance drive aisle, near the beginning of the looped fire lane.\n*   **\"Proposed Fire Hydrant\"**: Located on the right (east) side of the property. It is situated adjacent to the eastern curve of the fire lane, positioned southeast of \"Bldg. 7\" and southwest of \"Bldg. 6\".\n\n**2. Any fire escapes, fire exit stairs, or emergency exit structures**\n*   There are no features explicitly labeled as fire escapes, fire exit stairs, or emergency exit structures visible on the building footprints (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) or the surrounding areas on this site plan. \n\n**3. Any fire lanes marked with dashed or colored lines**\n*   **Location:** The main looped drive aisle navigating through the center and around the perimeter of the buildings is designated as the fire lane. It is explicitly labeled with the text **\"Fire Lane\"** in multiple locations (e.g., between Bldg 1/3 and Bldg 2/4, and running horizontally south of Bldg 8).\n*   **Markings:** Because the plan is black and white, colored lines are not visible. The physical boundaries of the fire lane appear to be defined by solid lines representing the curbs. \n*   **Signage/Color details:** The plan includes a detail block titled **\"RESTRICTED, ZONE SIGNS, TYPE II\"** (bottom left) and **\"Fire Zone Notes\"**. Note 3 specifies: *\"Signs stating 'FIRE ZONE- TOW-AWAY ZONE' shall be posted on both ends of a fire zone and at each entry and exit point which constitutes a portion of the fire zone or fire lane. Signs shall comply with Standard City of Austin Detail 801S-6.\"* Note 5 specifies: *\"All private hydrants shall be painted red.\"*\n\n**4. The location of any transformer pads or electrical equipment if shown on this sheet**\n*   There are no explicit labels for transformer pads or specific electrical equipment units (such as \"Transformer\" or \"XFMR\") visible on this sheet.\n*   The plan does show designated electrical areas, specifically a **\"5' Elec. Easement\"** in the bottom-right (southeast) corner and an **\"Electric Easement\"** along the far right (east) property boundary, but no equipment is drawn or labeled within them.\n\n**5. Any dimension lines or distances marked on the plan**\nNumerous dimensions are provided, primarily to detail the fire lane and site boundaries. Examples include:\n*   **Fire Lane Widths:** Marked prominently as **\"26'\"** across the drive aisles in multiple locations (e.g., west of Bldg 2, north of Bldg 2, south of Bldg 4) and **\"24'\"** at the entrance aisle (bottom left).\n*   