{"level":30,"time":1778188816873,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJbvQuzWRWVg7teotzD4gk","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n     2→\n     3→This page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n    11→- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n    12→- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n    13→- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n    14→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n    15→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n    16→- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    19→- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n    20→- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n    21→- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n    22→- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n    23→- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n    28→\n    29→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    30→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4476681c-aa5e-420f-bcfe-9f06ce103f91","uuid":"7bb10300-996e-438a-bb01-36d2a7b25bfb","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n\nThis page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n\n**Key values**:\n- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778188817941,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24ZH09MQCY33HFBCRG8ZCJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the site plan, I can now provide findings for this grouping. Let me document my detailed research summary and then evaluate each checklist item.\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY — Overhead Electric Clearances\n\n**Overhead Electric Facilities Confirmed Present:**\n- Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey): Explicitly shows OHE (Overhead Utility Line) symbols with multiple utility poles and guy wires\n- Sheet 9 (Site Plan): Shows OHE line labeled with pole symbols crossing bottom property boundary near site entrances (Type II Driveways)\n- Sheet 11 (Grading Plan): Shows OHE lines on eastern and southern boundaries, parallel to Buildings 5-8\n- Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan): Shows OHE line labeled \"-OHE-\" running along southern boundary\n\n**Specific OHE Routing:**\n- **Eastern boundary:** Runs north-south parallel to Buildings 5-6, within/adjacent to marked electric easements (5' Electric Easement noted)\n- **Southern boundary:** Runs west-east parallel to Buildings 7-8, crosses two main site entrances (Type II Driveways labeled on Sheet 9)\n- **Poles and guy wires:** Multiple utility poles visible; at least one down guy wire shown on existing survey (Sheet 4, bottom-left)\n\n**Critical Gap — Clearance Verification NOT Provided:**\n1. **No surveyed conductor elevations** — NO building elevation sheets showing surveyed conductor heights relative to roof lines, overhangs, or vertical clearances\n2. **No clearance dimension annotations** — NO dimension lines shown from outside conductor to buildings, driveways, or site features\n3. **No vertical clearance verification** — NO section/profile exhibits showing heights from conductors to proposed grades, driveway surfaces, or building features\n4. **No measurement from outer conductor** — Cannot verify if dimensions originate from pole centerline vs. actual conductor location (critical per grouping guidance)\n5. **No surveyor mid-span data** — NO registered surveyor certification of pole locations and mid-span clearances for vertical clearance verification\n\n**Regulatory Requirements on Plans:**\n- Sheet 3 notes extensive Austin Energy transmission/distribution requirements including:\n  - Owner responsible for NESC/OSHA clearances\n  - **48-hour pre-construction safety meeting required** (via Andrew Perez 512-505-7153)\n  - 25-foot clearance from transmission structures for grading/digging\n  - 20-foot clearance during construction\n  - No structures in transmission easement\n  - Owner must provide additional easements as needed\n  - Owner responsible for costs of relocation\n\n**Deficiencies Identified:**\n- **EL-1.7**: Building elevations do NOT include surveyed conductor elevations\n- **EL-1.8**: Section/plan exhibits do NOT show clearance dimensions from outer conductor\n- **EL-1.23**: Clearance dimensions NOT provided on plans (cannot verify if measured from conductor vs. pole)\n- **EL-1.31**: NO registered surveyor data for vertical clearances despite apparent marginal clearances to driveways\n- **EL-1.46**: 48-hour notification note referenced on Sheet 3 but NOT explicitly stated on cover sheet or general notes (EL-1.46 requires cover sheet/general notes)\n- **EL-1.18**: Driveways cross overhead lines with no vertical clearance verification (16-18 feet required)\n- **EL-1.1, EL-1.2, EL-1.3, EL-1.6, EL-1.8, EL-1.9**: Clearance requirements cannot be verified without dimension annotations from outer conductor\n\nNow I'll evaluate each of the 47 checklist items:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce5a084e-a0f7-4302-9557-5dc167da4ff6","uuid":"de160c58-770a-41e2-b78e-286ba3a11b44"}
