. Tree symbols in the northwestern and southwestern corners (potential utility pole locations):**\n\n*   **Northwestern Corner:** Yes, there is a cluster of overlapping tree symbols directly in the extreme northwest corner of the property boundary. \n*   **Southwestern Corner:** Yes, as noted above, there is one tree symbol located directly in the extreme southwest corner, overlapping the boundary lines.\n\n**4. Tree species/designations based on labels:**\n\nBased on the \"KEY NOTES\" legend provided on the plan:\n*   \"SY\" = STREET YARD TREE\n*   \"M\" = MITIGATION TREE\n\nApplying this to the identified trees:\n*   **West Side / NW Corner:** The majority of the trees along the western boundary and in the NW corner are labeled \"**SY, M**\" (indicating they serve as both Street Yard and Mitigation trees). A few are labeled solely \"**M**\".\n*   **South Boundary / SE Area:** The trees explicitly labeled in the southeast cluster near the OHE line carry the \"**M**\" designation (Mitigation trees).\n*   **East Side:** The tree in the recessed alcove near the H.4 bubble has an \"**M**\" label pointing toward it. \n\n**5. Total distinct tree symbols within 25 lateral feet of visible electrical infrastructure:**\n\nBasing this count on visually identifiable electrical lines on this sheet (the `- E -` underground lines and the `- - - OHE - - -` overhead line) and utilizing the provided scale (1\" = 20'-0\", where 25 feet is 1.25 inches on the plan):\n\n*   **Along the West `- E -` line:** There are **6** distinct overlapping tree symbols directly adjacent to or sitting on top of this line running parallel to Valley View Road.\n*   **Along the South `- - - OHE - - -` line:** There is **1** tree symbol in the SW corner and **4** distinct circular symbols (including those marked with an 'X') in the SE corner cluster.\n*   **Total:** There appear to be **11** distinct tree or vegetation symbols located within 25 lateral feet of explicitly marked electrical lines on this pl