{"level":30,"time":1778188825964,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR250AGD2FSYP5XBHJSWY8M4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tree list in Sheet 32 is for EXISTING trees that are being surveyed for removal or retention. These are not the PROPOSED trees that are being planted. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows the proposed plantings with tags like \"M\" (mitigation), \"SY\" (street yard), \"PL\" (parking lot), \"P\" (plant), but the species are not identified on Sheet 31 itself.\n\nTo properly evaluate EL-1.37, I need to know what specific species are being proposed for planting in the narrow strip along the south and west edges of the property, particularly within 10 feet of the OHE lines. Let me check Sheet 31 blocks.md to see if it contains a plant schedule.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4476681c-aa5e-420f-bcfe-9f06ce103f91","uuid":"8738d945-8d8e-4d48-822b-cfe93d99f4ee"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188826251,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24Z7CJZ7JCB0W56KD32AN7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CbVjgxF52xgC9xN8rDXH7U","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 7 and 8 adjacent to southern overhead electric line","all buildings in proximity to overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric (OHE) line is shown on site plan (Sheet 9) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) running along the southern property boundary with utility poles visible, but no horizontal sky-to-ground clearance dimensions are provided for any buildings. Buildings 7 and 8 are identified as closest to the OHE line. Without dimension annotations showing the distance from the outside conductor to building walls, compliance with the 7.5-foot minimum horizontal clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 vision analysis confirms OHE line runs along southern boundary with at least 3 poles; Buildings 7 and 8 are closest to this line. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) also shows OHE line. Sheet 9 blocks description shows no clearance annotations or dimension lines in the detailed site plan drawing.","reasoning":"The grouping's documentation requirements section (page 1) explicitly requires 'Profile plans: Engineered, sealed profile drawings showing vertical relationships between overhead conductors and building features, including overhangs, balconies, and canopies, with dimensioned clearances.' The absence of any clearance dimensions on the site plan, combined with Buildings 7 and 8 being in proximity to the OHE line, makes verification of compliance impossible. This is status not-verifiable rather than fail because the feature exists but clearances are not documented.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 7 and 8 adjacent to southern overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution conductors are present on the southern boundary. The site plans do not provide clearance annotations showing that the minimum 15-foot radial clearance from the outside conductor is maintained. No dimension lines, radial clearance arcs, or verified distances are shown for any customer facilities (buildings, structures) relative to the distribution line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows OHE line along southern boundary with buildings nearby; Sheet 31 also depicts OHE but neither sheet shows radial clearance dimensions. The 5-foot electrical easements documented in facts.md indicate distribution-level infrastructure (not transmission), so the 15-foot radial clearance applies.","reasoning":"Without clearance dimension annotations or verified surveyor data, the 15-foot radial clearance requirement cannot be confirmed as met. The regulatory overview in the grouping specifies that 'All clearances must be measured from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), never from the utility pole centerline.' Without such dimensions shown on the plans, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8, particularly Buildings 7 and 8 adjacent to overhead distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are included in the plan set. The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and site plan (Sheet 9) show building locations and the overhead electric line, but neither includes elevation data for the conductors with dimension lines to verify required vertical clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 guide describes it as 'Preliminary Electrical Design Plan' focusing on 'underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes.' No building elevations with overhead conductor elevations were found in the plan set index (README.md lists sheets 1-39; no dedicated building elevation sheets identified).","reasoning":"The checklist requires 'Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors not included on building elevation sheets to demonstrate required clearances are met' per UCM § 1.10.3. The absence of surveyed elevation data showing conductor heights and clearance dimensions to buildings means this requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 7 and 8 in proximity to overhead distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plan and section view exhibits are absent. The site plan (Sheet 9) shows the overhead electric line and buildings in plan view only, with no dimension lines from the outside conductor to the outermost edges of buildings. No cross-sections, profile views, or enlarged details showing clearance dimensions from conductor to building faces are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 blocks show OHE line and buildings in plan view; Sheet 31 landscape plan also shows OHE in plan view only. No section views, elevations, or detail sheets were identified in the sheet index that show vertical clearance dimensions from conductors to buildings.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires 'Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings and building projections for clearance verification.' The complete absence of such exhibits means the requirement cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways adjacent to or beneath overhead distribution line routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways are shown on the site plan in proximity to overhead electric facilities. Minimum 16-foot vertical clearance (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot vertical clearance (areas with truck traffic) is required, but no vertical clearance dimensions are provided. Grading plan shows finished floor elevations but not vertical clearance from driveways to the lowest point of overhead facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows driveway routing through the site; overhead electric line runs along southern boundary. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows site topography and building elevations but no vertical clearance dimensions to the overhead line.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.6.2 requires verification of vertical clearances from driveways to 'lowest point of overhead electric facilities including telecommunications attachments.' Without surveyed data showing the overhead line height and vertical clearance dimensions to driveways, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line and all site features in proximity"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any plan sheets. The site plan and landscape plan identify the overhead electric (OHE) line but provide zero dimension annotations measuring clearances from the outside conductor to any site features. The grouping regulatory overview explicitly warns against 'Clearances measured from pole instead of conductor: Dimension annotations read \"10'-0\" from pole\" instead of \"15'-0\" from outside conductor\"; conductor may be several feet offset from pole center on three-phase installations.' This project provides no dimensions at all.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of Sheets 9, 31, 11, and 21 shows OHE line depicted but with zero dimension lines or annotations showing distances from the conductor. No measurement from conductor to buildings, driveways, parking, or other site features is provided on any sheet.","reasoning":"The regulatory overview (page 7-8 of grouping) identifies this pattern as a common violation: 'Missing profile plans: Site plan shows building and overhead lines in plan view only, no elevation/section view; no surveyed mid-span clearance data; cannot verify vertical clearances meet requirements.' This is a clear fail because the deficiency is present—no dimensions from conductor are shown, making it impossible to verify that measurements are being taken from the conductor rather than the pole.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 7 and 8 adjacent to southern overhead line; all driveways in proximity"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric line is present on the southern boundary with buildings and driveways nearby. The clearances from site features to the overhead line appear marginal based on the site plan visual layout, but no registered surveyor data is provided showing pole locations and mid-span clearances. Without surveyed elevation data, compliance with vertical clearance requirements cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows OHE line and Buildings 7/8 in close proximity on plan view. Vision analysis identified Buildings 7 and 8 as 'closest structures to this southern OHE line.' No surveyor stamp, elevation data, or mid-span clearance measurements are visible on any plan sheet.","reasoning":"Checklist item EL-1.31 specifically requires: 'Survey by registered surveyor showing pole locations and mid-span clearances not provided when existing overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements.' The visual proximity of Buildings 7/8 to the OHE line suggests clearances may be marginal, yet no surveyor data is provided to verify compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Overall site with overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The general notes on Sheet 3 do not include a required note stating that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. While Sheet 3 contains extensive Austin Energy requirements and Electric Transmission Notes, the specific 48-hour notification requirement is not explicitly stated as a general note.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of Sheet 3 general notes (via vision tool) shows extensive Electric Notes and Electric Transmission Notes but does not include the specific language: 'Owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines.' Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes #3 requires 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction' but this is about transmission lines specifically, not the general distribution overhead electric line.","reasoning":"Checklist item EL-1.46 requires a note specifically regarding notification before work near 'high-voltage overhead lines' per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752. While Sheet 3 has transmission-specific 48-hour meeting notes, it does not have a general cover sheet note about the 48-hour notification requirement for the overhead distribution line that exists on the property.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3251e5e3-3f03-4e85-9bab-d2e9039fdd51","uuid":"b150228c-cfec-47f2-9442-aaa54f4640f0"}
