{"level":30,"time":1778188827400,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TGURa9n3ojuZHDDdad83W5","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n     4→\n     5→NORTH\n     6→[North Arrow Symbol]\n     7→SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n     8→0 10 20 50\n     9→\n    10→## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n    11→\n    12→This block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n    13→- Building footprints\n    14→- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n    15→- Sidewalks and pathways\n    16→- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n    17→- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n    18→- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n    19→- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n    20→- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n    21→- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n    22→- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n    23→\n    24→## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n    25→\n    26→NOTE:\n    27→FINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\n    28→IF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\n    29→SUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\n    30→FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n    31→\n    32→## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n    33→\n    34→KEY NOTES:\n    35→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n    36→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n    37→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n    38→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n    39→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n    40→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n    41→[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\n    42→SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    43→PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    44→P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n    45→M - MITIGATION TREE\n    46→\n    47→## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n    48→\n    49→OWNER:\n    50→WM 41 AUSTIN\n    51→RE, LLC\n    52→\n    53→## Block 8: text_block — Name of the project.\n    54→\n    55→PROJECT NAME:\n    56→VALLEY VIEW\n    57→TOWNHOMES\n    58→\n    59→## Block 9: text_block — Address of the project location.\n    60→\n    61→PROJECT LOCATION:\n    62→3759 VALLEY\n    63→VIEW ROAD,\n    64→AUSTIN,\n    65→TEXAS 78704\n    66→\n    67→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4476681c-aa5e-420f-bcfe-9f06ce103f91","uuid":"6ac80910-e95e-4ede-8c90-a9efe71e9387","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — North arrow and graphical scale for the drawing.\n\nNORTH\n[North Arrow Symbol]\nSCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\n0 10 20 50\n\n## Block 2: drawing — A detailed site plan drawing showing the layout of buildings, parking lots, landscaping areas, and other site features. The drawing includes contours, property lines, utility lines, and symbols corresponding to the key notes.\n\nThis block contains a complex site plan drawing. It illustrates the layout of the proposed townhomes, parking areas, and surrounding landscaping. Key features include:\n- Building footprints\n- Parking lot with designated spaces and landscaping islands\n- Sidewalks and pathways\n- Trees and vegetation indicated by various symbols (e.g., circles for trees)\n- Contour lines with elevation labels (e.g., 680, 681, 682)\n- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\n- Fences marked with 'X' along the property lines\n- Various key note symbols (e.g., H.1, H.2, H.3) referencing the legend\n- Text labels indicating specific areas or features (e.g., 'Valley View Road', 'Existing Stone Retaining Wall')\n- Coordinates and station numbers along the edges\n\n## Block 4: notes — General notes regarding landscape requirements, including finished elevations for parking lot islands and supplemental irrigation during drought stages.\n\nNOTE:\nFINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\nIF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE. CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPVAR@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512)974-2199.\nSUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-8-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX 0.\nFOR PARKING-LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.4.7].\n\n## Block 5: notes — Key notes for various landscape elements, including proposed paving, street yard, parking lot landscaping, common open spaces, and fences, with corresponding symbols.\n\nKEY NOTES:\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.1'] [Pattern: Stippled] PROPOSED PAVING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.2'] [Pattern: Solid grey] STREET YARD\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.3'] [Pattern: Diagonal lines] STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.4'] [Pattern: Crosshatch] PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.5'] [Pattern: Vertical lines] PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.6'] [Pattern: Line with 'X's] WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n[Symbol: Hexagon with 'H.7'] [Pattern: Wavy lines] SOD\nSY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nPL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\nP - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\nM - MITIGATION TREE\n\n## Block 7: text_block — Details of the project owner.\n\nOWNER:\nWM 41 AUSTIN\nRE, LLC\n\n## Block 8: text_block — Name of the project.\n\nPROJECT NAME:\nVALLEY VIEW\nTOWNHOMES\n\n## Block 9: text_block — Address of the project location.\n\nPROJECT LOCATION:\n3759 VALLEY\nVIEW ROAD,\nAUSTIN,\nTEXAS 78704\n\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778188827871,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":19,"prompt":"Examine the Utility Tap Plan and identify:\n1. Underground water line (marked \"W\") locations and routing - especially near transformer pad locations\n2. Underground wastewater line (marked \"WW\") locations and routing\n3. Underground storm drain lines (marked \"SD\") locations and routing\n4. Any utility crossings or intersections with electrical infrastructure\n5. Cleanouts, lift stations, or other utility structures and their locations\n6. Any notes about horizontal or vertical separations from other utilities\n7. The location of the single private fire hydrant on the site\n8. Any gas lines or other utilities shown\nBe specific about which transformer locations (west side, east central, etc.) have nearby utilities and note the apparent spacing/clearances.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Utility Tap Plan\" for Valley View Townhomes, here are the observations addressing your specific points. \n\n### 1. Underground Water Line (\"W\") Locations and Routing\n*   **Legend Designation:** Proposed Water Lines are marked with a dashed line labeled \"W\".\n*   **Main Routing:** The primary proposed water main connects to the existing 6\" water line on Valley View Road (west side of the site) at a note reading \"Replace Existing Fire Hydrant with New Fire Hydrant\" and \"Install 6\" Gate Valve on Existing 6\" Water Line\". \n*   **Path:** The line runs eastward along the southern boundary of the property, utilizing lines such as \"212.62 lf 8\" C-900\". It branches northward in several locations to service the individual buildings (Buildings 1 through 8).\n*   **Near Transformer Pads:**\n    *   **West Side Transformer Pad:** Located south of the gap between Building 1 and Building 2. A proposed underground water line runs directly adjacent to the southern and eastern edges of this transformer pad to feed services to Buildings 1 and 2. \n    *   **East Central Transformer Pad:** Located south of Building 5 and east of Building 7. The main proposed water line runs generally parallel and to the south of the electrical line feeding this pad. A branch line feeding the central fire hydrant (\"11.98 lf 6\" C-900\") runs in very close proximity to the electrical line feeding this transformer pad.\n\n### 2. Underground Wastewater Line (\"WW\") Locations and Routing\n*   **Legend Designation:** Proposed Wastewater Lines are marked with a dashed line labeled \"WW\".\n*   **Main Routing:** The primary wastewater system runs through the central and northern portions of the site, collecting flow from individual building service lines (marked with an \"O\" symbol).\n*   **Path:** The system generally flows from east to west. It begins near the southeast corner of Building 6 at a \"6\" Cleanout Traffic Bearing FL Out 6\": 676.95\". It routes westward between the northern and southern rows of buildings, passing through manholes such as \"4\" Dia WW MH #3\" and \"4\" Dia WW MH #2\".\n*   **Outflow:** The entire site's wastewater routes to a \"Duplex Grinder Pump Lift Station\" near the northwest corner of Building 1. From there, a line marked \"29.4 lf 6\" SDR 26 @ 1.00%\" forces the wastewater westward across the property line to connect to an \"Existing #15466 Wastewater MH\".\n\n### 3. Underground Storm Drain Lines (\"SD\") Locations and Routing\n*   **Legend Designation:** Proposed Storm Drain lines are marked with a solid line labeled \"SD\".\n*   **Routing:** The site features an extensive network of storm drains to manage runoff.\n    *   A major line runs along the northern boundary behind Buildings 1, 3, and 5.\n    *   Lines run north-to-south between the building clusters (e.g., between Bldgs 1/2 and 3/4, and between Bldgs 3/4 and 5/6).\n    *   A line runs along the southern boundary, generally parallel to the proposed water main, flowing westward toward Valley View Road. Numerous square inlet/catch basin symbols are connected to this network.\n\n### 4. Utility Crossings or Intersections with Electrical Infrastructure\n*   **Legend Designation:** Proposed Underground Electric is marked with a solid line labeled \"E\".\n*   Several utility crossings are visible on the plan (shown in 2D layout):\n    *   **Southwest area:** The main proposed water line (\"W\") crosses the underground electric line (\"E\") that routes to the western transformer pad.\n    *   **South central area:** A storm drain line (\"SD\") crosses an underground electric line (\"E\") running between Building 7 and Building 6.\n    *   **East central area:** The 6\" water line branch feeding the private fire hydrant crosses the underground electric line (\"E\") routing into the eastern transformer pad.\n\n### 5. Cleanouts, Lift Stations, or Other Utility Structures\n*   **Lift Station:** A major structure is noted near the northwest property corner: \n    *   \"Duplex Grinder Pump Lift Station (DFU = 1,214) Rim: 687.00 FL In 8\": 671.18 FL In 6\" (SE): 680.61 FL Out 8\" (Out): 672.57\"\n*   **Wastewater Manholes:** \n    *   \"4\" Dia Drop WWMH #2 (DFU = 882) Rim: 684.77...\" (North of Bldg 3)\n    *   \"4\" Dia WWMH #3 (DFU = 590) Rim: 681.18...\" (Between Bldg 7 and 8)\n*   **Cleanouts:** Numerous cleanouts are labeled, primarily at the ends of lines or building connections. Examples include:\n    *   \"6\" 2-Way Cleanout Rim: 687.79...\" (Near west property line)\n    *   \"6\" Cleanout Traffic Bearing FL Out 8\": 671.49\" (Between Bldg 1 & 2)\n    *   \"6\" Cleanout Traffic Bearing FL Out 6\": 682.14\" (North of Bldg 4)\n    *   \"6\" Cleanout Traffic Bearing FL Out 6\": 676.95\" (Southeast of Bldg 6)\n\n### 6. Notes About Horizontal or Vertical Separations\nWhile the plan does not dictate a specific numeric minimum separation distance (e.g., \"maintain 5 feet\") in a dedicated note, it addresses the responsibility of verifying crossings and locations in the general notes:\n*   **Utility Notes (Bottom Center):**\n    *   \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"\n    *   \"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"\n*   **General Note (Bottom Right Box):**\n    *   \"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"\n\n### 7. Location of the Single Private Fire Hydrant\n*   The private fire hydrant on the site is located centrally, positioned in the paved area between Building 4 (to the north) and Building 7 (to the south). \n*   It is fed from the south by a line labeled: \"12.24 lf 6\" DI Fire Lead Fire Hydrant Assembly See Detail 511-AW-02\", which branches off an \"8\"x6\" Tee\" and passes through a \"6\" Gate Valve\". \n*   *(Note: This is distinct from the note on the western street frontage indicating \"Replace Existing Fire Hydrant with New Fire Hydrant\").*\n\n### 8. Any Gas Lines or Other Utilities Shown\n*   Based on the provided legend and a visual scan of the line types on the drawing, **no gas lines (typically marked \"G\") are shown on this specific Utility Tap Plan.** \n*   The only utilities explicitly documented and routed on this sheet are Water (W), Wastewater (WW), Storm Drain (SD), and Underground/Overhead Electric (E / OHE).\n\n***\n\n### Requested Table Transcription\nAs requested, here is the exact, character-by-character transcription of the table found in the bottom left quadrant of the document:\n\n**Drainage Fixture Unit Table**\n| Building # | Building Type | DFU's |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | 4 Plex | 136 |\n| 2 | 6 Plex | 204 |\n| 3 | 5 Plex | 170 |\n| 4 | 5 Plex | 170 |\n| 5 | 4 Plex | 136 |\n| 6 | 4 Plex | 136 |\n| 7 | 5 Plex | 170 |\n| 8 | 6 Plex | 204 |","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1462,"outputTokens":1861,"totalTokens":6169,"reasoningTokens":2846},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2591576]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Utility Tap Plan and identify:\n1. Underground water line (marked \"W\") locations and routing - especially near transformer pad locati