ucture\n\nBefore measuring, I should verify whether ECM Appendix F is referenced elsewhere in the documentation or if I need to look up utility compatibility for these specific species. The grouping criteria requires checking the UC column in Appendix F to identify utility-compatible trees and those with mature heights ≥ 40 feet. The four species in the plan are Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, and Mexican Redbud—I need their botanical names and mature height data to properly evaluate compliance.\n\nSince I don't have direct access to Appendix F, I can't confirm utility compatibility or mature heights as specified. Instead, I'll measure the actual clearances from the trees to transformer pads (requiring >10 feet) and to overhead electrical lines (which have varying distance requirements). Using the scale on Sheet 31 (1\" = 20'), I can calculate distances to assess whether the placement meets infrastructure separation standards.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f00b2f4f-4bf8-4369-b6e1-683efc1760e1","uuid":"eeed7932-3a10-48ba-85fc-acbe370239d7"}
