{"level":30,"time":1778188833492,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":35,"prompt":"Review Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations and Plant List) to determine: (1) Are specific trees or tree locations on the landscape plan identified by species on this sheet? (2) Do the plant schedule tables (Shade Trees, Ornamental Trees) reference locations on the landscape plan such as \"western boundary trees\" or \"southeast corner trees\"? (3) Is there any callout or note that cross-references specific species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) to the landscape plan symbols (M, ST, PL, P)? (4) What are the mature heights and utility compatibility statuses of the proposed species?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed review of Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations and Plant List), here are the findings regarding your questions:\n\n**(1) Are specific trees or tree locations on the landscape plan identified by species on this sheet?**\nNo. The \"PLANT LIST\" tables on this sheet only list the quantity of each species to be planted overall. There is no column, note, or text identifying where specific trees are located on the actual landscape plan. \n\n**(2) Do the plant schedule tables (Shade Trees, Ornamental Trees) reference locations on the landscape plan such as \"western boundary trees\" or \"southeast corner trees\"?**\nNo. The plant schedule tables (\"SHADE TREES\", \"ORNAMENTAL TREES\", \"SHRUBS\", \"GROUNDCOVERS\") do not contain any references to specific locations or areas of the site (e.g., \"western boundary trees\"). The tables only contain columns for \"SYM.\" (Symbol), \"QTY.\" (Quantity), \"COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME\", and \"MIN. SPEC.\" (Minimum Specification). \n\n**(3) Is there any callout or note that cross-references specific species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) to the landscape plan symbols (M, ST, PL, P)?**\nNo. There are no notes or callouts cross-referencing these species to the alphabetical symbols \"M\", \"ST\", \"PL\", or \"P\". Instead, the \"SYM.\" column in the \"PLANT LIST\" uses graphical symbols for the trees:\n*   **Live Oak** is assigned a graphical circle with a plus sign inside.\n*   **Cedar Elm** is assigned a graphical circle with a center dot and radiating lines.\n*   **Texas Mountain Laurel** is assigned a scalloped circle (cloud-like shape) with a center dot.\n*   **Mexican Redbud** is assigned a graphical circle containing three smaller circles (clover-like shape).\n\n**(4) What are the mature heights and utility compatibility statuses of the proposed species?**\nThis sheet **does not** list the mature heights or the utility compatibility statuses for any of the proposed species. The only height information provided is the required planting size listed under the \"MIN. SPEC.\" column:\n*   **Live Oak:** \"16' HT. MINIMUM\"\n*   **Cedar Elm:** \"16' HT. MINIMUM\"\n*   **Texas Mountain Laurel:** \"8' HT. MINIMUM\"\n*   **Mexican Redbud:** \"10' HT. MINIMUM\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1443,"outputTokens":528,"totalTokens":3479,"reasoningTokens":1508},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2584864]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being vali