.md:    Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, grading contours, drainage easements, and the specific locations of the cross-section cut lines (XS 1, XS 2, XS 3) relative to buildings 5 and 6 and existing retaining walls.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:This sheet contains the Addressing Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, illustrating the layout, numbering, and finished floor elevations of the proposed residential buildings. Its primary purpose is to define the unit addressing scheme, building square footages, and spatial relationships between the structures, property boundaries, and existing site features like easements.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/guide.md:*   **Block 1: drawing** — Main site addressing plan showing the townhome layout, individual unit locations, building dimensions, and property lines. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of buildings, unit addressing sequences, finished floor elevations (FFEs), and locations of surrounding easements and utility infrastructure.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4476681c-aa5e-420f-bcfe-9f06ce103f91","uuid":"eeda08b8-09a8-4ae5-a696-bcd98c626beb","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-05/guide.md:    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of proposed buildings, contour lines, utility routings, and the exact placement of erosion controls like silt fences, mulch socks, and tree protection fencing. *READ* for specific spot elevations and building square footages.\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md:This sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail e