{"level":30,"time":1778188840794,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EgGCzgvgarpbbRSxECXyBq","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 37 — Landscape Details\n     2→\n     3→Contains landscape details for tree planting, tree protection, and shrubs.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides standard landscape detail drawings for the Valley View Townhomes project. It primarily contains City of Austin compliant specifications for tree planting, tree protection during construction, and general shrub planting guidelines.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   **Tree Protection Critical Root Zone (CRZ)**: Radius = 1ft per inch (12mm per mm) of trunk diameter.\n    11→*   **Tree Protection Mulch**: 150mm (6\") depth inside the protection zone.\n    12→*   **Tree Protection Clearance**: Minimum 1.5m (5') necessary work space; if less, add boards strapped to trunk.\n    13→*   **Tree Planting Pit Size**: 3x the width of the rootball.\n    14→*   **Tree Planting Stakes**: 8' length black painted steel T-post, driven min. 18\" below tree pit.\n    15→*   **Tree Planting Rootball**: Set level to grade or slightly above grade (1/2\").\n    16→*   **Tree Trunk Support**: Arborbrace webbing allowing a maximum 2\" movement in any direction.\n    17→*   **Planting Mulch (Trees & Shrubs)**: 3\" depth organic wood mulch; for trees, keep mulch 6\" away from the root crown.\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 1: diagram — City of Austin Tree Protection Detail**: Illustrates standard fencing and mulching requirements to protect existing trees during construction (Standard 610S-4). READ the block content for specific CRZ calculation formulas and standard watershed protection notes. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the fencing relative to the dripline and building footprint.\n    22→*   **Block 2: diagram — Shrub Planting Detail**: Shows the standard trenching and soil amendment layout for shrubbery. READ the block content for contractor coordination instructions regarding dirt removal and amended soil mix placement. Use VISION to observe the 15\" planting depth and continuous soil trenching layout.\n    23→*   **Block 3: diagram — City of Austin Tree Planting Detail**: Comprehensive cross-section and specification list for new tree installations. READ the block content for extensive text instructions covering rootball preparation, acceptable pruning, hardware specifics (Arborbrace webbing, Stakesafe protectors), and soil settling methods. Use VISION to examine the 4'-6\" stake height above ground, the 3x rootball width pit dimensions, and the rootball elevation relative to the finished grade.\n    24→*   **Block 4: seal — Professional Seal & Administrative**: Contains the Registered Landscape Architect seal (dated 02/13/2026), project title (Valley View Townhomes), and sheet indexing (34 of 35). READ for basic administrative verification.\n    25→\n    26→---\n    27→\n    28→- `block-3.md` — diagram: Detailed drawing showing the requirements for planting a tree in the City of Austin. Includes instru\n    29→\n    30→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    31→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e41429b8-28b1-469f-8aa7-638b39040e37","uuid":"31a492ce-a50f-4144-8d7f-9742912ce55b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-37/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 37 — Landscape Details\n\nContains landscape details for tree planting, tree protection, and shrubs.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides standard landscape detail drawings for the Valley View Townhomes project. It primarily contains City of Austin compliant specifications for tree planting, tree protection during construction, and general shrub planting guidelines.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Tree Protection Critical Root Zone (CRZ)**: Radius = 1ft per inch (12mm per mm) of trunk diameter.\n*   **Tree Protection Mulch**: 150mm (6\") depth inside the protection zone.\n*   **Tree Protection Clearance**: Minimum 1.5m (5') necessary work space; if less, add boards strapped to trunk.\n*   **Tree Planting Pit Size**: 3x the width of the rootball.\n*   **Tree Planting Stakes**: 8' length black painted steel T-post, driven min. 18\" below tree pit.\n*   **Tree Planting Rootball**: Set level to grade or slightly above grade (1/2\").\n*   **Tree Trunk Support**: Arborbrace webbing allowing a maximum 2\" movement in any direction.\n*   **Planting Mulch (Trees & Shrubs)**: 3\" depth organic wood mulch; for trees, keep mulch 6\" away from the root crown.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — City of Austin Tree Protection Detail**: Illustrates standard fencing and mulching requirements to protect existing trees during construction (Standard 610S-4). READ the block content for specific CRZ calculation formulas and standard watershed protection notes. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the fencing relative to the dripline and building footprint.\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Shrub Planting Detail**: Shows the standard trenching and soil amendment layout for shrubbery. READ the block content for contractor coordination instructions regarding dirt removal and amended soil mix placement. Use VISION to observe the 15\" planting depth and continuous soil trenching layout.\n*   **Block 3: diagram — City of Austin Tree Planting Detail**: Comprehensive cross-section and specification list for new tree installations. READ the block content for extensive text instructions covering rootball preparation, acceptable pruning, hardware specifics (Arborbrace webbing, Stakesafe protectors), and soil settling methods. Use VISION to examine the 4'-6\" stake height above ground, the 3x rootball width pit dimensions, and the rootball elevation relative to the finished grade.\n*   **Block 4: seal — Professional Seal & Administrative**: Contains the Registered Landscape Architect seal (dated 02/13/2026), project title (Valley View Townhomes), and sheet indexing (34 of 35). READ for basic administrative verification.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — diagram: Detailed drawing showing the requirements for planting a tree in the City of Austin. Includes instru\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}}}
