, drives, concrete pads or walkways, compacted surfaces for driving, etc.\n    29→Are any underground storage tanks existing or proposed? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    30→\n    31→Section 9: Related Cases\n    32→FILE NUMBERS\n    33→Zoning Case? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    34→Restrictive Covenant? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    35→Subdivision? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    36→Land Status Determination? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    37→Existing Site Plan? [ ] Yes [x] No\n    38→\n    39→City of Austin | Consolidated Site Plan Completeness Check Application 10/21/24 | Page 5 of 8\n    40→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ee23800-1891-4c6c-9860-87ab169d6f67","uuid":"63a31b13-fcd0-4ae8-84b8-c75d6656b323","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/consolidated-site-plan-application/04-application-assessment-and-site-area.md","content":"# Application Assessment and Site Area\n\n*Contains traffic impact analysis requirements, site area calculations, existing/proposed zoning use tables, and impervious cover percentages.*\n\nSection 7: Application Assessment\nIs a Traffic Impact Analysis (TIA) required? [ ] Yes [x] No\nLarge Retail Use, as defined in Sec. 25-2-815? [ ] Yes [x] No\nIs this use Conditional within the site's zoning district? [ ] Yes [x] No\nHas there been a Development Assessment or Concept Site Plan? [ ] Yes [x] No File Number: \nWill all parking be located on site? [x] Yes [ ] No (If No, an Off-Site/Shared Parking Application and fees are required)\nShared parking? [ ] Yes [x] No (If Yes, an Off-Site/Shared Parking Application and fees are required)\n\nSection 8: Site Area Information\nGross Site Area: Acres -OR- Sq. Ft. 2.16\nSee Section 25-1-21(44) of the Land Development Code for a definition of Gross Site Area.\nNet Site Area: Acres -OR- Sq. Ft. 2.16\nSee Section 25-8-62 of the Land Development Code for a definition of Net Site Area.\nLimits of Construction: Acres -OR- Sq. Ft. \n\n| EXISTING ZONING | EXISTING USE | TRACT # | ACRES / SQ FT | PROPOSED USE |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| MF-2 | Assisted Living | 1 | 2.16 / | Multi-family townhomes |\n| | | | / | |\n| | | | / | |\n| | | | / | |\n\nExisting Impervious Cover (%): 65 Proposed Impervious Cover (%): 59.5\nIndicate the existing and proposed percent of impervious cover. Impervious cover is anything that prevents water from percolating into the ground, such as buildings, drives, concrete pads or walkways, compacted surfaces for driving, etc.\nAre any underground storage tanks existing or proposed? [ ] Yes [x] No\n\nSection 9: Related Cases\nFILE NUMBERS\nZoning Case? [ ] Yes [x] No\nRestrictive Covenant? [ ] Yes [x] No\nSubdivision? [ ] Yes [x] No\nLand Status Determination? [ ] Yes [x] No\nExisting Site Plan? [ ] Yes [x] No\n\nCity of Austin | Consolidated Site Plan Completeness Check Application 10/21/24 | Page 5 of 8\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778188854105,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR250PSK5JN886ZMXANH57BH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The measure-distance tool is failing because it can't resolve the document version. Let me try a different approach - I'll examine the site plan documents manually and use the vision tool to get more specific information about the exact distances and relationships.\n\nLet me focus on what I can determine from the existing analysis and create findings based on what I've found:\n\nFrom my research so far:\n1. **Electrical Infrastructure Present:** YES - OHE line on western and southern boundaries, transformer pads, underground equipment, poles\n2. **Trees Proposed:** YES - 40+ tree symbols on landscape plan, including trees near electrical infrastructure\n3. **Clearance Issues Identified:**\n   - Trees shown directly adjacent to/overlapping OHE line on southern boundary\n   - Trees along western boundary near underground electric lines\n   - Trees in corners near poles\n\nWhat I CANNOT verify without additional documentation:\n1. **Plant species and utility compatibility:** I have a plant list (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but no ECM Appendix F to verify UC status or mature heights\n2. **Exact clearance distances:** Vision tool shows trees near infrastructure but I don't have precise measurements\n3. **Whether overhead electric is distribution or transmission:** No voltage classification provided\n\nLet me look at what information I can definitively find or cannot find:\n\n**FINDINGS SO FAR:**\n\n**Can verify:**\n1. Trees ARE shown on landscape plan near electrical infrastructure (confirmed by vision)\n2. Plant species are listed on Sheet 35 but no utility compatibility designation shown\n3. No clearance dimensions shown on landscape plan\n4. Landscape plan shows utility lines but doesn't explicitly reference clearance requirements\n\n**Cannot verify without additional sources:**\n1. Utility compatibility (UC) designation of proposed species per ECM Appendix F\n2. Mature heights per ECM Appendix F\n3. Exact measured clearances between specific trees and electrical infrastructure\n4. Voltage classification of electrical infrastructure (distribution vs. transmission)\n\nBased on this, many items will be \"not-verifiable\" because:\n\n\n- The plant schedule lacks utility-compatible status for each species\n- No clearance measurements or calculations appear on the plans\n- There's no documentation showing how species selection was validated against utility compatibility standards\n\nNow I'll work through the 15 checklist items systematically. Items like EL-2.1 (non-UC trees within 15 feet of distribution lines) and EL-2.2 (non-UC trees within 50 feet of transmission) cannot be verified since the plant species lack UC designations and transmission lines aren't identified. Similarly, EL-2.3 regarding large trees near distribution infrastructure cannot be confirmed without mature height data from the ECM appendix.\n\nFor items EL-2.4 through EL-2.9, the issues center on missing clearance documentation. While the plans show trees positioned near poles, transformer pads, and underground equipment, there are no specific measurements to verify compliance with the 10-foot pole clearance, 10-foot pad-mounted equipment clearance, or 5-foot underground equipment clearance requirements. Root barrier details for trees within 20 feet of underground utilities are also absent from the documentation.\n\nMoving to the plant identification and labeling requirements, the landscape plan fails to identify individual species at their locations—the plant list exists separately but symbols on the plan itself lack species designation. There's also no visual differentiation marking which trees meet the \"large tree\" threshold of 40+ feet. The clearance dimensions themselves are entirely missing, making it impossible to confirm whether measurements were taken from the conductor versus the pole, or from the trunk versus the canopy edge. The overhead electric line appears on the plan, but the relationship between most trees and these facilities lacks documented verification. Finally, no approval documentation from Austin Energy regarding any requested variations is included in the submission. represents which species. For EL-2.14, no clearance dimensions appear on the plans, so this requirement doesn't apply. Regarding EL-2.15, while trees are positioned near electrical infrastructure in the vision analysis, I lack the utility compatibility data and height information needed to confirm whether they fall within prohibited clearance zones or if Austin Energy approval exists.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f00b2f4f-4bf8-4369-b6e1-683efc1760e1","uuid":"85f9983f-bddb-4fa4-804a-237af19f9566"}
