{"level":30,"time":1778188871987,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2518YYD6Q8KWVJM2ZPWCHJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Sheet 30 is the Existing Tree Plan (which deals with removal), and Sheet 31 is the Landscape Plan (proposed plantings). Now let me look at the specific blocks for Sheet 31 to see if there are notes about electrical clearances that I may have missed.\n\nActually, let me step back and compile my findings. Based on my research:\n\n**ESTABLISHED FACTS:**\n1. Electrical infrastructure is present: OHE line on west/south boundaries, transformer pads (east and west), underground electric lines, poles\n2. Trees ARE proposed on the landscape plan: 40+ tree symbols throughout the site\n3. Proposed tree species: Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud\n4. Trees shown in proximity to electrical infrastructure per vision analysis:\n   - 6 trees along western underground electric line\n   - 5 trees along southern OHE line\n   - Trees near corners where poles exist\n5. No clearance dimensions shown on landscape plan\n6. No species/utility compatibility designations shown on landscape plan symbols\n7. No Austin Energy approval letters referenced in any documents reviewed\n\n**CRITICAL GAPS:**\n1. ECM Appendix F data not available (needed for UC designation and mature height)\n2. Exact clearance distances not dimensioned\n3. Tree species not identified on landscape plan symbols themselves\n4. No documentation of electrical infrastructure assessment in landscape plan notes\n5. No reference to utility clearance requirements in landscape notes\n\nNow let me systematically evaluate each checklist item:\n\n**EL-2.1:** Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- Reason: No UC designations shown for proposed species\n\n**EL-2.2:** Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission\n- Status: N/A (no transmission line identified - only distribution/service lines on site)\n- Reason: Facts.md only mentions 5' electric easements, not transmission easement\n\n\n- **EL-2.3:** Large trees (40+ ft mature) within 25 ft of distribution - NOT-VERIFIABLE because plant specs only list minimum purchase heights (16' HT minimum for shade trees), not mature heights per ECM Appendix F. **EL-2.4:** Large trees within 50 ft of transmission - N/A since no transmission line identified on site. **EL-2.5:** Trees in transmission easement - N/A because facts.md references only plat-dedicated electric easements, not transmission easement. **EL-2.6:** Trees within 10 ft of utility pole - NOT-VERIFIABLE (possibly FAIL) as the landscape plan shows trees positioned at corners with poles present, but lacks clearance dimensions and precise measurements. **EL-2.7:** Trees near pad-mounted equipment - NOT-VERIFIABLE (possibly FAIL) since the vision indicates trees adjacent to transformer pad locations without exact measurements. **EL-2.8:** Trees within 5 ft of underground electric equipment - NOT-VERIFIABLE because while the electrical plan shows underground equipment, the landscape plan provides no clearance measurements. **EL-2.9:** Root barriers for trees within 20 ft of underground equipment - NOT-VERIFIABLE or FAIL as no root barrier details appear in landscape plan notes or details. **EL-2.10:** Plant legend does not identify species - FAIL because the landscape plan uses symbols (M, SY, PL, P) without indicating which symbol corresponds to which species; species names only appear on Sheet 35 plant schedule, not on the landscape plan itself where the trees are located. **EL-2.11:** Large trees not differentiated on plans - FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE since the landscape plan doesn't designate which trees qualify as \"large\" (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) or show mature height information. **EL-2.12 and EL-2.13:** Clearance measurement methodology - PASS or N/A as no clearance dimensions appear on the plans, making these measurement issues inapplicable. **EL-2.14:** Trees not shown in relation to overhead facilities - FAIL because while the landscape plan depicts the OHE line on the southern boundary, there's no cross-reference or verification that clearances between tree symbols and the OHE line meet requirements; trees are drawn but lack callouts or measurements confirming adequate clearances. **EL-2.15:** Trees in prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval - FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE because the vision analysis indicates trees near overhead and underground electric lines (prohibited zones), but I can't definitively determine restricted zones without understanding the UC/height data, and no Austin Energy approval letters are provided or referenced.\n\nThe deficiency language specifies that a violation occurs when trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval. From the vision analysis, trees are clearly shown near electrical infrastructure, and the grouping establishes prohibited zones based on distance thresholds and tree type. However, without precise measurements or confirmed tree species UC status, I cannot definitively establish whether the proposed trees actually fall within those prohibited zones, making this NOT-VERIFIABLE. I should also check for any additional documentation referencing clearances or approvals.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f00b2f4f-4bf8-4369-b6e1-683efc1760e1","uuid":"a89f0680-ae7d-4db2-bf9c-297e781e47bc"}
