{"level":30,"time":1778188896315,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR252AYG1ADY7MBRSN50YA9C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me use the vision tool to examine the electrical infrastructure and tree locations more carefully. First, let me look at Sheet 21 to see the transformer locations:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed658f06-b65b-479d-b752-f47b92243df6","uuid":"c01c3066-3c48-4c85-9441-73e7151803a9"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188898090,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR251ZN28RTXZBW8R5PRQEYE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CRITICAL FINDINGS from Sheet 3:\n\n**Sheet 3, Block 13 - Electric Transmission Notes:**\nNote 1: \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.\"\n\nThis is EXACTLY matching the requirement for EL-2.2 and EL-2.4 (trees within 50 feet of transmission).\n\nHowever, this is transmission-specific. The grouping distinguishes between:\n- Distribution facilities (< 60kV, typically 12.47kV or 34.5kV)\n- Transmission facilities (≥ 60kV, such as 69kV, 138kV, 345kV)\n\nThe facts.md and electrical plan appear to show only DISTRIBUTION and UNDERGROUND facilities, not transmission.\n\nBut the site plan notes reference \"transmission easement\" and \"transmission structures\" - so there IS transmission infrastructure on or near this site. However, facts.md says there's no transmission easement identified. Let me reconcile this.\n\nLooking at facts.md again:\n- It mentions electric easements from Mecey Subdivision (5' wide)\n- But NO transmission easement is listed\n\nBut Sheet 3 clearly references transmission structures, transmission easements, and provides extensive requirements for them.\n\nThis is a discrepancy. The electrical plan notes acknowledge transmission facilities are present or adjacent to the site, but facts.md doesn't list them as being on the property.\n\nLooking back at the electrical plan (Sheet 21) vision analysis:\n- The OHE line shown is on the WESTERN BOUNDARY (outside the property)\n- This could be transmission infrastructure running along the right-of-way\n\nSo the situation appears to be:\n1. There is a TRANSMISSION line running along the western property boundary (outside the property)\n2. The transmission notes in Sheet 3 require:\n   - No trees within transmission easement (N/A if not on property)\n   - No trees within 25 feet of transmission structures\n   - Tree pruning responsibility within 10 feet of center line of overhead facilities\n\nThe \"25 feet of transmission structures\" requirement in Sheet 3 is STRICTER than the 50 feet in the grouping code (UCM § 1.10.10.4). The critical issue is whether proposed trees along the western boundary fall within this 25-foot setback. Sheet 31 shows approximately 5 to 6 tree symbols positioned along the western boundary where the overhead line runs, and these appear to be situated roughly 10 to 30 feet from the transmission structures—potentially violating the stricter setback requirement.\n\nHowever, since the electrical plan indicates poles are located outside the property boundary, I cannot definitively confirm whether the western trees are within the 25-foot threshold without precise measurements. The lack of exact distances makes this determination impossible to verify conclusively.\n\nFor the checklist items, non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution lines cannot be verified because plant species lack UC designations on the landscape plan. Similarly, the 50-foot transmission setback requirement is not verifiable, though Sheet 3's stricter 25-foot note suggests a potential failure condition if trees are indeed positioned within that distance.\n\nLarge trees present another verification gap—the specifications only show minimum purchase heights rather than mature heights as required by ECM Appendix F, making it impossible to assess the 25-foot distribution and 50-foot transmission setbacks. Trees within transmission easements don't apply here since no easement is identified on the property itself, with the transmission line appearing to run along an adjacent right-of-way instead.\n\nUtility pole proximity also cannot be verified with precision. While trees are visible near corners where poles exist, exact measurements aren't provided, though the vision analysis does show trees in the northwest and southwest corners.\n\nPad-mounted transformer equipment and underground electric installations lack clearance measurements on the landscape plan, preventing verification of the 10-foot and 5-foot setback requirements respectively. Root barrier specifications are entirely absent from the landscape details and notes, resulting in a clear failure. Additionally, the plant legend fails to identify species—the landscape plan uses symbols (M, SY, PL, P, etc.) that aren't defined, and while Sheet 35 contains a separate plant schedule with species names, the actual drawing doesn't connect which species corresponds to which symbol.\n\nLarge trees aren't differentiated on the plan, with no indication of which plantings will reach 40+ feet at maturity. Clearance measurements aren't shown, so whether they're taken from conductors versus poles or from trunk versus canopy cannot be assessed. The landscape plan shows the overhead electric line along the southern boundary and underground lines, but lacks explicit verification that trees are positioned appropriately in relation to these facilities.\n\nTrees planted near the western boundary where transmission infrastructure exists may violate the 25-foot prohibition zone without documented Austin Energy approval. Since I cannot confirm either that plantings stay outside this buffer or that written approval exists, this fails verification. The plan does display the OHE line, but doesn't demonstrate compliance with clearance requirements.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f00b2f4f-4bf8-4369-b6e1-683efc1760e1","uuid":"753dff64-b4f8-433b-b7dc-a280d090c78c"}
