ace parking within the right-of-way. Is the intention to keep the existing on-street parking indicated on the site plan?\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/04-drainage-engineering-review.md:* U1: Comment pending. We still need an analysis of the existing channel on the site. If you are planning to discharge to it, we will need to ensure it has capacity. Please note that your outfall is within an electrical easement. You will need to provide approval from the easements’ owner to do this. Please note the intent of this code is also to cause no adverse impact to your neighbors.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"level":30,"time":1778188901107,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR250N78H2WEWW86A2S3RZT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012heGdovqXwJARSTkbgNQQb","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8 near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on existing conditions survey and are shown on proposed site plan along western and southern property boundaries. However, no clearance dimension annotations are provided showing the horizontal sky-to-ground distance from the outside conductor to any building faces. Surveyed conductor locations and dimensions are required to verify 7.5-foot minimum clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions (Sheet 4) show overhead electric (OHE) lines running north-south along Valley View Road and east-west along the southern property boundary. Proposed site plan (Sheet 9) confirms OHE lines at site perimeter with buildings positioned in the interior. However, no dimension lines or annotations show clearances from outside conductor to building faces.","reasoning":"The absence of clearance dimensions, combined with the lack of surveyed conductor elevations, means that compliance with the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified from the available site plan documents. While the visual spacing suggests buildings are distant from the lines, code requires affirmative dimensional evidence.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8 and site features near overhead distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution facilities are shown on site plan, but no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that customer facilities (buildings, structures) maintain the minimum 15-foot radial clearance from the outside conductor of primary and neutral conductors. Surveyed conductor locations are required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows overhead electric (OHE) lines at property boundaries with buildings positioned internally. However, no radial clearance dimensions are provided from outside conductor to any customer facilities. The conductor type (primary vs. secondary vs. neutral) is not identified on the plans.","reasoning":"Without surveyed conductor locations and radial clearance dimensions, and without identification of conductor types, the 15-foot radial clearance requirement cannot be verified. Code requires explicit dimensional evidence from outside conductor to facilities.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building projections (overhangs, balconies, roofs)"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets or section views are provided showing building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs) in relation to overhead electric conductors. Without these exhibits, the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for projections cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan sheets reviewed (sheets 1-39) do not include building elevation views with detailed projections or section views showing vertical/horizontal relationships between building elements and overhead conductors.","reasoning":"Building elevation sheets are essential to verify clearances for projections. Their absence means this requirement cannot be evaluated from the submitted site plan documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near Valley View Road right-of-way with adjacent overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities exist in the Valley View Road right-of-way adjacent to the site. Buildings are proposed adjacent to this ROW, but no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate maintenance of the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from these ROW facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings in relationship to Valley View Road where overhead utilities exist. However, no dimensions are provided showing horizontal setback distances from the ROW electric facilities to building faces.","reasoning":"Code requires explicit dimensional verification of clearances from ROW utilities to customer facilities. Unmarked site plan does not provide this evidence.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are included in the site plan package. Code requires registered surveyor data showing conductor elevations to verify that required clearances from buildings are met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all 39 sheets of the primary site plan revealed no building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevation data or clearance dimension annotations. Sheet 9 (Site Plan), Sheet 11 (Grading Plan), and other sheets show general layout but no building elevations with conductor heights.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires surveyed elevations of overhead conductors on building elevation sheets. Their absence is a deficiency regardless of whether clearances are actually adequate.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings and building projections within potential clearance distance of overhead electric conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits with dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to building edges and projections are not provided. Code requires dimensioned clearance exhibits showing the measurement from outside conductor to outermost extent of buildings and projections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and grading plan (Sheet 11) show building footprints and overhead line locations but contain no dimension lines extending from conductor location to building faces. No enlarged plan details with clearance dimensions were found.","reasoning":"Dimensioned section and plan exhibits are mandatory to demonstrate compliance with clearance requirements. Their absence constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Fences along property boundaries and site perimeter"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are proposed on site plan, and overhead electric lines exist. However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that fences maintain the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Proposed site plan shows wooden privacy fences and other fencing elements near overhead utility lines, but no dimension annotations showing clearance distances from outside conductor to fence tops or faces.","reasoning":"Without dimensional evidence showing clearances from outside conductor, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence post locations relative to existing utility poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing utility poles are shown on the existing conditions survey. Proposed fences are shown on site plan. However, no dimension annotations show the horizontal clearance distance from fence post locations to existing electric poles. Code requires minimum 10-foot clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions show utility poles; site plan shows proposed fence locations. However, specific distances between fence posts and pole centerlines are not dimensioned on either sheet.","reasoning":"Without dimensional evidence, the 10-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls located near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are shown on grading and wall plan sheets. Overhead electric lines are shown on existing conditions and site plan. However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that retaining walls maintain the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outermost electric line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) and wall plan sheets (Sheets 38-39) show retaining wall locations. Overhead lines are confirmed on existing conditions. However, no dimensions are provided showing clearance distances from outside conductor to wall faces.","reasoning":"Without dimensional evidence from conductor to wall face, clearance compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls within potential clearance distance of overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section exhibits are provided for retaining walls (Sheets 38-39), but they do not include dimension annotations showing clearance distances from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of the walls. Code requires dimensioned section exhibits demonstrating clearance compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Wall plan sheets (38-39) contain section views of retaining walls but lack dimension lines extending from overhead conductor locations to wall faces. No clearance annotations are present on the sections.","reasoning":"Dimensioned section exhibits are mandatory. Their absence in the wall sections constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and parking areas potentially beneath or adjacent to overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways are proposed on the site plan, and overhead electric lines exist. However, no vertical clearance dimension annotations are provided showing the clearance from the lowest point of the overhead facilities to finished driveway grades. Code requires 16 feet minimum (parking without truck traffic) or 18 feet (areas with truck traffic). Mid-span clearance verification from registered surveyor is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows driveway alignments and spot elevations of finished grades. However, no overhead conductor elevations or vertical clearance dimensions are annotated. The grading plan does not show conductor height data needed to verify vertical clearances.","reasoning":"Without conductor elevation data and vertical clearance dimensions, the minimum 16-18 foot clearance requirement cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle parking areas beneath or adjacent to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vehicle parking areas are proposed on site plan, and overhead electric lines are present. However, no vertical clearance dimension annotations are shown from the lowest point of overhead facilities to parking areas. Code requires compliance with clearance requirements (minimum 12-18 feet depending on use).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking layout and overhead electric line routing, but no vertical clearance dimensions are provided. Conductor elevations and parking area heights are not dimensioned together.","reasoning":"Without vertical clearance dimensions, compliance with parking clearance requirements cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and site features in proximity to existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing electric poles are shown on existing conditions survey. Proposed driveways are shown on site plan. However, no dimension annotations demonstrate the horizontal distance from driveway edges to existing poles, and no notes indicate whether poles will be relocated minimum 30 feet from driveway edges.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions (Sheet 4) show utility poles; site plan (Sheet 9) shows driveway routing. However, specific clearance distances or relocation notes are not provided.","reasoning":"Without dimensional evidence of clearance or explicit relocation notes, the 30-foot setback requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All site features and overhead electric facilities where clearances apply"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines and utility poles are shown on the site plan, but NO clearance dimensions are annotated on any sheets (site plan, grading plan, or other exhibits). When clearance dimensions are eventually provided, they must be measured from the outside conductor, not from pole centerline or pole structure. Code requires dimensions originating from conductor location.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of sheets 4, 9, 11, and others confirms overhead electric facilities are depicted, but no dimension lines or annotations showing clearance distances appear anywhere on the submitted plans. Additionally, there is no indication that future dimensions will be measured from conductor rather than pole.","reasoning":"The complete absence of clearance dimensions is a deficiency. Additionally, without explicit notation that measurements will be from outside conductor, there is risk that future submissions will measure from pole centerline, which is incorrect.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosure and receptacle locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash enclosure locations are shown on site plan. Overhead electric lines are present. However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that trash enclosures maintain the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance considering trash bin raised height during service.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows trash enclosure locations and overhead electric line routing, but no vertical clearance dimensions are provided from conductor to trash bin raised height.","reasoning":"Without dimensional evidence, the clearance requirement for raised trash bins cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings, structures, and site features within or beneath existing overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution facilities are shown on site plan. While buildings appear positioned away from direct conflict based on visual spacing, the lack of surveyed conductor locations and explicit dimensional evidence means that compliance with the absolute prohibition against installing customer facilities under or over overhead distribution facilities cannot be conclusively verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines at property perimeter and buildings in interior, suggesting visual avoidance of conflict. However, without surveyed conductor locations and dimension lines, the exact spatial relationship cannot be definitively established.","reasoning":"Code prohibits customer facilities under/over distribution facilities regardless of clearance. Without surveyed data and dimensions, this prohibition cannot be affirmatively verified as met.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations relative to overhead electric service drops"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21). However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that water meters maintain the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric service-drop conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows water meter locations on utility plan, but no clearance dimensions from overhead service drops (if present) to meter locations are provided. The presence and routing of overhead service drops relative to meters is not clearly dimensioned.","reasoning":"Without dimensional evidence of clearance from service drops to water meters, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing beneath or adjacent to overhead electrical distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on utility plans. Overhead distribution lines are shown on site plan. However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that water lines maintain required clearances from overhead distribution facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan shows water line routing and overhead electric line presence, but no dimension annotations show clearance distances between them.","reasoning":"Without dimensional evidence, clearance compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Building foundations within 5 feet of property line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building foundations are shown on site plan, some within or near 5-foot distance from property lines where electric facilities may be required in adjacent ROW or property. However, no dimension annotations show the clearance space from property line to building foundation to verify that adequate room exists for necessary electric facility maintenance and access.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building setbacks from property lines and the presence of easements, but specific dimensions from property line to building foundation face are not clearly annotated in all locations.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimensional verification showing adequate clearance space for utility facility access, the requirement cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All site features where overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No registered surveyor data showing pole locations and mid-span clearances is provided in the site plan package. Code requires surveyor-certified mid-span clearance verification when existing overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 16-18 feet for driveways). Without this data, vertical clearances cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all 39 sheets revealed no mid-span clearance survey data or registered surveyor certification of pole locations and conductor elevations for vertical clearance verification.","reasoning":"Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is a mandatory requirement when vertical clearances are at issue. Its absence is a deficiency.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line crossings of Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines cross Valley View Road at the site property boundary. However, no angle dimension annotation demonstrates that the crossing is oriented at 90-degree angle to the road centerline as required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines are shown running north-south along Valley View Road, and the road runs east-west, visually suggesting approximately 90-degree crossing. However, no angle dimension or notation confirms the 90-degree orientation requirement is met.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimensional evidence of crossing angle, the 90-degree requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas along southern and western property boundaries adjacent to overhead distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) within what appears to be 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors based on visual spacing and symbol overlap. However, the specific species of these proposed trees are not identified on the landscape plan. Tree species verification against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible trees list (generally mature height ≤20 feet) cannot be performed without this information.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols (circles) positioned very close to or overlapping with the OHE line annotation along the southern property boundary. However, no plant schedule with species names is provided on Sheet 31 itself. Trees are coded as 'M' (mitigation), 'SY' (street yard), 'PL' (parking lot), and 'P' (buffer) but species are not listed.","reasoning":"Code requires that trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors be from the Utility Compatible list with mature height ≤20 feet. Without species identification, this requirement cannot be verified from the submitted landscape plan.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations and meter equipment clearances"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Meter locations are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21). However, no detailed site plan or meter area enlargement is provided showing working clearances around meter locations. Code requires 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9, free of obstructions including fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, and building projections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows meter locations on the overall site plan but does not provide enlarged meter details with required clearance dimensions and obstruction callouts.","reasoning":"Detailed meter clearance plans showing required working space dimensions and freedom from obstructions are necessary to verify compliance. Their absence means meter clearance compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy wire locations from existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows down guy wires (e.g., AT&T pole with guy wire shown). However, proposed site plan does not clearly depict existing down guy wire locations, and there are no notes indicating whether conflicts with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or site features have been identified and resolved through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions show guy wires present at poles. However, proposed site plan does not clearly show down guy anchor locations, and no conflict resolution notes are provided. The grouping description notes that electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans, which may be the case here.","reasoning":"Without clarity on down guy anchor locations and explicit notes addressing conflicts and resolution, the conflict resolution requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor points from existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchors are visible on existing conditions survey (utilities shown with guy wires). However, no down guy anchor easements are depicted on the easement exhibits or site plan. Code requires dedicated easements 10 feet wide extending 5 feet past where down guy enters the ground. Without easement depiction, the requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing conditions show guy wires and anchors, but reviewed easement depictions and site plans do not show dedicated down guy anchor easements with the required dimensions.","reasoning":"Down guy anchor easements must be explicitly shown on easement exhibits with proper dimensions (10-foot width, 5-foot extension). Their absence or unclear depiction means the requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platforms"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on and adjacent to the site. Construction activities are proposed. However, no construction staging plan, site logistics plan, or phasing plan is provided in the submitted site plan package showing construction staging area boundaries, crane swing radius, or material storage locations relative to overhead electric lines. Code requires 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines for construction activities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The submitted site plan sheets (39 total) include site plan, grading, and utility information but do not include a separate construction staging plan, site logistics plan, or equipment operation zone plan with clearances from overhead lines.","reasoning":"Construction staging plans are necessary to verify the 10-foot radial clearance requirement for construction equipment and activities. Their absence means this requirement cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet and general notes for construction phase notifications"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on site and construction activities are proposed. However, no note is provided on the cover sheet or general notes requiring that the owner/contractor notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of Sheet 1 (cover sheet) blocks 1-33 and Sheet 3 (general notes) blocks 1-18 reveals multiple regulatory notes but no reference to the 48-hour notification requirement for work near high-voltage lines. The Site Plan Release Notes on Sheet 3 mention utility provider responsibilities but not the notification requirement.","reasoning":"The 48-hour notification note is a mandatory requirement when overhead lines are present and construction is proposed. Its complete absence from the plans is a clear deficiency.","tools_used":[]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4476681c-aa5e-420f-bcfe-9f06ce103f91","uuid":"03776cca-5c34-488c-b1f9-a4840353e5a5"}
