{"level":30,"time":1778188914371,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR252MKBMK0H8E4X4ABVFAJ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the electrical infrastructure, landscape plan, plant schedule, and project specifications, I can now compile my findings. Let me document the results:\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**Electrical Infrastructure Present:**\n- Overhead Electric (OHE) line running along western and southern property boundaries\n- Utility poles on western boundary (3 visible per electrical plan)\n- 4 Electrical Transformer Pads (2 west side, 2 east side)\n- Underground electric lines throughout site with pull boxes\n- Sheet 3 confirms transmission infrastructure with specific clearance requirements (25 feet from transmission structures; 10 feet tree pruning responsibility)\n\n**Proposed Trees:**\n- 40+ tree symbols shown on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)\n- Species identified: Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud (per Sheet 35 plant schedule)\n- Trees concentrated along perimeters and parking islands\n- Vision analysis confirms trees along western boundary and southern boundary near OHE line\n\n**Critical Documentation Gaps:**\n- No ECM Appendix F reference to determine utility-compatible (UC) designation for proposed species\n- No mature height specifications per ECM Appendix F\n- No clearance dimensions shown on landscape plan\n- No root barrier details shown\n- No Austin Energy approval letters referenced\n- Plant species NOT identified on landscape plan symbols (only on separate Sheet 35)\n- No large tree (40+ feet) differentiation on landscape plan"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f00b2f4f-4bf8-4369-b6e1-683efc1760e1","uuid":"d95ea926-bc7a-4be0-9568-50e9676002a2"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188914877,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2530S1V5B6H43C15NBN1D9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The measure-distance tool is having issues with the documentId. Looking back at the README, the document ID is provided as: \"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777\" which appears to be correct. However, the tool is unable to resolve the plan_set_version.\n\nLet me try a different approach - I'll look at the blocks.md for Sheet 19 to get more detailed information about the utility routing that might help me assess the clearance situation without the tool.\n\nActually, given the issues with the measure tool, let me proceed with my analysis based on what I've found from the vision tools. The vision analysis was quite clear about \"directly adjacent\" and \"very close proximity\" which are terms indicating potential violations. However, \"directly adjacent\" doesn't necessarily mean less than 5 feet - it could mean 3 feet, 2 feet, or could even be satisfactory. I need to be careful about marking this as fail without actual measurements.\n\nLet me read the blocks.md for Sheet 19 to see if there's more specific routing information.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d58ee498-dfec-48cc-9e17-589e166908f5","uuid":"552f4e0e-6d32-42be-9142-52ce56b01166"}
