{"level":30,"time":1778188915556,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VSrZwHT9HgrD41hUxb4kqd","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 19 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — A legend explaining the symbols and line types used in the site plan diagram for various utilities.\n     4→\n     5→### Legend\n     6→| Symbol | Description |\n     7→| :--- | :--- |\n     8→| W | Existing Water Line |\n     9→| W | Proposed Water Line |\n    10→| [Solid Square Symbol] | Single Water Service |\n    11→| [Split Square Symbol] | Double Water Service |\n    12→| WW | Existing Wastewater Line |\n    13→| WW | Proposed Wastewater Line |\n    14→| [Dashed Line] | Wastewater Service |\n    15→| RW | Existing Reclaimed Water Line |\n    16→| RW | Proposed Reclaimed Water Line |\n    17→| E | Proposed Underground Electric |\n    18→| SD | Proposed Storm Drain |\n    19→| [FH Symbol] | Fire Hydrant |\n    20→| [Valve Symbol] | Gate Valve |\n    21→| [AARV Symbol] | AARV |\n    22→| [T Symbol] | Transformer Pad |\n    23→\n    24→## Block 2: drawing — The main diagram showing the layout of the townhomes, including buildings, units, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain), fire hydrants, cleanouts, and other site features. It includes numerous annotations and specific measurements for the utility infrastructure.\n    25→\n    26→[Detailed diagram showing the layout of multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each containing multiple units. The diagram includes extensive utility routing with lines for water (W), wastewater (WW), and storm drain (SD). There are numerous callouts for specific components like '6\" Cleanout Traffic Bearing', 'Air Spade Trench', 'Duplex Grinder Pump Lift Station', 'Fire Demand Meter', and 'PVC Wastewater Service Line'. Topographic lines and elevations are also visible. Various easements and setbacks are marked. The layout is bounded by 'Valley View Road' to the west.]\n    27→\n    28→## Block 3: notes — The legal description of the property.\n    29→\n    30→### Legal Description\n    31→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    32→\n    33→## Block 4: notes — A note detailing the requirements for restraining joints on water line components.\n    34→\n    35→### Restrained Joints for all Water Line Bends, Tees, Gate Valves & Ends\n    36→All horizontal and vertical water line bends, tee's, gate valves and dead end's shall be restrained to the water main using factory restrained joint pipe as approved in SPL WW-27F, or, mechanical joint restraint devices as approved in SPL WW-27A.\n    37→\n    38→## Block 5: notes — A disclaimer regarding the accuracy of existing utility locations shown on the plans, requiring the contractor to field verify.\n    39→\n    40→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    41→\n    42→## Block 6: notes — A brief note directing the reader to the landscape plan sheet for the tree list.\n    43→\n    44→### Tree List\n    45→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    46→\n    47→## Block 7: notes — A table listing the Drainage Fixture Units (DFU's) for each building, broken down by building type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex).\n    48→\n    49→### Drainage Fixture Unit Table\n    50→| Building # | Building Type | DFU's |\n    51→| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n    52→| 1 | 4Plex | 136 |\n    53→| 2 | 6Plex | 204 |\n    54→| 3 | 5Plex | 170 |\n    55→| 4 | 5Plex | 170 |\n    56→| 5 | 4Plex | 136 |\n    57→| 6 | 4Plex | 136 |\n    58→| 7 | 5Plex | 170 |\n    59→| 8 | 6Plex | 204 |\n    60→\n    61→## Block 8: notes — A note indicating the requirement for a pressure reducing valve for lots/structures with high water pressure.\n    62→\n    63→### PRV Note\n    64→Lots/Structure with 65 psi or greater require a pressure reducing valve, set at 65 psi, to be installed on the property owner's side of the right of way.\n    65→\n    66→## Block 9: notes\n    67→\n    68→## Block 11: table — The logo and contact information for Bleyl Engineering, the firm responsible for the planning, design, and management of the project.\n    69→\n    70→### Bleyl Engineering\n    71→Planning • Design • Management\n    72→7701 San Felipe Blvd., Suite 200, Austin TX 78729\n    73→Texas Firm Registration No. F-678\n    74→Tel. 512-454-2400\n    75→www.bleylengineering.com\n    76→\n    77→Austin | Bryan | Conroe | Houston\n    78→\n    79→## Block 12: table — A note regarding the requirements for private fire hydrants, including compliance with the Austin Fire Code and annual maintenance.\n    80→\n    81→### City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division\n    82→(512) 972-1060\n    83→This project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin Fire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of this obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced, maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project includes __1__ private hydrants.\n    84→\n    85→## Block 13: text_block\n    86→\n    87→## Block 14: text_block — A disclaimer regarding the verification of data and calculations, stating the engineer's responsibility.\n    88→\n    89→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    90→\n    91→## Block 16: text_block — Information about the benchmarks used for the project, including elevation and location details.\n    92→\n    93→### Benchmarks\n    94→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    95→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    96→\n    97→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    98→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    99→\n   100→## Block 19: text_block — A list of utility notes instructing the contractor to verify existing utility locations, notify the engineer of conflicts, and specifying pipe materials for private domestic water and wastewater branches.\n   101→\n   102→### Utility Notes\n   103→1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n   104→2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n   105→3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tubing. See Detail 520-AW-01B\n   106→4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the buildings are to be 6\" PVC @ 2.0% min. See Detail 520-AW-01C\n   107→\n   108→## Block 20: text_block — A general note stating that the project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule and requires inspection by a geologist for trenches deeper than 5 feet.\n   109→\n   110→### Note\n   111→This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n   112→\n   113→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d58ee498-dfec-48cc-9e17-589e166908f5","uuid":"2fd42d41-5b5f-4200-8a5c-a0e26d5ad873","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-19/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 19 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — A legend explaining the symbols and line types used in the site plan diagram for various utilities.\n\n### Legend\n| Symbol | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| W | Existing Water Line |\n| W | Proposed Water Line |\n| [Solid Square Symbol] | Single Water Service |\n| [Split Square Symbol] | Double Water Service |\n| WW | Existing Wastewater Line |\n| WW | Proposed Wastewater Line |\n| [Dashed Line] | Wastewater Service |\n| RW | Existing Reclaimed Water Line |\n| RW | Proposed Reclaimed Water Line |\n| E | Proposed Underground Electric |\n| SD | Proposed Storm Drain |\n| [FH Symbol] | Fire Hydrant |\n| [Valve Symbol] | Gate Valve |\n| [AARV Symbol] | AARV |\n| [T Symbol] | Transformer Pad |\n\n## Block 2: drawing — The main diagram showing the layout of the townhomes, including buildings, units, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain), fire hydrants, cleanouts, and other site features. It includes numerous annotations and specific measurements for the utility infrastructure.\n\n[Detailed diagram showing the layout of multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each containing multiple units. The diagram includes extensive utility routing with lines for water (W), wastewater (WW), and storm drain (SD). There are numerous callouts for specific components like '6\" Cleanout Traffic Bearing', 'Air Spade Trench', 'Duplex Grinder Pump Lift Station', 'Fire Demand Meter', and 'PVC Wastewater Service Line'. Topographic lines and elevations are also visible. Various easements and setbacks are marked. The layout is bounded by 'Valley View Road' to the west.]\n\n## Block 3: notes — The legal description of the property.\n\n### Legal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 4: notes — A note detailing the requirements for restraining joints on water line components.\n\n### Restrained Joints for all Water Line Bends, Tees, Gate Valves & Ends\nAll horizontal and vertical water line bends, tee's, gate valves and dead end's shall be restrained to the water main using factory restrained joint pipe as approved in SPL WW-27F, or, mechanical joint restraint devices as approved in SPL WW-27A.\n\n## Block 5: notes — A disclaimer regarding the accuracy of existing utility locations shown on the plans, requiring the contractor to field verify.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 6: notes — A brief note directing the reader to the landscape plan sheet for the tree list.\n\n### Tree List\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n## Block 7: notes — A table listing the Drainage Fixture Units (DFU's) for each building, broken down by building type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex).\n\n### Drainage Fixture Unit Table\n| Building # | Building Type | DFU's |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | 4Plex | 136 |\n| 2 | 6Plex | 204 |\n| 3 | 5Plex | 170 |\n| 4 | 5Plex | 170 |\n| 5 | 4Plex | 136 |\n| 6 | 4Plex | 136 |\n| 7 | 5Plex | 170 |\n| 8 | 6Plex | 204 |\n\n## Block 8: notes — A note indicating the requirement for a pressure reducing valve for lots/structures with high water pressure.\n\n### PRV Note\nLots/Structure with 65 psi or greater require a pressure reducing valve, set at 65 psi, to be installed on the property owner's side of the right of way.\n\n## Block 9: notes\n\n## Block 11: table — The logo and contact information for Bleyl Engineering, the firm responsible for the planning, design, and management of the project.\n\n### Bleyl Engineering\nPlanning • Design • Management\n7701 San Felipe Blvd., Suite 200, Austin TX 78729\nTexas Firm Registration No. F-678\nTel. 512-454-2400\nwww.bleylengineering.com\n\nAustin | Bryan | Conroe | Houston\n\n## Block 12: table — A note regarding the requirements for private fire hydrants, including compliance with the Austin Fire Code and annual maintenance.\n\n### City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division\n(512) 972-1060\nThis project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin Fire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of this obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced, maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project includes __1__ private hydrants.\n\n## Block 13: text_block\n\n## Block 14: text_block — A disclaimer regarding the verification of data and calculations, stating the engineer's responsibility.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\n## Block 16: text_block — Information about the benchmarks used for the project, including elevation and location details.\n\n### Benchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 19: text_block — A list of utility notes instructing the contractor to verify existing utility locations, notify the engineer of conflicts, and specifying pipe materials for private domestic water and wastewater branches.\n\n### Utility Notes\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tubing. See Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the buildings are to be 6\" PVC @ 2.0% min. See Detail 520-AW-01C\n\n## Block 20: text_block — A general note stating that the project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule and requires inspection by a geologist for trenches deeper than 5 feet.\n\n### Note\nThis project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n\n","numLines":113,"startLine":1,"totalLines":113}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778188915797,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2503QVJMWGPYE94H19CA6V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SM7mYo41aug5GF9WAFGrXv","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations on site (4 pads identified)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pad locations but provides no dimension lines or callout notes showing clearance distances from any transformer pad to adjacent buildings. No detail references or specifications provided. Minimum 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified from submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) depicts four transformer pads via dashed rectangular outlines with leader lines labeled 'Electrical Transformer Pad.' Vision analysis confirmed no dimension lines, callout notes, or detail references appear near any of the four pad locations.","reasoning":"Although transformer pads are clearly located and labeled on Sheet 21, the absence of dimensional clearances from the pads to building walls prevents verification of compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement. The burden of proof is on the applicant to provide dimensioned drawings showing required clearances.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if reduced clearances are proposed)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any sheets. Therefore, it cannot be determined whether reduced 3-foot clearances (to brick/masonry buildings) were proposed, or whether the conditions for the reduction exception (not in confined space, 10 ft+ to windows/doors/ducts, 15 ft+ vertical clearance, 3-hour fire rating) were met. If reduced clearances were intended, evidence of Austin Energy Design written approval is not present in submitted documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision examination of Sheet 21 found no dimension lines indicating any clearance distances (whether standard 5 feet or reduced 3 feet) from transformer pads to buildings. No architectural fire rating specifications appear in the submitted plans.","reasoning":"This item is conditional on whether reduced clearances are proposed. Since no clearances of any magnitude are dimensioned on the plans, the applicability condition cannot be confirmed. Additionally, no Austin Energy Design written approval documentation for reduced clearances appears in the supplementary documents reviewed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if balconies or overhangs are present above or adjacent)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The site plan shows building footprints and transformer pad locations, but no vertical elevations or cross-sections are provided for the transformer pad areas showing whether balconies or building overhangs exist above or adjacent to any pad. Additionally, no dimension lines show clearance distances. Compliance cannot be verified from available evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site Plan (Sheet 9) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) are plan-view drawings showing horizontal layout only. No building elevation sheets or cross-section details for transformer pad areas were located in the primary site plan sheets (1-39).","reasoning":"To verify this requirement, building elevations or cross-sections showing the vertical relationship between transformer pads and overhangs/balconies would be necessary. The absence of these drawings prevents assessment of whether overhangs exist and, if so, whether 5-foot lateral clearance is maintained.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if windows, doors, or ventilating ducts are present with inadequate separation)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets showing window/door/duct locations relative to transformer pads were provided. No dimension lines show clearance distances from pads to windows, doors, or ventilating ducts. Specification of transformer equipment as oil-filled or dry-type was not provided. Compliance with the 12-foot horizontal clearance requirement for oil-filled equipment with inadequate lateral separation cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan sheets are plan-view only and do not show window/door/duct elevations. No elevation drawings or architectural details depicting building façades near transformer pads were found in the plan set.","reasoning":"Assessment requires both elevation information (window/door/duct locations) and transformer specification (oil-filled vs. dry-type) and dimensional clearances, none of which are documented on the submitted sheets.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if sidewalks are adjacent to transformer pads)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows sidewalk locations and transformer pad locations, but no dimension lines measure the distance from transformer pad edges to back of sidewalks. The 2-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified from dimensioned evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The vision analysis of Sheet 21 confirmed no dimension lines appear between transformer pads and adjacent sidewalk edges.","reasoning":"Although sidewalks are shown near some transformer pad locations, the absence of dimensioned clearances prevents verification that the 2-foot minimum distance is maintained.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows no fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes. No such features appear on the buildings. Requirement to maintain 20-foot clearance from oil-filled equipment is not applicable as the triggering condition (fire escapes/stairs serving as fire exits) is not present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) confirmed no features labeled as fire escapes, emergency exit stairs, or structures designated as fire exits.","reasoning":"This item is conditional. The presence of fire escapes or emergency exit stairs serving as fire escapes triggers the requirement. Vision analysis found no such structures on the submitted plans, so this item may not be applicable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations (4 pads identified)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not indicate which side of each pad is the access door. No dimension lines show clearance distances from the access door side to open areas or adjacent buildings. The 10-foot hot-stick use area clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis found that transformer pads on Sheet 21 are shown as dashed rectangular outlines with no directional indicators, access door markers, or dimension lines showing clearances to open areas or structures.","reasoning":"Compliance with this requirement requires identifying which side of the transformer pad houses the access door, then verifying the 10-foot clearance in that direction. The submitted plans do not provide this information.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if in confined space such as niche, vault, or notched-out building area)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings or elevation views showing whether any transformer pads are located in niches, vaults, or enclosed areas were provided. No documentation of 35-foot vertical clearance inside niche and niche entrance if applicable. Confined space configuration cannot be verified from submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan-view sheets (Sheets 9, 21) do not depict vertical relationships. No cross-section or elevation sheets showing building profiles with transformer locations were identified in the plan set.","reasoning":"Determining whether a transformer faces a confined space requires cross-section analysis, which is not provided for any transformer pad location.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["fire hydrant locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan does not identify transformer pad locations relative to the fire hydrants shown. No dimension lines measure distances between transformer pads and fire hydrants. The 5-foot minimum clearance from fire hydrants cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows fire hydrant locations. Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations. No dimension lines appear on either sheet measuring distances between these features. Vision analysis confirmed no callouts or notes relating fire hydrant clearances to transformer equipment.","reasoning":"Although both features are shown on respective plan sheets, the absence of dimensioned distances prevents verification of the 5-foot clearance requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows no dumpsters or waste collection enclosures on the property. This requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Site Plan (Sheet 9) and cross-reference with Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) revealed no dumpster enclosures or waste containers shown anywhere on the site.","reasoning":"This item is conditional on the presence of dumpsters. Since no dumpsters are depicted on the plans, the requirement to maintain 5-foot clearance does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["parking and common areas (only if bike racks are present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and landscape plan show bicycle parking locations. No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pad locations to any bicycle parking areas. The 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) both reference bicycle parking with callouts showing 'Bicycle Parking' symbols and counts. However, no dimension lines measure distances from transformer pads to these bicycle parking locations.","reasoning":"While bicycle racks are present on the site, the absence of dimensioned distances between transformer pads and bike racks prevents verification of the 5-foot clearance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["site areas with light poles and transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not clearly identify all light pole locations or show dimension lines measuring distances between light poles and transformer pads. The 5-foot minimum clearance from light poles cannot be verified from available evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) focuses on electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, meters) but does not include lighting fixture callouts. Photometric or site lighting details were not located in the primary site plan sheets reviewed.","reasoning":"Without identification of light pole locations and dimensioned clearances, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["fire lanes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan shows fire lanes with dimensions, but no dimension lines measure distances from transformer pad locations to the fire lane boundaries. The 15-foot minimum clearance from fire lanes cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows fire lane boundaries labeled 'Fire Lane' with width dimensions (26', 24'). Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads. Vision analysis found no dimension lines on either sheet connecting transformer pads to fire lane edges.","reasoning":"Although fire lanes are clearly marked and dimensioned on Sheet 10, the absence of dimensions showing distances from transformer pads prevents verification of the 15-foot clearance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pads, but no dimension lines measure distances between any pair of pads. The 5-foot minimum clearance between transformer pads cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 confirmed four distinct transformer pads are labeled 'Electrical Transformer Pad' but no dimension lines appear between them.","reasoning":"With four transformer pads shown, verification of the 5-foot inter-pad clearance requires dimensioned evidence, which is not provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and water lines on the site, but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances from transformer pads to water lines. The 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from water lines cannot be verified from available evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) and Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) both show utility routing, but vision analysis confirmed no dimension lines on Sheet 21 measuring distances between transformer pads and water lines.","reasoning":"Compliance verification requires dimensioned clearances between transformer pads and water infrastructure, which are not provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and wastewater lines on the site, but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances from transformer pads to wastewater lines. The 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from wastewater lines cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) and Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) show both transformer pads and wastewater routing, but vision analysis found no dimensioned clearances between these features.","reasoning":"Compliance requires documented horizontal separations between transformer pads and wastewater infrastructure, which are absent from submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations and Sheet 12 shows storm drain routing on the site, but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances from transformer pads to storm drain lines. The 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from storm drains cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads. Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12) shows drainage infrastructure. Vision analysis found no dimension lines on electrical sheets measuring distances between transformer pads and storm drain lines.","reasoning":"Compliance requires documented horizontal separations between transformer pads and storm drainage, not provided in submitted evidence.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and underground utility lines, but no dimension lines measure the 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities. Compliance with UCM § 1.10.5.A separation requirements cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads and the general routing of underground electric lines and other utilities, but vision analysis confirmed no dimension lines providing specific clearances between the transformer pads and adjacent underground infrastructure.","reasoning":"The 12-inch minimum separation (OD to OD) requires precise dimensioning that is not provided on the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and underground utility routing. No cross-section drawings or elevation views confirm whether transformer pads or Austin Energy underground facilities are located over or under other utility lines, or whether customer structures are installed over AE underground facilities. Compliance cannot be verified from available evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan-view sheets do not show vertical relationships between utilities. No cross-section or profile sheets for utility zones containing transformer pads were identified.","reasoning":"Verification of this requirement requires vertical section drawings showing utility layering at transformer pad locations, which are not provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["areas with overhead electric distribution lines (none identified adjacent to transformer pads)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines labeled 'OHE' along property boundaries, but no transformer pads appear to be located under or directly adjacent to these lines. No 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance dimension lines are shown. If transformer pads are positioned within the 7.5-foot clearance area, this would require verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 9 showed overhead electric (OHE) lines running along southern and eastern property boundaries. Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) showed transformer pads at interior and western locations. The spatial relationship between OHE lines and transformer pads appears separated, but without dimension lines, exact proximity cannot be confirmed.","reasoning":"If overhead lines do pass near any transformer pad location, the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance (extending from ground to sky) would require dimensioned verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["areas with overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors (none clearly identified adjacent to transformer pads)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines at property boundaries. No dimension lines show distances from transformer pad locations to overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors. The 15-foot radius clearance requirement (measured from conductors) cannot be verified from submitted evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines are shown on site plans as 'OHE' labels, but specific identification of primary vs. neutral vs. secondary conductors is not provided on the submitted electrical plan. No radii or dimension lines measure distances from transformer pads to overhead conductor locations.","reasoning":"Compliance verification requires both identification of primary/neutral conductor locations and dimensioned radii from those conductors to transformer pads, neither of which are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if located in niche, enclosed area, or notched-out building configuration)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances inside niches or enclosed transformer access areas were provided. No niche configuration details or 35-foot clearance documentation exists in submitted plans. If any transformer is located in a niche (accessible from outside but within building footprint), this cannot be verified from available evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan-view sheets show transformer pads at ground level but do not indicate whether any pad is within a niche configuration. No vertical section drawings show clearance heights inside access areas.","reasoning":"Niche service verification requires cross-section analysis demonstrating 35-foot vertical clearance from grade through entire access path, not provided in plan set.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if located in niche service configuration)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service is identified on submitted plans. No documentation of 3-hour fire wall rating, ventilation specifications, or Austin Energy Design business unit consultation appears in any sheet or supplementary document. If a niche service configuration is proposed, required fire rating and ventilation specifications are not demonstrated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis found no indication on Sheet 21 or associated documents that any transformer is located in a niche (accessible from outside but within building footprint). No architectural specifications referencing fire ratings or AE Design niche consultation were identified.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to niche service installations. The absence of niche designation and specifications suggests this may not be applicable, but if niche service is intended, evidence of compliance is absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas above them"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas adjacent to or above transformer pad locations. If such vertical obstructions exist, required clearance documentation is missing.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Primary site plan sheets (9, 21) are plan-view only and do not show vertical clearances. No cross-section or profile sheets specifically addressing transformer access areas were identified.","reasoning":"Verification of vertical clearances from transformer access doors to overhead obstructions requires cross-section drawings, which are not provided in the submitted plan set.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["oil-filled transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type) are not documented on the electrical plan. Grading and drainage plans show contours but do not show surface flow direction relative to transformer pad locations, particularly whether drainage slopes toward or away from buildings. If oil-filled equipment is installed, proper grading to ensure liquid flow away from building cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis found no specification notes on Sheet 21 identifying transformers as oil-filled or dry-type. Grading Plan (Sheet 11) shows topographic contours but does not include annotations showing surface flow direction relative to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both transformer type identification and grading verification showing drainage away from buildings for oil-filled equipment. Neither element is clearly documented in submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows property lines and transformer pad locations. No dimension lines or callout notes specifically confirm that all transformer pads are located 100% on private property (not straddling property lines). Plat sheet shows property boundaries, but correlation to transformer pad positions requires explicit callouts not present on electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat (Sheet 2) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) both exist but contain separate information. Vision analysis of Sheet 21 found no dimension lines or notes confirming that transformer pads are entirely on private property.","reasoning":"Confirmation that transformer pads are placed entirely within private property (not on property lines or in right-of-way) would require explicit callouts or dimensions from pads to property lines, which are not provided on the electrical plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 (property requirement); easement-specific regulations"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plat and Site Plans show easement callouts (drainage, water, wastewater, electrical). No explicit notation confirms whether any transformer pad is located within prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines). No Austin Energy Design written approval for pad placement in easements is documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show easement labels on boundaries (e.g., '25' Drainage Easement', '5' Electrical Easement') and in property corners, but no callouts explicitly state whether transformer pad footprints fall within or outside these easement zones. No AE Design approvals for easement placement appear in supplementary documents.","reasoning":"Confirmation that transformer pads are not located in prohibited easements would require explicit callouts identifying pad placement relative to each easement boundary, not provided on submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (additional clearance and access easements may be required)"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Easement callouts appear on plat and site plan boundary areas (drainage, water, electrical), but no specific transformer pad easement callouts or dimensions are shown on the electrical plan. Easement width adequate for Austin Energy accessibility requirements cannot be verified from submitted evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat (Sheet 2) and Site Plan (Sheet 9) show existing easement callouts along property boundaries and in corners, but no callouts on the Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) identify transformer pad easements or specify their width for AE accessibility.","reasoning":"Compliance requires documented transformer pad easements with dimensions demonstrating adequacy for AE access equipment, not provided on electrical plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["electrical service routing from all transformer pads to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and meter locations connected by blue electrical lines, but no dimension lines or property line callouts confirm that the electrical routing from each transformer pad to its corresponding meter is 100% on private property and does not cross property lines or right-of-way areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 showed blue lines connecting transformers to meters, but no annotations confirm routing is entirely on private property.","reasoning":"Explicit callouts or dimension lines from transformer to meter routing relative to property lines would be required to confirm 100% private property placement, not provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0 (obtain transformer pad detail from AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations (4 pads identified)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pad locations but provides no dimensions (length x width). No reference callouts or detail reference bubbles direct readers to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets. No specification of service type (single-phase or three-phase) is provided. Required transformer pad dimensions and AE Design detail references matching the specified service type are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed that transformer pads on Sheet 21 are shown as dashed rectangular outlines without dimension callouts, detail reference numbers, or service type specifications. No AE Design pad detail sheets appear in the plan set.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.5.2.6 and § 1.18.0 require transformer pad specifications from AE Design matching the service type. The absence of dimensions, detail references, and service type documentation constitutes a failure to provide required information.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if within 4 feet of parking or vehicle routes)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows transformer pads and parking areas. Specific dimension lines measuring distances from each transformer pad to nearby parking spaces and drive aisles are not provided. No bollard details or protective barrier specifications are shown on the electrical plan or referenced in detail sheets. If any pad is located within 4 feet of parking/traffic areas, required 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal post specifications and spacing cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 showed transformer pads adjacent to parking areas and circulation routes, but no dimension lines measure specific distances from pads to parking spaces. No bollard callouts or protective barrier details appear on electrical or construction detail sheets.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both measurement confirming pad location within 4 feet of parking/traffic areas and bollard specification details, neither of which are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations and site structures relative to overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines along property boundaries and transformer locations. No cross-section drawings or vertical clearance documentation confirms that customer structures (buildings, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks) are not installed under Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. Vertical clearance verification is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan-view sheets show overhead electric lines ('OHE') at property boundaries and transformer pads at various site locations, but no vertical section drawings show the spatial relationship between structures and overhead conductors.","reasoning":"Verification that structures are not under overhead distribution requires cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances, not provided in submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if retaining walls are present and adjacent to pads)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows retaining walls around the property perimeter. Transformer pad locations are shown, but no dimension lines measure clearance distances from any transformer pad to adjacent retaining walls. The 5-foot minimum clearance from retaining walls cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site Plan (Sheet 9) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) both show retaining wall locations and transformer pads respectively, but vision analysis found no dimension lines connecting these features.","reasoning":"While retaining walls are present on site, absence of dimensioned clearances from transformer pads prevents verification of the 5-foot minimum requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if fences or gates are adjacent)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows wooden privacy fences around property perimeter and parking areas. No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pads to fence lines. No callouts identify which sides of transformer pads have operators/controls (requiring 5-foot clearance) versus sides without operators/controls (requiring 3-foot clearance). The required fence clearances cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site Plan (Sheet 9) shows fences marked with 'X' symbols along property lines and parking areas. Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads. Vision analysis found no dimension lines measuring distances between pads and fences, and no callouts identifying pad access door orientation.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both dimensioned fence clearances and identification of which pad side has operators/controls to determine whether 5-foot or 3-foot clearance applies. Neither is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if stairwells serving as fire exits are adjacent)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan identifies fire exit requirements. No stairwells are explicitly labeled on the site plan as serving fire exits. Dimension lines from transformer pads to any potential stairwell locations are not shown. The 5-foot minimum clearance from stairwells cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) found no features labeled as fire exit stairs or emergency exit structures. While buildings are shown with unit access, no specific stairwell callouts for fire egress appear.","reasoning":"This item is conditional on the presence of stairwells designated as fire exits. Since no such structures are explicitly identified, applicability cannot be confirmed, and clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["fire hydrant locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan shows 3 fire hydrant locations (1 existing, 2 proposed). No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pads to fire hydrants. The 5-foot minimum clearance from fire hydrants cannot be verified from submitted evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) clearly labels fire hydrant locations with dimensions to site features, but vision analysis found no dimension lines measuring distances from transformer pad locations (shown on Sheet 21) to fire hydrants.","reasoning":"Compliance verification requires dimensioned distances between transformer pads and fire hydrants across separate plan sheets, not provided in submitted evidence.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["areas with trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and Tree List (Sheet 32) identify proposed trees and plantings. Dimension lines from any trees to transformer pad locations are not provided. Tree species are listed, but verification that trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F 'UC' column cannot be confirmed without dimensioned clearances from trees to electrical equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows tree locations with species symbols (SY, PL, P, M). Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations. Vision analysis found no dimension lines measuring distances between trees and transformer pads. No cross-reference notes link tree species to ECM Appendix F utility-compatible designations.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both identification of trees within utility clearance zones (measured distances) and verification of species utility-compatibility (ECM Appendix F review). Without dimensioned distances, proximity cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscaped areas adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan shows plantings and shrubs around the site. No dimension lines measure clearance distances from transformer pads to shrubs or low-lying vegetation. The 10-foot clearance from the access door side and 5-foot clearance from other sides cannot be verified. Additionally, transformer pad access door orientation is not identified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) depicts vegetation distribution with H-series key notes (H.4 parking lot landscaping, H.5 common open space, etc.) but no dimension lines measure distances from transformer pads to shrub/vegetation locations. No callouts identify transformer access door orientation.","reasoning":"Compliance requires dimensioned clearances from transformer pads to vegetation and identification of which pad side is the access door (to determine 10-foot vs. 5-foot requirement). Neither is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["areas with trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan shows proposed trees and plantings. No dimension lines measure distances from trees to transformer pad locations or underground electric equipment. No root barrier details or specifications are shown on landscape or detail sheets. If trees are located within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment, required root barrier specifications (4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows tree plantings with species and sizing indicators, but vision analysis found no dimension lines measuring distances from trees to transformer pads or underground electric lines. No root barrier callouts appear on landscape or construction detail sheets.","reasoning":"Compliance requires measurement confirming trees are within the 20-foot zone and specification details for root barriers, neither provided on submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if gas service is present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not indicate whether gas infrastructure is present on the site or near transformer pads. Gas pressure specifications are not provided. No dimension lines show clearance distances between transformer pads and gas lines. The 24-inch minimum for low-pressure gas and 36-inch minimum for high-pressure gas (60 psi and over) cannot be verified without gas line identification and pressure confirmation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 found no callouts or labels identifying gas service lines on the electrical plan. No utility notes mention gas infrastructure. Supplementary documents reviewed do not reference gas service specifications.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both confirmation that gas infrastructure is present and dimensioned clearances showing required separation. Without these elements, the requirement's applicability and compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f2fc17a-22f3-4791-8627-5877b81951c5","uuid":"b205fc46-40e0-42ab-9bc6-6d080cacbda4"}
