Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if located in niche, enclosed area, or notched-out building configuration)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances inside niches or enclosed transformer access areas were provided. No niche configuration details or 35-foot clearance documentation exists in submitted plans. If any transformer is located in a niche (accessible from outside but within building footprint), this cannot be verified from available evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan-view sheets show transformer pads at ground level but do not indicate whether any pad is within a niche configuration. No vertical section drawings show clearance heights inside access areas.","reasoning":"Niche service verification requires cross-section analysis demonstrating 35-foot vertical clearance from grade through entire access path, not provided in plan set.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if located in niche service configuration)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service is identified on submitted plans. No documentation of 3-hour fire wall rating, ventilation specifications, or Austin Energy Design business unit consultation appears in any sheet or supplementary document. If a niche service configuration is proposed, required fire rating and ventilation specifications are not demonstrated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis found no indication on Sheet 21 or associated documents that any transformer is located in a niche (accessible from outside but within building footprint). No architectural specifications referencing fire ratings or AE Design niche consultation were identified.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to niche service installations. The absence of niche designation and specifications suggests this may not be applicable, but if niche service is intended, evidence of compliance is absent.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas above them"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas adjacent to or above transformer pad locations. If such vertical obstructions exist, required clearance documentation is missing.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Primary site plan sheets (9, 21) are plan-view only and do not show vertical clearances. No cross-section or profile sheets specifically addressing transformer access areas were identified.","reasoning":"Verification of vertical clearances from transformer access doors to overhead obstructions requires cross-section drawings, which are not provided in the submitted plan set.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["oil-filled transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type) are not documented on the electrical plan. Grading and drainage plans show contours but do not show surface flow direction relative to transformer pad locations, particularly whether drainage slopes toward or away from buildings. If oil-filled equipment is installed, proper grading to ensure liquid flow away from building cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis found no specification notes on Sheet 21 identifying transformers as oil-filled or dry-type. Grading Plan (Sheet 11) shows topographic contours but does not include annotations showing surface flow direction relative to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both transformer type identification and grading verification showing drainage away from buildings for oil-filled equipment. Neither element is clearly documented in submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows property lines and transformer pad locations. No dimension lines or callout notes specifically confirm that all transformer pads are located 100% on private property (not straddling property lines). Plat sheet shows property boundaries, but correlation to transformer pad positions requires explicit callouts not present on electrical plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat (Sheet 2) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) both exist but contain separate information. Vision analysis of Sheet 21 found no dimension lines or notes confirming that transformer pads are entirely on private property.","reasoning":"Confirmation that transformer pads are placed entirely within private property (not on property lines or in right-of-way) would require explicit callouts or dimensions from pads to property lines, which are not provided on the electrical plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 (property requirement); easement-specific regulations"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plat and Site Plans show easement callouts (drainage, water, wastewater, electrical). No explicit notation confirms whether any transformer pad is located within prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines). No Austin Energy Design written approval for pad placement in easements is documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show easement labels on boundaries (e.g., '25' Drainage Easement', '5' Electrical Easement') and in property corners, but no callouts explicitly state whether transformer pad footprints fall within or outside these easement zones. No AE Design approvals for easement placement appear in supplementary documents.","reasoning":"Confirmation that transformer pads are not located in prohibited easements would require explicit callouts identifying pad placement relative to each easement boundary, not provided on submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (additional clearance and access easements may be required)"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Easement callouts appear on plat and site plan boundary areas (drainage, water, electrical), but no specific transformer pad easement callouts or dimensions are shown on the electrical plan. Easement width adequate for Austin Energy accessibility requirements cannot be verified from submitted evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat (Sheet 2) and Site Plan (Sheet 9) show existing easement callouts along property boundaries and in corners, but no callouts on the Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) identify transformer pad easements or specify their width for AE accessibility.","reasoning":"Compliance requires documented transformer pad easements with dimensions demonstrating adequacy for AE access equipment, not provided on electrical plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["electrical service routing from all transformer pads to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and meter locations connected by blue electrical lines, but no dimension lines or property line callouts confirm that the electrical routing from each transformer pad to its corresponding meter is 100% on private property and does not cross property lines or right-of-way areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 showed blue lines connecting transformers to meters, but no annotations confirm routing is entirely on private property.","reasoning":"Explicit callouts or dimension lines from transformer to meter routing relative to property lines would be required to confirm 100% private property placement, not provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0 (obtain transformer pad detail from AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations (4 pads identified)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pad locations but provides no dimensions (length x width). No reference callouts or detail reference bubbles direct readers to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets. No specification of service type (single-phase or three-phase) is provided. Required transformer pad dimensions and AE Design detail references matching the specified service type are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed that transformer pads on Sheet 21 are shown as dashed rectangular outlines without dimension callouts, detail reference numbers, or service type specifications. No AE Design pad detail sheets appear in the plan set.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.5.2.6 and § 1.18.0 require transformer pad specifications from AE Design matching the service type. The absence of dimensions, detail references, and service type documentation constitutes a failure to provide required information.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if within 4 feet of parking or vehicle routes)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows transformer pads and parking areas. Specific dimension lines measuring distances from each transformer pad to nearby parking spaces and drive aisles are not provided. No bollard details or protective barrier specifications are shown on the electrical plan or referenced in detail sheets. If any pad is located within 4 feet of parking/traffic areas, required 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal post specifications and spacing cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 showed transformer pads adjacent to parking areas and circulation routes, but no dimension lines measure specific distances from pads to parking spaces. No bollard callouts or protective barrier details appear on electrical or construction detail sheets.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both measurement confirming pad location within 4 feet of parking/traffic areas and bollard specification details, neither of which are provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations and site structures relative to overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines along property boundaries and transformer locations. No cross-section drawings or vertical clearance documentation confirms that customer structures (buildings, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks) are not installed under Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. Vertical clearance verification is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan-view sheets show overhead electric lines ('OHE') at property boundaries and transformer pads at various site locations, but no vertical section drawings show the spatial relationship between structures and overhead conductors.","reasoning":"Verification that structures are not under overhead distribution requires cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances, not provided in submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if retaining walls are present and adjacent to pads)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows retaining walls around the property perimeter. Transformer pad locations are shown, but no dimension lines measure clearance distances from any transformer pad to adjacent retaining walls. The 5-foot minimum clearance from retaining walls cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site Plan (Sheet 9) and Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) both show retaining wall locations and transformer pads respectively, but vision analysis found no dimension lines connecting these features.","reasoning":"While retaining walls are present on site, absence of dimensioned clearances from transformer pads prevents verification of the 5-foot minimum requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if fences or gates are adjacent)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows wooden privacy fences around property perimeter and parking areas. No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pads to fence lines. No callouts identify which sides of transformer pads have operators/controls (requiring 5-foot clearance) versus sides without operators/controls (requiring 3-foot clearance). The required fence clearances cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site Plan (Sheet 9) shows fences marked with 'X' symbols along property lines and parking areas. Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads. Vision analysis found no dimension lines measuring distances between pads and fences, and no callouts identifying pad access door orientation.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both dimensioned fence clearances and identification of which pad side has operators/controls to determine whether 5-foot or 3-foot clearance applies. Neither is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if stairwells serving as fire exits are adjacent)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan identifies fire exit requirements. No stairwells are explicitly labeled on the site plan as serving fire exits. Dimension lines from transformer pads to any potential stairwell locations are not shown. The 5-foot minimum clearance from stairwells cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) found no features labeled as fire exit stairs or emergency exit structures. While buildings are shown with unit access, no specific stairwell callouts for fire egress appear.","reasoning":"This item is conditional on the presence of stairwells designated as fire exits. Since no such structures are explicitly identified, applicability cannot be confirmed, and clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["fire hydrant locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire Protection Plan shows 3 fire hydrant locations (1 existing, 2 proposed). No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pads to fire hydrants. The 5-foot minimum clearance from fire hydrants cannot be verified from submitted evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) clearly labels fire hydrant locations with dimensions to site features, but vision analysis found no dimension lines measuring distances from transformer pad locations (shown on Sheet 21) to fire hydrants.","reasoning":"Compliance verification requires dimensioned distances between transformer pads and fire hydrants across separate plan sheets, not provided in submitted evidence.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["areas with trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and Tree List (Sheet 32) identify proposed trees and plantings. Dimension lines from any trees to transformer pad locations are not provided. Tree species are listed, but verification that trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F 'UC' column cannot be confirmed without dimensioned clearances from trees to electrical equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows tree locations with species symbols (SY, PL, P, M). Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations. Vision analysis found no dimension lines measuring distances between trees and transformer pads. No cross-reference notes link tree species to ECM Appendix F utility-compatible designations.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both identification of trees within utility clearance zones (measured distances) and verification of species utility-compatibility (ECM Appendix F review). Without dimensioned distances, proximity cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscaped areas adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan shows plantings and shrubs around the site. No dimension lines measure clearance distances from transformer pads to shrubs or low-lying vegetation. The 10-foot clearance from the access door side and 5-foot clearance from other sides cannot be verified. Additionally, transformer pad access door orientation is not identified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) depicts vegetation distribution with H-series key notes (H.4 parking lot landscaping, H.5 common open space, etc.) but no dimension lines measure distances from transformer pads to shrub/vegetation locations. No callouts identify transformer access door orientation.","reasoning":"Compliance requires dimensioned clearances from transformer pads to vegetation and identification of which pad side is the access door (to determine 10-foot vs. 5-foot requirement). Neither is provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["areas with trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan shows proposed trees and plantings. No dimension lines measure distances from trees to transformer pad locations or underground electric equipment. No root barrier details or specifications are shown on landscape or detail sheets. If trees are located within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment, required root barrier specifications (4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows tree plantings with species and sizing indicators, but vision analysis found no dimension lines measuring distances from trees to transformer pads or underground electric lines. No root barrier callouts appear on landscape or construction detail sheets.","reasoning":"Compliance requires measurement confirming trees are within the 20-foot zone and specification details for root barriers, neither provided on submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations (only if gas service is present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not indicate whether gas infrastructure is present on the site or near transformer pads. Gas pressure specifications are not provided. No dimension lines show clearance distances between transformer pads and gas lines. The 24-inch minimum for low-pressure gas and 36-inch minimum for high-pressure gas (60 psi and over) cannot be verified without gas line identification and pressure confirmation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 found no callouts or labels identifying gas service lines on the electrical plan. No utility notes mention gas infrastructure. Supplementary documents reviewed do not reference gas service specifications.","reasoning":"Compliance requires both confirmation that gas infrastructure is present and dimensioned clearances showing required separation. Without these elements, the requirement's applicability and compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f94124c8-c797-46d1-b1dc-dc86b33fa112"}
