{"level":30,"time":1778188935015,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine this electrical design plan and identify:\n1. The exact locations of all transformers/pad-mounted electrical equipment on the site - note their location relative to buildings\n2. Any overhead electric lines or utility poles shown on this sheet\n3. The type of electrical infrastructure (is this distribution or transmission voltage?)\n4. Any callouts or notes about electrical clearances or tree restrictions\n\nThis is a preliminary electrical design plan. Please describe what you see regarding the placement of electrical equipment and any utility infrastructure that might conflict with tree planting.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here are the details regarding the electrical infrastructure and its placement:\n\n**1. Exact locations of all transformers/pad-mounted electrical equipment:**\nThe plan uses blue boxes to indicate pad-mounted electrical equipment, specifically labeled as \"Electrical Transformer Pad\", \"Electrical Pull Box\", and \"Electrical Meters\".\n\n*   **Transformers (\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"):**\n    *   One is located on the western edge of the site, south of the main entrance drive, situated west of Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 2.\n    *   One is located centrally between Bldg. 2 (to its north) and Bldg. 8 (to its south).\n    *   One is located between Bldg. 4 (to its west) and Bldg. 5 (to its east).\n    *   One is located between Bldg. 7 (to its west) and Bldg. 6 (to its east).\n*   **Pull Boxes (\"Electrical Pull Box\"):**\n    *   North of Bldg. 1, near the site entrance.\n    *   Northeast of Bldg. 3.\n    *   South of Bldg. 4.\n    *   South of Bldg. 8.\n    *   South of Bldg. 7.\n*   **Meters (\"Electrical Meters\"):** These are shown attached to or immediately adjacent to the building footprints (e.g., north side of Bldg. 1, north side of Bldg. 3, west side of Bldg. 4, west side of Bldg. 7, west side of Bldg. 8).\n\n**2. Overhead electric lines or utility poles:**\n*   There is an overhead electric line running north-south along the western boundary of the site (outside the main property line, along the street right-of-way). It is denoted by a dashed line labeled with **\"- OHE -\"**.\n*   There are utility poles indicated along this \"- OHE -\" line, represented by small circular symbols with lines passing through them. There is also a label pointing to a line entering the site from this western edge that reads **\"Underground Electric Line\"**, indicating the transition from overhead to underground infrastructure for the development.\n\n**3. Type of electrical infrastructure:**\n*   While the specific voltage is not labeled, the infrastructure shown is characteristic of standard residential **distribution**. It features an overhead line (\"- OHE -\") along the street that transitions to an \"Underground Electric Line\" network throughout the site, feeding into multiple pad-mounted transformers (\"Electrical Transformer Pad\") to step down power for the individual townhome buildings. It does not display the large easements or tower structures associated with transmission lines.\n\n**4. Callouts or notes about electrical clearances or tree restrictions:**\n*   **Clearances:** There are no explicit text callouts defining required numerical clearances (e.g., \"10 ft clearance required\") around the transformers on this specific sheet. However, there are faint dashed rectangular boxes drawn around each \"Electrical Transformer Pad\", which typically represent the required clear working space, though the dimensions are not provided here.\n*   **Tree Restrictions:** There are no specific notes detailing restrictions for planting near electrical equipment. There is a box labeled **\"Tree List\"** that states: *\"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"*\n\n**Placement of electrical equipment and potential conflicts with trees:**\nThe site is heavily populated with existing trees, indicated by large, scalloped circles representing their canopies and critical root zones. The proposed underground electrical routing (solid blue lines connecting the equipment) appears to have significant potential conflicts with these existing trees:\n*   The blue underground electrical lines are routed directly through the canopy/root zone circles of numerous existing trees across the site.\n*   For example, the line routing east from the transformer between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8 passes straight through the center of several large existing tree canopies located in the courtyard space between Bldg. 8, Bldg. 7, and Bldg. 4.\n*   The initial \"Underground Electric Line\" entering from the street (west side) routes very closely to and through the canopy circles of existing trees near the entrance.\n*   Any future tree planting (referencing sheet 32) would need to avoid the dashed clear zones around the four identified \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations and avoid planting large woody species directly over the extensive underground electrical trenching network shown in blue.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1420,"outputTokens":928,"totalTokens":4325,"reasoningTokens":1977},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this electrical design plan and identify:\n1. The exact locations of all transformers/pad-mounted electrical equipment on the site - note their location relative to buildings\n2. Any overhead electric lines or utility poles shown on this sheet\n3. The type of electrical infrastructure (is this distribution or transmission voltage?)\n4. Any callouts or notes about electrical clearances or tree restrictions\n\nThis is a preliminary electrical design plan. Please describe what you see regarding the placement of electrical equipment and any utility infrastructure that might conflict with tree planting."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-1UyTAOpmclH4e5t9EfPZkrvb","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-spec