4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission infrastructure referenced in Sheet 3 general notes with stricter 25-foot clearance requirement. Proposed tree species lack UC designation verification per ECM Appendix F. Actual lateral distances from transmission conductors cannot be precisely measured from submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 13 states 'No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.' Electrical plan shows OHE line on western property boundary. Landscape plan shows trees along western boundary. Vision analysis indicates 5-6 trees within approximately 10-30 feet of western facade.","reasoning":"Cannot determine if trees are within prohibited 25-foot zone without precise measurements and cannot verify UC status without ECM Appendix F. The applicability of this item is confirmed by presence of transmission structures, but compliance cannot be verified from submitted evidence.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant specifications on Sheet 35 show minimum purchase height (e.g., '16 HT MINIMUM' for Cedar Elm and Live Oak) but not mature height per ECM Appendix F. Cannot verify if proposed trees meet large tree definition (40+ feet mature height) needed to evaluate this restriction.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant list specifies minimum container specifications and heights (e.g., Cedar Elm 100 GAL., 4 CAL., 16 HT minimum). These are nursery purchase specifications, not mature growth heights. Grouping specifies mature height ≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F determines large tree classification.","reasoning":"Without ECM Appendix F mature height classifications for each species, cannot determine which proposed trees qualify as 'large.' The 16-foot minimum height is not the same as mature height. Cannot verify compliance.","tools_used":["Read","vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas within 50 lateral feet of overhead electric transmission conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mature height per ECM Appendix F cannot be determined from submitted plant specifications. Actual lateral distances from transmission structures cannot be precisely measured. Compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Transmission infrastructure is present on western property boundary per Sheet 3. Proposed trees lack mature height documentation and precise clearance measurements from transmission conductors.","reasoning":"Two requirements necessary for verification: (1) mature height per ECM Appendix F, and (2) precise lateral distance from transmission structures. Both are unavailable in submitted documents.","tools_used":["Read","vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Northwestern, southwestern, and other areas near utility poles on property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision analysis confirms tree symbols are positioned in corner areas where utility poles are located. Exact lateral distances cannot be measured from available plans. Clearance verification requires precise measurement not provided on landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan shows three utility poles along OHE line on western property boundary (northwest, midpoint, southwest locations). Sheet 31 landscape plan vision analysis identified tree symbol clusters in NW and SW corners near pole locations.","reasoning":"While trees are visible near pole locations, the 10-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified without precise lateral distance measurements. No dimensions are provided on the landscape plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas near transformer pad locations on west and east sides of site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Four electrical transformer pads shown on Sheet 21 (west side near Bldg 1-2 and 8; east side near Bldg 4-5 and 6-7). Landscape plan shows trees in these general areas but precise lateral distances from equipment access doors and pad edges cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 identifies four 'Electrical Transformer Pad' locations. Sheet 31 landscape plan vision analysis found 5-6 trees along west side and additional trees on east side near these general locations.","reasoning":"The 10-foot minimum clearance from equipment and from access door to drivable surface cannot be verified without precise measurements. No clearance dimensions or callouts shown on landscape plan.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas along underground electric lines and pull box locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electric lines and pull boxes are shown on Sheet 21 electrical plan. Landscape plan shows trees throughout site but no clearance measurements documented to verify 5-foot minimum distance from underground equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electric lines (marked with solid blue lines) and pull boxes (marked with 'E' symbols) throughout the site distribution network. Sheet 31 shows tree symbols in multiple areas but no callouts or dimensions referencing underground facilities.","reasoning":"Without precise measurements or documented clearances from underground equipment, compliance with 5-foot minimum distance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where trees are proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) and landscape details (Sheet 37) do not show root barrier specifications. No 4-foot deep root barriers positioned 5 feet from underground equipment are detailed or dimensioned on the landscape plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan shows trees throughout site but contains no detail callouts or notes referencing root barrier requirements for trees near underground electric equipment. Sheet 37 (Landscape Details) was referenced in the project guide but review of landscape plan blocks confirms no root barrier details are provided.","reasoning":"The requirement is explicit: 'minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment.' The landscape plan submission contains no such details, indicating this requirement has not been addressed in the design.","tools_used":["Read","vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"a