lassifications needed for electrical clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan shows all trees with same symbol categories (M, SY, PL, P) with no notation for mature height or size class. Sheet 35 lists minimum purchase specifications but not mature heights per ECM Appendix F, which is the controlling reference per the grouping.","reasoning":"Large tree designation (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) is essential for applying the appropriate clearance restrictions from electrical facilities. The landscape plan provides no mechanism for identifying which trees fall into this category, preventing field verification of clearance compliance.","tools_used":["Read","vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan areas showing trees in proximity to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows both tree symbols and overhead electric (OHE) line on the same drawing but lacks sufficient documentation to verify clearances. Vision analysis identified trees positioned directly on or immediately adjacent to OHE line markings on southern boundary, with no dimensions, callouts, or notes confirming clearance compliance. Cross-reference to electrical plan (Sheet 21) required for clearance verification is not explicitly shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows OHE line marking on southern boundary and tree symbols in same area. Vision analysis found approximately 5 tree symbols in south-central and southeast areas positioned directly on or overlapping the OHE line representation. No dimensions or verification notes reference clearances between these specific trees and the overhead line.","reasoning":"While trees are technically shown 'in relation to' overhead facilities on the same plan sheet, the deficiency is insufficient clarity for clearance verification. The trees overlap with utility line symbols with no documented clearance verification, preventing confirmation that trees are beyond restricted zones.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas within transmission structure clearance zones (25 feet per Sheet 3 notes) along western property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 Block 13 explicitly states 'No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.' Landscape plan shows trees along western boundary near transmission infrastructure. No Austin Energy written approval letter is referenced or provided in submitted documents authorizing trees within this prohibited clearance zone.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 general notes contain transmission clearance requirements from Austin Energy specifying 25-foot tree-free buffer from transmission structures. Sheet 21 electrical plan shows transmission poles on western boundary. Sheet 31 landscape plan vision analysis identified 5-6 trees along western boundary in areas approximately 10-30 feet from western facade (where transmission structures are located).","reasoning":"The project has explicitly acknowledged transmission structure clearance requirements in general notes (Sheet 3). Trees are proposed in areas that appear to fall within the 25-foot prohibited zone based on visual analysis. No Austin Energy approval letter authorizing this variation is provided with the submitted plans, indicating non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision","Read"]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context