 structure clearance requirements without Austin Energy approval\n\nThe analysis is thorough and based on the available documentation, with clear citations to the code and evidence from the submitted plans.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f00b2f4f-4bf8-4369-b6e1-683efc1760e1","uuid":"64027c0c-a4a6-4ede-8ecb-2c385b8620f2"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188957834,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2544FJXD2CQ26ESW7XX3G5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Completion Summary\n\nI have completed the comprehensive review of **Grouping EL-2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines)** for the Valley View Townhomes project. Here's what was evaluated:\n\n### Research Conducted:\n- **Electrical Infrastructure**: Confirmed presence of transmission facilities, distribution lines, transformer pads, utility poles, and underground equipment throughout the site\n- **Proposed Plantings**: Reviewed 40+ tree symbols on landscape plan; identified four proposed species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud)\n- **Plan Examination**: Analyzed Sheets 21 (Electrical), 31 (Landscape), 35 (Plant Schedule), and Sheet 3 (General Notes with Austin Energy requirements)\n- **Documentation Gaps**: Identified critical missing elements: ECM Appendix F utility-compatibility designations, mature height specifications, clearance dimensions, root barrier details, and Austin Energy approvals\n\n### Findings Summary:\n\n**5 FAIL items identified:**\n- **EL-2.9**: Root barriers not specified for trees near underground equipment\n- **EL-2.10**: Plant species not identified on landscape plan symbols\n- **EL-2.11**: Large trees not differentiated on plans\n- **EL-2.14**: Trees shown near overhead facilities without documented clearance verification\n- **EL-2.15**: Trees within transmission structure 25-foot clearance zone (per Sheet 3) without Austin Energy approval\n\n**7 NOT-VERIFIABLE items identified:**\n- **EL-2.1, EL-2.2, EL-2.3, EL-2.4**: Cannot verify utility-compatible status or mature heights without ECM Appendix F\n- **EL-2.6, EL-2.7, EL-2.8**: Cannot precisely measure clearances from poles, pads, and underground equipment\n\n**3 items not flagged** (passing or not applicable):\n- EL-2.5: No transmission easement on property (N/A)\n- EL-2.12, EL-2.13: No clearance dimensions shown on plans; measurement methodology not applicable (PASS)\n\nAll findings have been submitted with code citations, applicable areas, and detailed reasoning."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f00b2f4f-4bf8-4369-b6e1-683efc1760e1","uuid":"2a4965df-8999-4a23-a8f6-b1a3e5f9393b"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188957911,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":389029,"duration_api_ms":185281,"num_turns":24,"result":"## Completion Summary\n\nI have completed the comprehensive review of **Grouping EL-2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines)** for the Valley View Townhomes project. Here's what was evaluated:\n\n### Research Conducted:\n- **Electrical Infrastructure**: Confirmed presence of transmission facilities, distribution lines, transformer pads, utility poles, and underground equipment throughout the site\n- **Proposed Plantings**: Reviewed 40+ tree symbols on landscape plan; identified four proposed species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud)\n- **Plan Examination**: Analyzed Sheets 21 (Electrical), 31 (Landscape), 35 (Plant Schedule), and Sheet 3 (General Notes with Austin Energy requirements)\n- **Documentation Gaps**: Identified critical missing elements: ECM Appendix F utility-compatibility designations, mature height specifications, clearance dimensions, root barrier details, and Austin Energy approvals\n\n### Findings Summary:\n\n**5 FAIL items identified:**\n- **EL-2.9**: Root barriers not specified for trees near underground equipment\n- **EL-2.10**: Plant species not identified on landscape plan symbols\n- **EL-2.11**: Large trees not differentiated on plans\n- **EL-2.14**: Trees shown near overhead facilities without documented clearance verification\n- **EL-2.15**: Trees within transmission structure 25-foot clearance zone (per Sheet 3) without Austin Energy approval\n\n**7 NOT-VERIFIABLE items identified:**\n- **EL-2.1, EL-2.2, EL-2.3, EL-2.4**: Cannot verify utility-compatible status or mature heights without ECM Appendix F\n- **EL-2.6, EL-2.7, EL-2.8**: Cannot precisely measure clearances from poles, pads, and underground equipment\n\n**3 items not flagged** (passing or not a