{"level":30,"time":1778188958048,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":389480,"duration_api_ms":178155,"num_turns":27,"result":"I have completed my comprehensive site plan review for the **Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines** grouping (EL-2). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI identified **7 deficiency findings** out of 15 checklist items:\n\n### **FAIL Findings (5 items):**\n1. **EL-2.1** – Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution: Multiple trees are positioned 3-5 feet, 8-10 feet, and 12-15 feet from overhead electric lines, but species are not identified at these locations, making utility compatibility unverifiable.\n\n2. **EL-2.6** – Trees within 10 feet of utility poles: A mitigation tree in the southwest corner is located only 3-5 feet from a utility pole.\n\n3. **EL-2.7** – Trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment: Multiple proposed trees are shown directly above or in immediate proximity to 5 electrical transformer pads on the site.\n\n4. **EL-2.10** – Plant legend doesn't identify species: The landscape plan shows trees only by category (M, ST, PL, P) with no species names. The plant schedule lists species using different symbols with no cross-reference to the landscape plan.\n\n5. **EL-2.11** – Large trees not differentiated: No mature height information is provided for any species. Landscape plan contains no notation indicating which trees will mature to large size (40+ feet).\n\n### **NOT-VERIFIABLE Findings (2 items):**\n1. **EL-2.3** – Large trees (40+ feet) within 25 feet of distribution: Multiple trees are within this zone, but mature heights are not provided, making it impossible to verify the 40-foot threshold.\n\n2. **EL-2.15** – No Austin Energy approval for restricted-zone plantings: Trees are proposed in violation zones without documented written approval from Austin Energy.\n\n### **Pass/N/A Items (8 items) - Omitted from output:**\nThe remaining items either don't apply (no transmission facilities or easements identified) or have no measurable dimensions shown on the plans (EL-2.12, EL-2.13), or requirements are met (EL-2.14 – trees ARE shown in relation to overhead facilities).\n\n**The output has been provided in structured format above.**","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e41429b8-28b1-469f-8aa7-638b39040e37","total_cost_usd":0.27096570000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":756,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73392,"cache_read_input_tokens":915247,"output_tokens":17389,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":73392},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":756,"outputTokens":17389,"cacheReadInputTokens":915247,"cacheCreationInputTokens":73392,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27096570000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows multiple proposed trees within the 15-foot distribution clearance zone: SE corner easternmost tree at 8-10 feet from the southern OHE line; SE corner middle tree at 12-15 feet; SW corner tree at 3-5 feet from western OHE line. However, no species identification is provided at these locations, making utility compatibility unverifiable.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.10.4, only utility-compatible trees are permitted within 15 feet of distribution conductors. Trees are planted within this zone, but applicant has not identified species at specific locations (see EL-2.10 deficiency), preventing verification that they are utility-compatible. Burden of proof is on applicant to demonstrate compliance; absent species identification, this requirement cannot be verified as met.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary overhead electric line","Western boundary overhead electric line","Southeast corner trees (3 trees)","Southwest corner tree","Western boundary street yard trees (southern portion)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed within 15 feet of overhead electric distribution lines (some as close as 3-5 feet), but species are not identified at these locations on the landscape plan, making it impossible to verify utility compatibility. Applicant must identify species at each tree location and confirm utility-compatible status per ECM Appendix F, or provide documented Austin Energy approval."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows multiple trees within 25 feet of the southern OHE line (easternmost at 8-10 feet; middle at 12-15 feet). The plant schedule lists Live Oak and Cedar Elm as proposed species, but does not provide their mature heights, only minimum planting specs (16' height). No ECM Appendix F reference or mature height designation is provided.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 prohibits large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F definition) within 25 feet of distribution lines. The applicant has not provided: (1) the mature heights of proposed species, or (2) a cross-reference between species and tree locations on the landscape plan. Without this information, it cannot be determined whether any trees meet the 40+ foot mature height threshold.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner trees within 25 feet of southern OHE line","Southern property boundary area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mature heights for proposed tree species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) are not provided. Only planting specs show minimum installation heights (16' or 8-10'). Cannot verify whether proposed trees will mature to 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F definition. Applicant must provide mature height information for all species proposed within 25 feet of overhead lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan and vision analysis identify a utility pole at the southwest corner intersection of the southern and western OHE lines. A mitigation tree is positioned 3-5 feet east of the western OHE line at this same location, directly adjacent to this utility pole.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 prohibits trees within 10 feet of any electric utility pole. The tree's distance of 3-5 feet from the pole clearly violates this requirement. The applicant has not provided any distance dimension or note explaining compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southwest corner tree at pole location","Western property boundary at southern terminus"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A tree is proposed 3-5 feet from a utility pole on the western property boundary. This violates the 10-foot minimum clearance required by UCM § 1.10.10.4. Applicant must either relocate this tree beyond 10 feet from the pole or provide documented Austin Energy approval for the variance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows 5 transformer pads (pad-mounted equipment) distributed across the site. The vision analysis of that sheet notes that 'all 5 transformer pads are located directly underneath or immediately adjacent to large circular outlines that typically denote existing or proposed tree canopies.' The landscape plan shows proposed trees at locations corresponding to these pad locations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 prohibits trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted electric equipment. The fact that tree canopy symbols overlap or are positioned directly above transformer pad symbols on the plans indicates distances less than 10 feet. Without specific location cross-reference and distance dimensions, the positions suggest non-compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Northwest transformer pad area (near Building 1)","Mid-west transformer pad area (near Building 2)","Southwest transformer pad area (near Building 8)","South-central transformer pad area (near Building 7)","East transformer pad area (near Building 4)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple proposed trees are shown directly above or within immediate proximity to electrical transformer pads on the site. This suggests non-compliance with the 10-foot clearance requirement from pad-mounted equipment. Applicant must provide clear distance dimensions and confirm all trees are at least 10 feet from each transformer pad, or provide Austin Energy approval."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) uses four categorical symbols (M, ST, PL, P) to denote trees. No species names appear anywhere on this plan. The plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists four species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but uses different graphical symbols (circle-plus, center-dot-with-lines, scalloped-circle, clover-shape) that do not match the landscape plan symbols. No legend or table cross-references the two symbol systems.","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, a plant legend must identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities. The landscape plan contains no species identification whatsoever. While a separate plant schedule exists, it uses an incompatible symbol system with no cross-reference to the landscape plan. Therefore, it is impossible to determine which species is planted at which location on the site.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All trees proposed on landscape plan (sheets 31)","Trees within 15 feet of overhead electric distribution lines","Trees near pad-mounted equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan identifies trees only by regulatory category (M, ST, PL, P) without species names. The plant schedule lists species using different symbols with no cross-reference to the landscape plan. A unified plant legend must be provided on the landscape plan identifying each tree location by species name (common and/or scientific) to allow verification of utility compatibility and mature height characteristics near electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The landscape plan shows multiple trees with no differentiation by size or maturity classification. The plant schedule provides minimum planting heights (16' for Live Oak/Cedar Elm; 8-10' for Mexican Redbud/Texas Mountain Laurel) but does not provide mature heights for any species. No notation on plans indicates which trees will mature to large sizes (40+ feet).","reasoning":"Per Reviewer Convention, large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) must be differentiated on plans to allow verification of clearances from overhead facilities. The applicant has not provided: (1) mature height data for proposed species, or (2) any designation on the landscape plan to identify which trees will be large at maturity. This prevents verification of compliance with the 25-foot clearance requirement for large trees.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All trees proposed within 25 feet of overhead electric distribution lines","Southeast corner trees","Western boundary trees"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No mature height information is provided for proposed tree species. The landscape plan contains no notation indicating which trees will mature to large size (40+ feet). Applicant must provide mature heights for all proposed species per ECM Appendix F and clearly designate large trees on the landscape plan with a distinct symbol or notation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multiple trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones: trees at 3-5 feet from western OHE line (violates 15-foot minimum), trees at 8-10 feet and 12-15 feet from southern OHE line (at or below 15-foot minimum), and at least one tree within 10 feet of a utility pole. A review of the site plan, electrical plan, landscape plan, plant schedule, and available supplementary documents reveals no letters, approvals, or written documentation from Austin Energy authorizing these clearance variances.","reasoning":"Per UCM § 1.10.10.4, variations to planting distances require explicit written approval from Austin Energy. The applicant has proposed trees in prohibited zones without providing documented Austin Energy approval. While absence of such approval is evident, it is possible approval exists in correspondence not included in the site plan submittal. However, if approval exists, it must be included in the plans or clearly referenced.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Bash"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southwest corner tree (3-5 feet from pole)","Southeast corner trees (8-15 feet from OHE line)","Trees within 10 feet of utility poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed within clearance zones that violate UCM § 1.10.10.4 minimums (less than 15 feet from distribution, less than 10 feet from poles). No documented written approval from Austin Energy authorizing these variances is evident in the submitted plans or supplementary documents. Applicant must either relocate trees to comply with clearance requirements, or provide documented Austin Energy written approval for the proposed variance."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0295c304-5dae-4d01-8d3b-c7f0ab52d4db"}
