{"level":30,"time":1778188958124,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR2542P6W8R7R96NCDV81QM7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive evaluation of all 47 checklist items in the EL-MD-EXP grouping 1 (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Applicability:** ✓ **APPLICABLE** — The project has overhead electric facilities present on the site:\n- Eastern boundary: OHE line running north-south parallel to Buildings 5-6 (marked with 5' Electric Easement)\n- Southern boundary: OHE line running west-east parallel to Buildings 7-8, crossing two main site driveways\n- Multiple utility poles with at least one down guy wire visible on existing conditions survey\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Found:** 7 FAIL items + 30 NOT-VERIFIABLE items\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**FAIL Items (Complete Documentation Gaps):**\n1. **EL-1.7** — No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations provided\n2. **EL-1.8** — No section/plan detail exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to buildings\n3. **EL-1.17** — No retaining wall section exhibits with clearance dimensions from conductor\n4. **EL-1.23** — **Critical deficiency:** No clearance dimension annotations provided anywhere on the entire site plan where overhead lines exist\n5. **EL-1.27** — Items within electric easements lack clearance verification dimensions from conductor\n6. **EL-1.31** — No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data for driveways crossing overhead lines (16-18 foot vertical clearance required but cannot be verified)\n7. **EL-1.46** — **Missing required note:** 48-hour Austin Energy notification requirement NOT stated on cover sheet/general notes (required by UCM § 1.10.2 and Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752)\n\n**Most Critical Issue:** The site plan shows overhead electric facilities adjacent to buildings and crossing driveways, but provides **zero clearance dimension annotations** from the outside conductor to any site feature. This is a fundamental documentation failure preventing verification of the required clearances (7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial, 16-18 feet vertical for driveways).\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items:** 30 items cannot be verified due to missing surveyed conductor elevations, clearance dimension exhibits, section views, and clearance verification documentation.\n\nThe structured output with detailed findings, code citations, and applicable areas has been submitted."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce5a084e-a0f7-4302-9557-5dc167da4ff6","uuid":"7703ae7e-44af-4744-800a-3ed27247e3c9"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188958595,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":389671,"duration_api_ms":233307,"num_turns":29,"result":"I have completed the comprehensive evaluation of all 47 checklist items in the EL-MD-EXP grouping 1 (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Applicability:** ✓ **APPLICABLE** — The project has overhead electric facilities present on the site:\n- Eastern boundary: OHE line running north-south parallel to Buildings 5-6 (marked with 5' Electric Easement)\n- Southern boundary: OHE line running west-east parallel to Buildings 7-8, crossing two main site driveways\n- Multiple utility poles with at least one down guy wire visible on existing conditions survey\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Found:** 7 FAIL items + 30 NOT-VERIFIABLE items\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**FAIL Items (Complete Documentation Gaps):**\n1. **EL-1.7** — No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations provided\n2. **EL-1.8** — No section/plan detail exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to buildings\n3. **EL-1.17** — No retaining wall section exhibits with clearance dimensions from conductor\n4. **EL-1.23** — **Critical deficiency:** No clearance dimension annotations provided anywhere on the entire site plan where overhead lines exist\n5. **EL-1.27** — Items within electric easements lack clearance verification dimensions from conductor\n6. **EL-1.31** — No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data for driveways crossing overhead lines (16-18 foot vertical clearance required but cannot be verified)\n7. **EL-1.46** — **Missing required note:** 48-hour Austin Energy notification requirement NOT stated on cover sheet/general notes (required by UCM § 1.10.2 and Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752)\n\n**Most Critical Issue:** The site plan shows overhead electric facilities adjacent to buildings and crossing driveways, but provides **zero clearance dimension annotations** from the outside conductor to any site feature. This is a fundamental documentation failure preventing verification of the required clearances (7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial, 16-18 feet vertical for driveways).\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items:** 30 items cannot be verified due to missing surveyed conductor elevations, clearance dimension exhibits, section views, and clearance verification documentation.\n\nThe structured output with detailed findings, code citations, and applicable areas has been submitted.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ce5a084e-a0f7-4302-9557-5dc167da4ff6","total_cost_usd":0.34731770000000006,"usage":{"input_tokens":13389,"cache_creation_input_tokens":93672,"cache_read_input_tokens":866437,"output_tokens":26039,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":93672},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":13389,"outputTokens":26039,"cacheReadInputTokens":866437,"cacheCreationInputTokens":93672,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.34731770000000006,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Eastern and southern property boundaries where overhead electric lines exist adjacent to proposed buildings (Buildings 5-8)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings do not have building elevation sheets showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations and dimensioned clearances from outside conductor. Without surveyed conductor location and elevation data, the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4, 9, 11, and 31 clearly show overhead electric (OHE) lines on the site with utility pole symbols. However, no building elevation sheets exist that display the surveyed elevation of the overhead conductors relative to building faces, roof lines, or other vertical features.","reasoning":"Checklist item EL-1.1 requires verification that buildings maintain 7.5-foot clearance from conductors. The site plan shows OHE lines adjacent to Buildings 5-8, but provides no surveyed conductor elevations or dimension annotations to demonstrate compliance. Without building elevations showing conductor location and clearance dimensions originating from the outside conductor, compliance cannot be determined. The applicant appears to have prepared only a preliminary electrical design showing underground service (Sheet 21) without addressing clearances from existing overhead facilities.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Eastern and southern property boundaries where overhead electric distribution lines exist (Buildings 5-8 and driveways)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines but provides no dimension annotations or clearance verification exhibits showing 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of distribution primary and neutral conductors to proposed buildings and site features.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines are depicted on Sheets 4, 9, 11, and 31 near the site boundaries. The site plan includes notes referencing distribution and transmission facilities (Sheet 3), but no plan or section view exhibits show radial clearance dimensions measured from the outer conductor to buildings, parking areas, or other customer facilities.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires customer facilities to maintain 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of distribution primary and neutral conductors. The site plan shows OHE lines adjacent to proposed buildings and driveways but provides no dimension lines originating from the outside conductor showing these clearances. Without explicit clearance verification exhibits, the 15-foot radial clearance cannot be confirmed, particularly for Buildings 5-8 which run parallel to the eastern OHE line within a marked electric easement.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8, specifically evaluating overhangs, awnings, balconies, roof overhangs relative to nearby overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation or section views provided showing building projections (overhangs, balconies, roof details) and their clearances from overhead electric conductors. Clearance verification from both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial envelopes cannot be assessed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan set includes architectural unit layouts (Sheet 29) and landscape/site plan views but does not include building elevation drawings showing roof lines, balconies, overhangs, or other projections that might extend toward overhead electric facilities.","reasoning":"Checklist item EL-1.3 specifically requires verification of clearances for building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios). The OHE lines run near Buildings 5-8 on the eastern boundary, but without building elevations showing vertical profiles and clearance dimensions, the requirement cannot be verified. No section views are provided that show the relationship between conductor location and building projections.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Site plan - if any gas pump canopies are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies identified on site plan. Item is not applicable as this is a residential townhome development with no fuel service facilities proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan shows 39 multi-family townhome units in 8 buildings with parking, driveways, and landscape features. No gas pumps or fuel service infrastructure are indicated anywhere on the plans.","reasoning":"The checklist item EL-1.4 only applies when gas pump canopies are proposed. The Valley View Townhomes is a residential multi-family project with no gas pump facilities shown or described. This item does not apply to this project.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and pedestrian walkways on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows driveways and pedestrian walkways but provides no section or plan view exhibits showing 15-foot radial clearance dimensions from overhead electric distribution facilities to the edges of these elevated features or walkways.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows two main site entrances labeled 'Construct Type II Driveway' on the southern boundary where the OHE line crosses (Sheet 9, vision analysis confirmed). Sheets 22 and 38 show driveway and site construction details but do not address clearances from overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"EL-1.5 requires stairs, elevated walkways, and elevated platforms to maintain 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution facilities. While elevated features (driveways) are shown on the site plan where OHE lines are present, no section views or clearance dimension annotations are provided to demonstrate the 15-foot radial clearance is maintained from the outer conductor.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 5-8 relative to electric facilities in right-of-way and easements on eastern and southern boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings maintain setback from property lines where electric easements are recorded, but no surveyed clearance dimensions from outside conductor to building faces are provided to demonstrate both 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained as permanent requirements per UCM § 1.10.3.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 2 (Plat) and Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) show recorded easements on the property boundaries. Sheet 4 shows overhead utility lines (OHE) along these boundaries with utility poles. OHE lines are shown along eastern and southern boundaries where electric easements are designated (5' Electric Easement, 25' Drainage Easement noted).","reasoning":"EL-1.6 specifically addresses buildings in right-of-way adjacent to site where electric facilities exist. The site has recorded easements with overhead electric lines. The 7.5-foot and 15-foot clearances must be measured from the outside conductor, not the pole or easement boundary. Without surveyed conductor locations and clearance dimensions on the plans, these permanent clearance requirements cannot be verified. The plans show building setbacks from easements but not specific clearances from the actual conductor.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site - Buildings 5-8 near overhead electric facilities on eastern and southern boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan set that show surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors with clearance dimensions to building faces and projections. Only architectural plan views are provided (Sheet 29) without elevation details.","agentTrace":{"observation":"A complete review of the 39-sheet site plan set shows no building elevation sheets. Sheet 29 (Addressing Plan) provides only plan-view building layouts. Sheets 21 and 22 address electrical and construction details but not conductor elevations relative to building heights. The existing overhead electric facilities are shown in plan view on Sheets 4, 9, 11, and 31 with no corresponding elevation documentation.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors on building elevation sheets to demonstrate required clearances are met when buildings are within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities. Buildings 5-8 are near OHE lines shown on multiple plan sheets, yet no building elevations with surveyed conductor data are provided. This is a clear deficiency as the submission lacks the required documentation type entirely.","tools_used":["Read","Glob"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All building locations on site; specifically Buildings 5-8 near overhead electric lines on eastern and southern boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows buildings and overhead electric lines in plan view on multiple sheets but provides no section or enlarged plan detail views with dimension lines showing clearances from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings and building projections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9, 11, and 31 show OHE lines and building locations in horizontal plan view only. Sheet 22 provides driveway construction details and Sheet 38 provides wall sections, but none of these sheets show section views or enlarged details with dimension lines originating from the conductor to building edges. The grouping guidance specifically requires 'dimension lines originating at the conductor location, not at the pole' - no such dimensions appear on any sheet.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires plan and section view exhibits showing dimensions from outer conductor to outermost edges of buildings and projections. The site plan provides plan views showing the relative locations of OHE lines and buildings, but provides no section views or detailed clearance verification exhibits with measured dimensions. This critical documentation is entirely missing from the submission.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Fence alignments on site - perimeter fences shown on site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fence locations are shown on site plan and landscape plan, but no dimension annotations demonstrate 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor of overhead electric facilities. Dimension lines are not provided from the conductor to fence faces.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9 and 31 show wooden privacy fences (marked with 'X' symbols on landscape plan - Block 5 legend indicates H.6 symbol for wooden privacy fences). OHE lines are also shown on these sheets running along property boundaries.","reasoning":"Fence clearances from overhead conductors cannot be verified without dimension annotations showing clearance from the outer conductor to the fence surface. The site plan shows both fences and OHE lines but provides no specific clearance dimensions between them. Without measured clearance documentation, compliance with the 7.5-foot requirement cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence alignments relative to electric utility poles shown on site plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility poles are shown on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) and site plan (Sheet 9), and fences are shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31), but no dimension annotations demonstrate that fence posts maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from electric poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows multiple utility poles marked with circle/cross symbols along OHE lines. Sheets 9 and 31 show fence alignments. However, no dimension lines or clearance annotations are provided between fence post locations and pole locations.","reasoning":"Without specific horizontal clearance dimensions between fence posts and utility poles, the 10-foot minimum clearance cannot be verified. The submission shows the relative locations of these elements in plan view but does not provide measured clearances.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no Austin Energy substation fences on adjacent property"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation fences shown on site plan or adjacent properties. Item does not apply to this project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) and Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) show all existing and proposed infrastructure on and adjacent to the property. No substation structures or substation fencing are depicted.","reasoning":"Checklist item EL-1.11 only applies when fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with existing Austin Energy substation fences. This project has no substation infrastructure shown on the adjacent properties per the existing conditions survey and grading plan.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no electric transmission lines on site"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric transmission lines (≥60kV) are shown on site plan. The overhead electric facilities on this site appear to be distribution lines only (referenced in notes as distribution facilities). Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 notes distinguish between transmission and distribution facilities, with transmission facilities requiring more restrictive clearances. The OHE lines shown on Sheets 4, 9, 11, and 31 are referenced in context with distribution service and developer easements, and the notes reference 'overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project' (Sheet 3, Electric Notes) suggesting distribution lines serving the development. No 69kV, 138kV, or 345kV transmission line symbols are shown.","reasoning":"EL-1.12 applies to fencing beneath or adjacent to electric transmission lines (≥60kV). The overhead facilities on this site are distribution lines (serving customer loads), not transmission lines. Per the grouping regulatory overview, transmission vs. distribution designation is critical and determines applicability. This item does not apply to distribution-level facilities.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and site access routes near overhead electric lines on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveway posts/barriers may exist near overhead lines, but no section exhibits showing vertical and horizontal clearance verification dimensions from outermost electric line to barrier posts are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The two main site entrances (Type II Driveways) cross the OHE line that runs along the southern boundary per Sheet 9 vision analysis. Sheet 22 shows standard driveway construction details but does not address clearances from overhead electric lines to driveway features or barrier posts.","reasoning":"EL-1.13 requires vehicle barrier fencing beneath overhead lines to maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance with vertical and horizontal clearance verification exhibits. While the site plan shows driveways near OHE lines, no section views are provided demonstrating clearance compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls on site - multiple retaining walls shown on grading plan, including walls parallel to overhead electric lines on eastern and southern boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are shown on grading plan (Sheet 11) and detail sheets (Sheets 38-39), including walls adjacent to areas with overhead electric lines, but no clearance dimensions from outermost electric line to wall faces are dimensioned. Measurement from conductor (not pole) cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 vision analysis confirmed OHE lines on eastern and southern boundaries. Sheet 11 also shows existing retaining walls to be replaced and new retaining walls constructed. Sheets 38-39 provide wall structural details but do not address clearances from overhead electric conductors.","reasoning":"EL-1.14 requires retaining walls to maintain 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outermost electric line, measured from the conductor, not pole. The grading plan shows retaining walls and OHE lines but provides no section views with clearance dimensions from the conductor to the wall face. Without these specific dimensions originating at the conductor location, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no Austin Energy substation walls adjacent to site"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation walls shown on or immediately adjacent to the site. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) and adjacent property information shown on Sheets 9 and 11 show the immediate surrounding properties and infrastructure. No substation structures or walls are depicted.","reasoning":"EL-1.15 applies only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. This project has no adjacent substation infrastructure.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Any emergency access structures or elevated platforms if proposed on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows fire lanes and emergency access routes (Sheet 10) but does not provide section views with clearance dimension annotations from outside conductor of overhead electric facilities showing both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained for emergency access structures.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) shows fire lanes and emergency access routes on the site plan. The site has OHE lines on the boundaries that could affect these routes if emergency structures (elevated platforms or bridges) were proposed near the lines.","reasoning":"If emergency access structures exist near overhead lines, they must maintain both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances per UCM § 1.10.3. The site plan does not provide section views or clearance verification exhibits for emergency access features relative to overhead facilities.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls throughout site, particularly walls on eastern and southern boundaries adjacent to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall detail sheets (38-39) show structural sections and dimensions but lack any section view exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of retaining wall faces where overhead electric facilities exist adjacent to wall locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 38-39 provide detailed retaining wall sections showing rebar spacing, heights, and footing details. These sections do not reference or dimension clearances to the adjacent overhead electric lines shown on Sheet 11.","reasoning":"EL-1.17 requires section exhibits showing dimensions from outer conductor to wall faces. Sheets 38-39 provide wall sections but do not show any overlay or reference to the adjacent OHE lines. Where retaining walls are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities (as shown on Sheet 11 with walls adjacent to eastern and southern boundary OHE lines), section views must include clearance dimension annotations from the conductor to the wall.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways crossing or located beneath overhead electric lines on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two main site entrances (Type II Driveways) cross the overhead electric line on the southern boundary. Grading plan and section views do not show vertical clearance dimensions from lowest point of overhead facilities to finished driveway grades. No mid-span clearance verification survey data from registered surveyor is provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 vision analysis confirmed two Construct Type II Driveways cross the OHE line that runs along the southern boundary. Sheet 11 shows grading plan with finished floor elevations and contours but no overhead line elevation data or vertical clearance dimensions. No surveyor mid-span clearance data is provided.","reasoning":"EL-1.18 requires 16-foot vertical clearance for parking without truck traffic and 18-foot for areas with truck traffic. This is a critical safety requirement. The site shows driveways crossing OHE lines, but the plans provide: (1) no surveyed conductor elevations, (2) no vertical clearance dimensions from conductor to finished grades, and (3) no registered surveyor mid-span clearance data. Given the apparent close proximity of the driveways to the overhead lines and lack of any clearance documentation, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads shown beneath overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows 78 garage parking spaces and 10 surface parking spaces, but no vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are proposed to be located directly beneath overhead electric lines requiring vertical clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows parking areas on site plan, including garage spaces and surface lot parking. The OHE lines run along perimeter boundaries and do not pass directly through parking areas based on plan view analysis.","reasoning":"EL-1.19 applies when vehicle parking or display pads are proposed beneath overhead lines. While parking areas are shown on the site plan, they do not appear to be positioned directly beneath the OHE lines which run along the property boundaries.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no electric transmission lines on site"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric transmission lines (≥60kV) are shown on site plan. The overhead facilities appear to be distribution lines only. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The overhead electric facilities on this site are shown and referenced in notes as distribution lines serving the development. No transmission line symbols (69kV, 138kV, or 345kV) are depicted.","reasoning":"EL-1.20 applies only when roads or driveways are proposed beneath electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV). This project involves distribution-level facilities only, not transmission.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no highway or freeway grading with distribution underbuilt shown"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows local driveways and parking areas, not highways or freeways. No roadway with distribution underbuilt is proposed. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The project is a multi-family residential development on a local street (Valley View Road). The grading plan shows site driveways and parking, not highway or freeway improvements.","reasoning":"EL-1.21 applies to highway or freeway grading with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures. This project involves local site improvements only.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway locations relative to existing electric utility poles on southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two main site driveways cross or are immediately adjacent to overhead electric utility poles and lines on the southern boundary (visible on Sheet 9 vision analysis). No dimension annotations show 30-foot minimum clearance from driveway edge to pole locations, and no pole relocation notes are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows existing utility poles with OHE lines. Sheet 9 shows these poles and lines relative to the two main site entrance driveways. Vision analysis confirmed driveways cross the OHE line near poles on the southern boundary.","reasoning":"EL-1.22 requires existing poles in conflict with proposed driveways to be relocated minimum 30 feet from driveway edge. If poles are in the driveway alignment, relocation is required. The plans do not show 30-foot clearance dimensions or relocation notes. Without such documentation, compliance cannot be verified, particularly where vision analysis shows driveways crossing the OHE line.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All overhead electric facilities on site - eastern and southern boundaries where OHE lines are shown"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The site plan shows overhead electric facilities but provides NO clearance dimensions at all on any sheet. Where clearances should be annotated from the outside conductor to building edges, driveways, or other site features per UCM § 1.10.3 and the grouping guidance (dimensions must originate from outer conductor, not pole centerline), NO DIMENSIONS are provided. This is a fundamental documentation failure preventing any clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Complete review of Sheets 4, 9, 11, 21, 31, and all construction detail sheets (22-39) shows OHE lines and utility pole symbols depicted on multiple sheets. However, NOT A SINGLE dimension line is shown originating from the conductor or pole to demonstrate clearances to any site feature (buildings, driveways, walls, fences, etc.).","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires clearance dimensions measured from the outside conductor. The grouping guidance explicitly notes that a common violation pattern is 'Clearances measured from pole instead of conductor' and emphasizes that dimensions must originate from conductor location. The site plan shows OHE lines exist but provides zero dimension annotations whatsoever. This is a complete deficiency in the required documentation.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Streetlight pole locations relative to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows fire lanes and potential lighting areas but does not provide photometric plan or explicit streetlight pole locations with clearance verification relative to overhead electric lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9 and 10 show site layout with lighting considerations noted. Sheet 9 notes require all exterior lighting to be full cut-off and fully shielded. However, specific streetlight pole locations are not explicitly dimensioned on the plans relative to overhead lines.","reasoning":"EL-1.24 requires verification that streetlight poles are not located under overhead lines. While site lighting is required, the plans do not show explicit streetlight pole placements with clearance verification from the OHE lines shown on multiple sheets.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalk along Valley View Road (western property boundary) where utility poles exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows sidewalk along Valley View Road (western frontage) but does not provide dimension annotations showing sidewalk clearance from existing utility poles at property line. Cannot verify that sidewalk is cleared from poles at each end of property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows utility poles near Valley View Road frontage on the western side of the property. Sheet 9 site plan shows sidewalk alignment along the road frontage, but no clearance dimensions from poles to sidewalk edges are provided.","reasoning":"EL-1.25 requires sidewalks to be cleared from existing power poles at each property end along ROW frontage. Without dimension annotations showing sidewalk locations relative to pole locations, clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosure locations relative to overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":29}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash receptacles and enclosure areas are shown on site plan, but no dimension annotations demonstrate that trash areas maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric facilities when trash bins are raised during service.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 notes address trash collection requirements and restrictions. Site plan shows general site layout but does not provide explicit trash enclosure locations with clearance verification dimensions from overhead lines.","reasoning":"EL-1.26 requires trash enclosures and receptacles under overhead lines to maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance considering the raised height of trash bins during service. Without specific location and clearance dimensions, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Electric easement areas on eastern and southern property boundaries where overhead electric lines and distribution facilities exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric easements are shown on plat (Sheet 2) and grading plan (Sheet 11) with recorded 5' electric easement dimensions noted. However, the site plan does NOT provide clearance dimension annotations demonstrating that items within electric easements maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor as required. The grouping regulatory overview explicitly states the absolute prohibition against customer facilities installed 'under or over' distribution facilities, separate from maintaining distance clearances, but clearance dimensions are not provided to verify compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 explicitly labels 5' Electric Easement on the eastern boundary parallel to where OHE lines are shown. Sheet 2 (Plat) shows easement boundaries. However, Sheet 11 and other sheets do not provide dimension annotations showing that easement contents maintain 7.5-foot clearance from the conductor.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 prohibits customer facilities 'under or over' distribution facilities AND requires 7.5-foot clearance for items within easements. The grouping guidance identifies this as a common violation: 'Facilities installed under/over overhead distribution' and 'Items within electric easements lack required clearance from conductor.' The site shows easements and OHE lines but provides no clearance dimension documentation to verify items within the easement maintain the required clearance from the actual conductor location.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter location relative to overhead electric service drops"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility tap plans (Sheets 19-20) show water and wastewater connections but do not show water meter locations or service drops with clearance dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor of overhead electric service-drop conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19 and 20 detail water utility taps and connections but focus on the water line routing. No water meter location details are provided with reference to overhead electrical service drops.","reasoning":"EL-1.28 requires water meter clearances from overhead service-drop conductors. The utility plans do not show water meter locations or service drop routing with clearance dimensions.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing relative to overhead electric distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility tap plans show water line routing but do not provide dimension annotations or clearance notes demonstrating minimum clearance from proposed water lines to overhead electrical distribution facilities shown on site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19 and 20 show proposed water and wastewater utility routing. No specific clearance dimensions are provided between water lines and the OHE lines shown on other plan sheets.","reasoning":"EL-1.29 requires clearance verification between new water lines and overhead distribution facilities. The utility plans do not reference or dimension clearances from water lines to overhead electric facilities.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 5-8 on eastern property boundary within 5 feet of property line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings 5-8 are shown near the eastern property boundary where electric facilities exist in adjacent ROW/easements. No clearance space verification is provided showing that building setbacks allow necessary clearance for electric facility installation and maintenance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 grading plan shows Buildings 5-6 positioned along the eastern property boundary where a 5' Electric Easement is marked. Buildings 7-8 are near the southern boundary with OHE lines present.","reasoning":"EL-1.30 requires permanent foundations within 5 feet of property line to allow clearance space for adjacent electric facilities. The plans show buildings near property lines where easements and overhead facilities exist, but do not verify that adequate clearance space is maintained for utility installation and maintenance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and buildings relative to overhead electric facilities where vertical clearances appear marginal"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows two main driveways crossing overhead electric lines on southern boundary with no surveyed conductor elevation data or mid-span clearance documentation provided. Given the absence of any vertical clearance dimensions and the presence of OHE lines crossing driveways, a registered surveyor's mid-span clearance verification is required but not provided. UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires this documentation when vertical clearances may not meet minimums.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 vision analysis confirmed driveways cross the OHE line on southern boundary. Sheet 11 grading plan shows driveway finished grades (FFE ranges 683-687.5 feet) but provides NO conductor elevation data. No surveyor mid-span clearance certification is included in the submission.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires registered surveyor data showing mid-span clearances when existing overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearances (16-18 feet for driveways). The grouping guidance identifies 'Missing profile plans' and 'no surveyed mid-span clearance data' as common violation patterns. Here, driveways cross overhead lines with no conductor elevation data and no surveyor verification. This is exactly the situation that requires registered surveyor certification per the code.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line crossing alignment relative to roadway"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines cross the property and site driveways on plan view, but the angle of crossing relative to roadway alignment is not annotated or verified. Cannot determine if crossings are perpendicular to driveway centerlines as required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9 and 11 show OHE lines crossing driveways, but no angle dimension or note indicates whether these crossings are perpendicular (90-degree) to the driveway alignments.","reasoning":"EL-1.32 requires overhead electric line crossings of roadways to be oriented at 90 degrees to the road. Without angle annotations or crossing detail, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no secondary and primary overhead electric line crossings shown"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows only single overhead electric line routing without indication of multiple voltage levels (secondary and primary) crossing over each other. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows OHE lines but does not depict separate secondary and primary overhead conductors crossing one another. The design appears to show distribution lines for site service only.","reasoning":"EL-1.33 applies when site plans show secondary lines crossing above or below primary lines. The Valley View site plan does not depict this configuration.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no marquee signs proposed on site"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are shown on site plan. This is a residential townhome development without commercial signage of this type. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 and site plan details show only residential unit identification and wayfinding signage for the townhome development, not marquee signs.","reasoning":"EL-1.34 applies when marquee signs are proposed. This residential project has no such signage.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Utility plan showing electric service infrastructure conversion from overhead to underground"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground service infrastructure but does not show any new power pole locations for underground service conversion or document clearances from new poles to existing poles if applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design) shows underground service routing and transformers but does not address pole relocation or new pole placement relative to existing overhead poles.","reasoning":"EL-1.35 applies when new power poles are proposed for underground service conversion. If applicable to this project, pole locations and 20-foot separation documentation would be required, but Sheet 21 does not show new pole construction.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative lighting fixture locations relative to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Photometric plan and landscape plan show site lighting but do not provide clearance verification dimensions from overhead electric lines to decorative or site lighting fixtures showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 lighting notes require full cut-off and fully shielded fixtures per Code. Sheet 31 landscape plan shows vegetation and site features but does not dimensionally verify clearances from lighting fixtures to nearby OHE lines.","reasoning":"EL-1.36 requires clearance verification (7.5-foot and 15-foot radial) for decorative lighting fixtures proposed beneath overhead lines, or relocation notes. The plans do not provide this documentation.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Tree planting locations on landscape plan, particularly trees near overhead electric lines on property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed tree plantings but does not verify that trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors are from Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, UC column), nor does it measure lateral distances from tree locations to conductors. Required clearance distances are not annotated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan shows proposed mitigation trees (M symbol), street yard trees (SY), and parking lot trees (PL). Sheets 32 and 35 provide tree lists and species details. However, no lateral clearance dimensions are provided between tree locations and the OHE lines shown on Sheets 9, 11, and 31.","reasoning":"ECM § 2.4.1.D and § 2.4.2.C require trees within clearance distances (10 lateral feet for distribution, 50 for transmission per UCM § 1.10.10.4) to be from the Utility Compatible list. The landscape plan does not: (1) measure lateral distances from trees to conductors, (2) verify species are UC-compatible, or (3) annotate required clearance zones. Without these verifications, compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations proposed on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows meter locations on site but does not provide enlarged meter area details showing clearance from obstructions (fences, walls, landscaping, building projections) that would conflict with meter access, installation, and required 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meter locations on the site plan. However, no enlarged details or notes verify that adequate clearance space exists around meters for access and maintenance.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.9.3.1 requires meter locations to be clear of obstructions. The plans show meter locations but do not provide detailed verification of access space (30-inch width, 36-inch depth, 6.5-foot height minimum) or notes confirming no fences, walls, or landscaping obstruct meters.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings relative to existing streetlight poles if any exist on adjacent properties"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utilities and existing features but does not clearly identify or dimension streetlight pole locations adjacent to property with proposed building clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 legend identifies LIGHT POLE symbol but the plan does not clearly show which poles are streetlights versus utility poles with conductors.","reasoning":"EL-1.39 requires new buildings to maintain clearances from existing streetlight poles. The existing conditions survey would show these, but specific streetlight locations and building clearances are not clearly documented or dimensioned.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy wire locations from existing overhead electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows at least one down guy wire symbol at bottom-left corner (visible in vision analysis), but site plan and grading plan do not identify all guy wire locations or verify that proposed accessible paths, driveways, and site features do not conflict with guy anchor points. No pole relocation or conversion notes are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 vision analysis confirmed a down guy wire from a pole near the bottom-left (southwest) corner. Sheet 9 site plan shows adjacent driveway access and site features, but no guy wire annotations or relocation notes appear on subsequent planning sheets.","reasoning":"EL-1.40 addresses down guy wire conflicts with proposed site features. The existing conditions survey identifies at least one guy wire, but subsequent plans do not show guy wire locations relative to final site improvements, nor do they address relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles if conflicts exist. The grouping guidance specifically notes 'Down guy conflicts' as a common violation and that 'Electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans.'","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no angled guy easements from transmission structures on site"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission line guy easements or angled guy anchors from transmission structures are shown on site plan. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site has distribution-level facilities and at most distribution-level down guys from poles. No transmission-level angled guy structures are depicted.","reasoning":"EL-1.41 applies to angled guy anchors from transmission structures requiring dedicated guy easements with specific dimensions. This project has no transmission-level guy structures.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations from distribution poles on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows at least one down guy wire and anchor, but the plat (Sheet 2) and grading plan do not show dedicated guy anchor easements with the required 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry point as required by Austin Energy Transmission Engineering Standards.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 vision analysis identified down guy wire at southwest corner with ground anchor point visible. Sheet 2 (Plat) should show all easements including guy easements, but specific guy anchor easement dimensions (10 feet wide, extending 5 feet past anchor) are not shown in the materials reviewed.","reasoning":"EL-1.42 requires dedicated guy anchor easements with specific dimensions when down guys from distribution poles are present. The existing conditions survey shows a down guy, but the easement exhibit does not clearly show or dimension the required guy anchor easement.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformers and electrical equipment relative to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer locations on site but does not provide section views with vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to top of transformer equipment showing 7.5-foot minimum vertical sky-to-ground clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not provide elevation sections showing heights of transformers relative to any overhead conductors on site.","reasoning":"EL-1.43 requires transformers to maintain 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance from overhead lines. While transformers are shown on the electrical plan, no section views document vertical clearances from conductors.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["N/A - no transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations shown"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows pad-mounted transformers, not niche-mounted configurations. This item applies only to niche installations which are not proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan shows transformer pads (pad-mounted installations), not recessed or niche-mounted configurations.","reasoning":"EL-1.44 applies only to transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations). The Valley View project uses pad-mounted transformers.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platforms adjacent to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 references construction sequence and staging notes. Sheet 5 shows erosion control plan. However, no site logistics plan or construction phasing plan is provided showing construction staging areas, crane swing radius, material storage, or scaffold locations with 10-foot radial clearance verification from energized overhead lines as required by OSHA and UCM § 1.10.2.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 includes a 13-step construction sequence note. Sheet 5 shows temporary erosion and sediment control measures. However, no detailed construction logistics plan is provided showing equipment staging areas, cranes, or work zones with clearance dimensions from overhead lines.","reasoning":"EL-1.45 requires construction staging areas to maintain 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines. This is distinct from permanent clearances and is a critical OSHA requirement. The submission does not provide a detailed site logistics/construction phasing plan that addresses this requirement.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet and general notes where required notification requirement should be stated"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required note regarding 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage overhead lines is NOT included on the cover sheet or general notes. While Sheet 3 (Electric Transmission Notes) mentions a pre-construction safety meeting with Andrew Perez 48 hours before construction, UCM § 1.10.2 requires this notification requirement to be explicitly noted on the cover sheet or general notes plan. The cover sheet (Sheet 1) lacks this required note.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 1 cover sheet contains project information, fire department requirements (Block 15 on Sheet 3), and various notes but does NOT include an explicit note about 48-hour notification to Austin Energy per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. Sheet 3 references a pre-construction meeting but this is not the same as the required notification note on the cover sheet.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 explicitly requires plans to include a note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines (Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003). The checklist item specifically requires this note on cover sheet or general notes - not buried in transmission-specific notes on an interior sheet. Sheet 1 (Cover) does not include this required note.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Service mast through-roof installations on proposed buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows electrical infrastructure but does not provide building elevation drawings showing service mast locations and roof clearance dimensions (3-foot minimum above roof, or 18-inch if mast within 4 feet of roof edge, for voltages ≤300V).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical design shows service connection points but does not include building elevation drawings detailing service mast installations through roofs with clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"EL-1.47 requires building elevations showing service mast through-roof installations with clearance dimensions (3 feet or 18 inches depending on proximity to roof edge). The submission does not include building elevations with this detail.","tools_used":["Read"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"55f2115f-5907-42a8-9edc-f1ba8580f9d9"}
