{"level":30,"time":1778188970514,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR252S35GD67RSD46T4Y8PSE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WiezkTMmoxwcPfLwFr5pEx","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations shown on electrical plan but clearance distances to buildings are not dimensioned. Visual estimation from the 1\" = 20' scale suggests approximately 5-8 feet from building walls, but precise dimensions are required to verify compliance with the minimum 5-foot clearance requirement from building edges.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan shows 5 transformer pads positioned adjacent to buildings. The vision analysis estimated distances of 5-8 feet from building walls, but no numerical dimensions are provided on the plan to confirm these clearances.","reasoning":"Clearance distances cannot be verified without explicit dimensions or scaled measurements on the submitted documents. The plans show symbol/label callouts only without quantitative verification of the 5-foot minimum clearance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 1 (northwest near Building 1)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer Pad 1 is located near a sidewalk easement on the western property edge. The plan indicates a 'Sidewalk Easement' and '5' Concrete Sidewalk' but the distance from the transformer pad to the back of the sidewalk is not dimensioned. The minimum 2-foot clearance from the back of sidewalk cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 identified Transformer Pad 1 located 5-10 feet east of the sidewalk easement line, but no dimension labels showing the actual distance from pad edge to sidewalk are provided on the electrical or site plan.","reasoning":"While the plan shows the sidewalk and easement features, the specific clearance dimension is not labeled, making verification impossible without scaling the as-printed plan.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads (universal requirement)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan but their orientation and access door locations are not indicated. Without knowing which side of each pad contains the access door (hot-stick use area), the required 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The 5 transformer pads are shown as solid rectangles on Sheet 21, but there are no orientation marks, access door callouts, or operator control indicators shown on any pad location.","reasoning":"The hot-stick access requirement in Table 1.10.4 depends on identifying the specific face/side of the transformer with the access door. Without this information, compliance cannot be assessed.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer Pad 1 (northwest area), Transformer Pad 3 (west of Building 8)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":30},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing trees are located within 10-15 lateral feet of transformer pads. Transformer Pad 1 has a tree estimated at 10-15 feet distance; Transformer Pad 3 has a tree within 5-10 feet. The tree species cannot be positively identified or confirmed as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F from the submitted plans. Tree identification numbers are not clearly labeled on the electrical or site plan in proximity to transformer locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 identified tree canopies near TP1 (10-15 ft distance) and TP3 (5-10 ft distance). The existing tree plan (Sheet 30) shows tree symbols with protection markings, but species identification and tree tag numbers are not clearly visible in those proximity areas on the electrical plan itself.","reasoning":"While Sheet 32 provides a comprehensive tree list with species and utility-compatibility ratings (Appendix F Y/N/I columns), cross-referencing specific tree numbers to transformer pad locations requires clear labeling on the electrical and site plans that is not present. The spatial relationship between specific tagged trees and transformer pads cannot be reliably confirmed from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water line routing is shown on the utility tap plan (Sheet 19) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) but the horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and water service lines are not dimensioned. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified without explicit dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19 and 21 show water (W) and electrical (E) routing separately, with water lines illustrated on the utility plan and electrical lines on the electrical plan, but no cross-referenced dimension showing pad-to-water-line clearances.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit dimensions showing the horizontal clearance from each transformer pad edge to the nearest water line. The utility and electrical plans do not provide these dimensions.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater line routing is shown on utility plans and electrical plan but horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and wastewater service lines are not dimensioned. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility tap plan (Sheet 19) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) show wastewater (WW) and electrical (E) routing but lack dimensions showing specific clearances between transformer pad edges and wastewater lines.","reasoning":"Verification requires explicit horizontal clearance dimensions from transformer pad edges to wastewater line locations, which are not provided on the submitted plans.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain line routing is shown on grading and drainage plans (Sheet 12) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) but horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and storm drain lines are not dimensioned. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The storm sewer plan (Sheet 12) and electrical design plan (Sheet 21) display storm drain (SD) and electrical (E) routing separately but do not provide dimension labels showing pad-to-storm-drain clearances.","reasoning":"Clearance verification requires explicit horizontal dimensions from transformer pad edges to storm drain line edges. These dimensions are absent from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations where gas service is present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Grading and utility plans show gas infrastructure on the site but the horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and gas lines are not dimensioned. The required minimum clearance (24 inches for low-pressure, 36 inches for high-pressure) cannot be verified without explicit dimensions or pressure specifications.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 11 (grading plan) and Sheet 21 (electrical plan) show gas meter locations and routing, but no dimension callouts indicate the distance from transformer pad edges to gas lines.","reasoning":"Compliance with the 24 or 36-inch minimum (depending on pressure) requires explicit dimensions and gas pressure specifications not provided on the site plans.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility routing (electrical, water, wastewater, storm drain, telephone) is shown on various plan sheets but the horizontal and vertical clearance distances between transformer pads and other underground utilities are not dimensioned. Minimum 12-inch clearance (horizontal and vertical) cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multiple utility routing layers are shown across sheets 19, 21, and others, but no dimension callouts quantify the separations between electrical and other underground infrastructure at transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Verification of 12-inch OD-to-OD separation requires explicit dimensions on the plans, which are not provided.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad and underground facility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-installation of utilities (customer buildings/structures installed over or under AE underground facilities, or AE facilities installed over/under customer utilities) cannot be verified from the submitted plan set. Underground utility coordination details and cross-section drawings showing relative elevations are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plan set shows utility routing at various locations but does not provide detailed underground coordination drawings, profile views, or cross-sections showing vertical relationships of intersecting utilities.","reasoning":"Verification of no cross-installation requires detailed underground utility coordination information not present in the submitted documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer locations if overhead distribution conductors are present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution line locations are not clearly identified on the electrical design plan. The required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution line conductors cannot be verified. The electrical notes reference consultation with Austin Energy Design regarding overhead lines but overhead line routing is not shown on the submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical routing (marked as 'E' or '-E-') but does not depict overhead distribution lines, poles, or conductor routing.","reasoning":"Without identification of overhead distribution line locations and conductor positions, compliance with the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be assessed.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer locations if overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors are present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution primary and neutral conductor locations are not shown on the submitted electrical plan. The required 15-foot radius clearance (measured from the conductor centerline, not pole centerline) cannot be verified without identifying the specific overhead line locations and conductor positions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 depicts underground electrical infrastructure only. No overhead distribution line routing, pole locations, or conductor positions are shown.","reasoning":"Compliance with the 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution conductors requires identification of the conductor positions, which are not provided in the submitted plan set.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances through transformer pad locations are not provided in the plan set. Verification of clearances to overhead structures, building overhangs, parking garage ceilings, or enclosed areas above transformer locations cannot be made without profile/cross-section views.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The plan set includes plan view drawings (sheets 9, 11, 19, 21) but does not include cross-section views through transformer pad locations showing vertical clearances to overhead features.","reasoning":"Verification of vertical clearances (particularly the 35-foot niche clearance if applicable, or general overhead obstruction clearances) requires cross-section drawings that are absent from the submitted documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical design plan or in the electrical notes. The grading plan shows surface contours and drainage flow arrows but does not explicitly confirm that liquid drainage (if applicable for oil-filled equipment) is directed away from buildings. Without equipment type specification, the drainage requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but includes no notes, callouts, or specifications indicating oil-filled or dry-type equipment. Sheet 11 grading plan shows general drainage flow but does not specifically address drainage from transformer pad areas.","reasoning":"The requirement to ensure liquid flow away from buildings applies only to oil-filled equipment. Without specification of equipment type on the plans, compliance cannot be verified. Additionally, explicit drainage direction callouts at transformer pad locations are absent.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Property lines are shown on the site and electrical plans, but transformer pad locations are not dimensioned or labeled to explicitly confirm they are 100% located on private property and not straddling property lines. Additionally, facts.md identifies critical undisclosed easements not depicted on the site plan that may affect the property availability for transformer pad installation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Property boundaries are drawn on the site plan (Sheet 9), and transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21), but no dimension callouts confirm the transformer pad edges are within private property boundaries. Facts.md documents two perpetual easements (Instruments 2010070731 and 2011021137) covering ~0.44 acres of the NE portion that are not depicted on submitted plans.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimensions confirming transformer pad edges are on private property, and with undocumented easements potentially affecting property availability, property location status cannot be verified from the submitted documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads must not be located in prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines) without written Austin Energy Design approval. Transformer pad locations are not dimensioned relative to the documented easements. Facts.md identifies that two critical easements (Instruments 2010070731 and 2011021137) are not depicted on the site plan. Additional plat-dedicated easements (Cortez Heights and Trico Subdivision easements) are also not verified on the submitted site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The submitted site plan (Sheet 9) shows some easement lines (labeled as 'Sidewalk Easement', 'Electric Easement', 'Wastewater Easement', etc.) but facts.md documents that the two most critical easements (NE greenbelt access easement 0.31 ac and City of Austin drainage easement 0.130 ac) are NOT depicted. No cross-hatching or labeling on the electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows which transformer pads, if any, conflict with depicted or undepicted easements.","reasoning":"Without transformer pad locations being dimensioned relative to easement boundaries, and with two major easements not depicted on the site plan, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on the electrical or site plans. The UCM § 1.10.3 and associated regulations require transformer easements around pads for Austin Energy Design accessibility and maintenance, with width determined by AE Design on a project-specific basis. No easement boundaries, widths, or AE Design approval documentation are provided in the submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads but no easement boundaries, hatching, or width dimensions are labeled around the pads. Site plans and plats do not identify specific transformer easement areas.","reasoning":"Verification requires identification of transformer easement boundaries and documentation of the easement width approved by Austin Energy Design, neither of which are provided in the submitted documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters must be 100% on private property. The routing is shown on the electrical plan but routing paths are not dimensioned or explicitly labeled to confirm they do not cross right-of-way, easements, or other properties.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows electrical routing from transformer pads toward buildings and meter locations using line symbols, but no dimension callouts confirm routing is on private property. Specific routing coordinates or property boundary cross-references are absent.","reasoning":"Without explicit documentation and dimensions showing the electrical routing path remains on private property throughout, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"def