{"level":30,"time":1778188975085,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR254TMTM00W3A0N5SC20Q83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! The structured output has been submitted successfully. Let me summarize what I found:\n\nOut of 39 checklist items in the EL-13 grouping:\n- 1 FAIL (EL-13.37 - no AE Design transformer pad details)\n- 20 NOT-VERIFIABLE (due to missing dimensions, specifications, or documentation)\n- 18 PASS or N/A (items not applicable or not applicable to this project)\n\nThe key failures and not-verifiable items are:\n1. **EL-13.37 (FAIL)**: No AE Design transformer pad detail sheets or dimensions provided\n2. **EL-13.1 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: No dimensions to verify 5-foot clearance from buildings\n3. **EL-13.10 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: No access door orientation shown for hot-stick clearance verification\n4. **EL-13.13 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Trees near pads not identified; utility-compatibility not confirmed\n5. **EL-13.21-25 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Utility clearances not dimensioned\n6. **EL-13.31 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: No cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances\n7. **EL-13.32 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Equipment type not specified; drainage not verified\n8. **EL-13.33-36 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Property location and easement status not confirmed\n9. **EL-13.38 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Bollard specifications not provided; parking proximity unclear\n\nThe grouping review is now complete.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ee23800-1891-4c6c-9860-87ab169d6f67","uuid":"c35049b7-e15f-4b3b-a63d-314cf8fc07e9"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188979215,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine this landscape plan and identify:\n1. All tree locations shown on the site - describe their positions relative to buildings and site features\n2. The location of the overhead electric (OHE) utility line on this sheet\n3. The location of underground utilities and transformers shown\n4. Any trees that appear to be within restricted clearance zones from overhead or underground electrical infrastructure\n5. What tree symbols are used and what they represent (e.g., different symbols for different tree types)\n6. Any callouts, dimensions, or notes regarding electrical clearances for trees\n\nPay special attention to trees near the western property boundary where the overhead electric line is located, and trees near any transformer pads.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35, \"VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\"), here are the findings corresponding to your requests.\n\n**Important Note Regarding Orientation and Prompt Details:** Your prompt mentions an overhead electric line on the \"western property boundary.\" Based *strictly* on the visual evidence in this specific document, the line explicitly labeled \"- OHE -\" runs along the **Southern** boundary line, not the Western boundary line along Valley View Road. My analysis reflects exactly what is drawn and labeled on the page.\n\n### 1. Tree Locations Shown on the Site\nTrees are primarily located along the perimeter boundaries of the site, with a specific grouping in the western setback area.\n*   **Northern Boundary:** A row of trees is shown along the top edge of the property line, north of the building footprint. Moving from west to east, these contain tags: M, M, H-7, M, M, M. Further east, adjacent to areas labeled \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN,\" are trees tagged PL and M.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** A continuous row of trees runs along the entire southern property line. This row includes proposed trees with tags (M, M, H-7, M) and several symbols representing existing trees (circles with an 'X' inside and numbers like 10\"X, 8\"X, 12\"X).\n*   **Western Boundary (Street Yard):** Within the shaded area on the left side of the sheet (adjacent to Valley View Road), there are three main clusters of proposed trees.\n    *   Northwest corner: Contains trees tagged SY and M.\n    *   Mid-West section: Contains a tree tagged SY.\n    *   Southwest section: Contains a tree tagged SY.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** There are a few scattered existing tree symbols (circles with an 'X') near the eastern property line.\n*   **Interior:** There are no major tree canopies shown within the interior building courtyards on this sheet.\n\n### 2. Location of the Overhead Electric (OHE) Utility Line\nOn this specific sheet, the Overhead Electric utility line is explicitly labeled with the line type **\"- OHE -\"**.\n*   This line runs horizontally along the entire **Southern** edge of the site plan, parallel to the property line/Limits of Construction (\"- - LOC - -\").\n*   There is no line explicitly labeled \"OHE\" running along the Western boundary (Valley View Road) on this document.\n\n### 3. Location of Underground Utilities and Transformers\nUnderground utilities are primarily visible entering the site from the West (Valley View Road).\n*   **Water and Storm Drain:** Lines labeled **\"- W -\"** (Water) and **\"- SD -\"** (Storm Drain) are shown running parallel to the western street and branching into the site towards the building footprint.\n*   **Underground Electric and Pad:** There is a line labeled **\"- E -\"** entering from the western street boundary near the middle-lower section of the shaded \"Street Yard.\" This line terminates at a small rectangular pad located just southwest of the building footprint's westernmost wall. While not explicitly text-labeled \"Transformer,\" this symbol and connection indicate an electrical equipment pad.\n\n### 4. Trees Within Restricted Clearance Zones\n*   **Disclaimer:** This specific document does *not* define or delineate any restricted clearance zones (e.g., dashed radii arcs or dimensioned setbacks) around the electrical infrastructure. Therefore, it is not possible to state if a specific clearance rule is violated based solely on this page.\n*   **Proximity Observations:** Based on physical proximity shown on the drawing:\n    *   **Near OHE (South):** The entire row of proposed \"M\" (Mitigation) trees and existing trees along the southern boundary are planted directly on top of, or immediately adjacent to, the line labeled \"- OHE -\". The drawn canopies heavily overlap the OHE line.\n    *   **Near Underground Electric Pad (West):** In the mid-west section of the shaded Street Yard, a proposed tree tagged **\"SY\"** is drawn extremely close to the rectangular electrical pad at the terminus of the \"- E -\" line. The outer ring of the drawn tree canopy overlaps the rectangular pad.\n\n### 5. Tree Symbols and Representation\nTrees are visually represented by large circles indicating the canopy spread, with a crosshair at the center point. Inside or near the center point is a smaller circle containing an alphabetic tag.\n\nThe tags used inside these circles are defined exactly as follows in the **\"KEY NOTES:\"** section at the top right of the document:\n\n*   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n*   **M** - MITIGATION TREE\n\n*(Note: There are also circles with an 'X' inside and numerical inch measurements [e.g., 8\"X, 10\"X]. While standard convention suggests these are existing trees, they are not explicitly defined in the provided Key Notes on this sheet).*\n\n### 6. Callouts, Dimensions, or Notes Regarding Electrical Clearances\nA thorough review of all text blocks on this sheet (\"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE\", and \"KEY NOTES\") reveals that **there are no callouts, dimensions, or notes regarding electrical clearances for trees.**\n*   The \"IRRIGATION NOTES\" deal exclusively with TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water distribution, and system requirements.\n*   The general \"NOTE\" section discusses finished elevations for parking islands and topsoil requirements.\n*   There are no dimension lines indicating required distance between tree center points and the \"- OHE -\" line or the underground \"- E -\" pad.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1453,"outputTokens":1245,"totalTokens":5415,"reasoningTokens":2717},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine this landscape plan and identify:\n1. All tree locations shown on the site - describe their positions relative to buildings and site features\n2. The location of the overhead electric (OHE) utility line on this sheet\n3. The location of underground utilities and transformers shown\n4. Any trees that appear to be within restricted clearance zones from overhead or underground electrical infrastructure\n5. What tree symbols are used and what they represent (e.g., different symbols for different tree types)\n6. Any callouts, dimensions, or notes regarding electrical clearances for trees\n\nPay special attention to trees near the western property boundary where the overhead electric line is located, and trees near any transformer pads."}]}],"providerOptions":{"gateway":{"user":"b877dead-f786-4bf6-9ac4-3cde3f2ec546","tags":["label:VISION_CHECK_REVIEW_EL_MD_EXP_VAR1_RUN_1","tool:vision"]}},"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-I0qdQfQRSHDoyWsi1cWP8kvf","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 07 May 2026 21:22:59 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-a