{"level":30,"time":1778188989317,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR25532XRVV7EFGM7013BAFF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is very important information! The vision analysis found:\n\n1. **Overhead Electric (OHE) line running along the SOUTHERN boundary** of the site (not western as I initially thought based on Sheet 21)\n\n2. **Trees planted directly on or immediately adjacent to the OHE line:**\n   - \"The entire row of proposed \"M\" (Mitigation) trees and existing trees along the southern boundary are planted directly on top of, or immediately adjacent to, the line labeled \"- OHE -\". The drawn canopies heavily overlap the OHE line.\"\n\n3. **A Street Yard (SY) tree very close to the electrical pad:**\n   - \"In the mid-west section of the shaded Street Yard, a proposed tree tagged **\"SY\"** is drawn extremely close to the rectangular electrical pad at the terminus of the \"- E -\" line. The outer ring of the drawn tree canopy overlaps the rectangular pad.\"\n\n4. **No electrical clearance callouts on the landscape plan:**\n   - There are no dimensions or notes indicating required clearances between trees and the OHE line\n\nThis is a significant finding! The landscape plan appears to show trees within restricted clearance zones from overhead electric lines.\n\nHowever, I need to be more precise about what I'm seeing. The vision tool indicates there's an OHE line on the southern boundary of the site. I need to determine:\n\n1. Is this OHE line inside or outside the property line?\n2. What are the specifications for trees near overhead electric lines per the code?\n3. What types of trees are being planted?\n\nLet me check the plant schedule more carefully. From Sheet 35, the trees being planted are:\n- 2 Live Oak (100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' ht.)\n- 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' ht.)\n- 2 