{"level":30,"time":1778189004681,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR255JM84XBS1BKNTE2NPWSA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The blocks file for Sheet 32 doesn't show the actual tree survey table - it only shows the text blocks. I need to look for the actual tree table. Let me check the guide.md again - it mentions \"Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table\". Let me search for that specific block content or check if there's more detailed information about the tree species being planted.\n\nActually, looking back at Sheet 35's blocks, I can see the proposed trees being planted:\n\n**Shade Trees (from Block 11 of Sheet 35):**\n- 2 Live Oak, QUERCUS VIRGINIANA - 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM\n- 10 Cedar Elm, ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA - 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM\n\n**Ornamental Trees (from Block 17 of Sheet 35):**\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel, SOPHORA SECUNDIFLORA - 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL., 8' HT. MINIMUM\n- 6 Mexican Redbud, CERCIS CANADENSIS VAR. MEXICANA - 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL., 10' HT. MINIMUM\n\nNow I need to check:\n1. Are these utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F?\n2. What are their mature heights according to ECM Appendix F?\n3. Are there any issues with clearances from the overhead electric line?\n\nThe grouping file mentions that I need to cross-reference against ECM Appendix F. I don't have direct access to ECM Appendix F in the project data, but I do have information from the grouping file itself that gives me the thresholds:\n\nFrom the grouping file:\n- **Utility-compatible trees**: Trees marked with \"x\" in the \"UC\" column of ECM Appendix F; generally mature height ≤ 20 feet with some exceptions (e.g., Goldenball Lead-Tree at 25 ft, Texas Mountain Laurel at 25 ft)\n\n\n- **Large trees**: Trees listed in ECM Appendix F with mature height ≥ 40 feet\n\nTexas Mountain Laurel qualifies as utility-compatible despite reaching 25 feet at maturity. However, I'm missing confirmation on the UC status and mature heights for Live Oak, Cedar Elm, and Mexican Redbud. The installation specs show minimum heights at planting (16' for shade trees, 8-10' for ornamentals) but not their ultimate mature sizes. I need to examine the landscape plan more closely to assess proximity to the overhead electric line and determine if any of these plantings create clearance violations.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed658f06-b65b-479d-b752-f47b92243df6","uuid":"33963f73-f1a8-4d84-9038-87fb444b6bd5"}
