{"level":30,"time":1778189054103,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR257A61KWPNXQZQNV1NX0DB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LrRX4oi1SAch5Ti2frsQNg","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/block-3.md"}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed658f06-b65b-479d-b752-f47b92243df6","uuid":"28f40502-1f02-41fe-91f5-6ebb2f3cbfe3"}
{"level":30,"time":1778189054134,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LrRX4oi1SAch5Ti2frsQNg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Block 3\n     2→\n     3→## notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter 344 and other specific regulations.\n     4→\n     5→IRRIGATION NOTES:\n     6→AUTOMATIC IRRIGATION SYSTEMS SHALL COMPLY WITH TCEQ CHAPTER 344, AS WELL AS THE FOLLOWING REQUIREMENTS:\n     7→\n     8→1. THESE REQUIREMENTS SHALL BE NOTED ON THE SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT AND SHALL BE IMPLEMENTED AS PART OF THE LANDSCAPE INSPECTION:\n     9→a. THE SYSTEM MUST PROVIDE A MOISTURE LEVEL ADEQUATE TO SUSTAIN GROWTH OF THE PLANT MATERIALS;\n    10→b. THE SYSTEM DOES NOT INCLUDE SPRAY IRRIGATION ON AREAS LESS THAN TEN (10) FEET WIDE (SUCH AS MEDIANS, BUFFER STRIPS, AND PARKING LOT ISLANDS);\n    11→c. CIRCUIT REMOTE CONTROL VALVES HAVE ADJUSTABLE FLOW CONTROLS;\n    12→d. SERVICEABLE IN-HEAD CHECK VALVES AREA ADJACENT TO PAVED AREAS WHERE ELEVATION DIFFERENCES MAY CAUSE LOW HEAD DRAINAGE;\n    13→e. A MASTER VALVE INSTALLED ON THE DISCHARGE SIDE OF THE BACKFLOW PREVENTER;\n    14→f. ABOVE-GROUND IRRIGATION EMISSION DEVICES ARE SET BACK AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES FROM IMPERVIOUS SURFACES;\n    15→g. AN AUTOMATIC RAIN SHUT-OFF DEVICE SHUTS OFF THE IRRIGATION SYSTEM AUTOMATICALLY AFTER MORE THAN A ONE-HALF INCH (1/2\") RAINFALL; AND\n    16→h. NEWLY PLANTED TREES SHALL HAVE PERMANENT IRRIGATION CONSISTING OF DRIP OR BUBBLERS.\n    17→\n    18→2. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL DEVELOP AND PROVIDE AN AS-BUILT DESIGN PLAN TO THE CITY AT THE TIME THE FINAL IRRIGATION INSPECTION IS PERFORMED;\n    19→a. UNLESS FISCAL SECURITY IS PROVIDED TO THE CITY FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE SYSTEM, IT MUST BE OPERATIONAL AT THE TIME OF THE FINAL LANDSCAPE INSPECTION.\n    20→\n    21→3. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL ALSO PROVIDE EXHIBITS TO BE PERMANENTLY INSTALLED INSIDE OR ATTACHED TO THE IRRIGATION CONTROLLER, INCLUDING:\n    22→a. A LAMINATED COPY OF THE WATER BUDGET CONTAINING ZONE NUMBERS, PRECIPITATION RATE, GALLONS PER MINUTE AND THE LOCATION OF THE ISOLATION VALVE; AND AN AS BUILT PLAN.\n    23→\n    24→4. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL PROVIDE A REPORT TO THE CITY ON A FORM PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER CERTIFYING COMPLIANCE WITH SUBSECTION 1. WHEN THE FINAL PLUMBING INSPECTION IS PERFORMED BY THE CITY.\n    25→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed658f06-b65b-479d-b752-f47b92243df6","uuid":"6efaef75-9704-4772-9e88-4d327f42ed4a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/block-3.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Block 3\n\n## notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter 344 and other specific regulations.\n\nIRRIGATION NOTES:\nAUTOMATIC IRRIGATION SYSTEMS SHALL COMPLY WITH TCEQ CHAPTER 344, AS WELL AS THE FOLLOWING REQUIREMENTS:\n\n1. THESE REQUIREMENTS SHALL BE NOTED ON THE SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT AND SHALL BE IMPLEMENTED AS PART OF THE LANDSCAPE INSPECTION:\na. THE SYSTEM MUST PROVIDE A MOISTURE LEVEL ADEQUATE TO SUSTAIN GROWTH OF THE PLANT MATERIALS;\nb. THE SYSTEM DOES NOT INCLUDE SPRAY IRRIGATION ON AREAS LESS THAN TEN (10) FEET WIDE (SUCH AS MEDIANS, BUFFER STRIPS, AND PARKING LOT ISLANDS);\nc. CIRCUIT REMOTE CONTROL VALVES HAVE ADJUSTABLE FLOW CONTROLS;\nd. SERVICEABLE IN-HEAD CHECK VALVES AREA ADJACENT TO PAVED AREAS WHERE ELEVATION DIFFERENCES MAY CAUSE LOW HEAD DRAINAGE;\ne. A MASTER VALVE INSTALLED ON THE DISCHARGE SIDE OF THE BACKFLOW PREVENTER;\nf. ABOVE-GROUND IRRIGATION EMISSION DEVICES ARE SET BACK AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES FROM IMPERVIOUS SURFACES;\ng. AN AUTOMATIC RAIN SHUT-OFF DEVICE SHUTS OFF THE IRRIGATION SYSTEM AUTOMATICALLY AFTER MORE THAN A ONE-HALF INCH (1/2\") RAINFALL; AND\nh. NEWLY PLANTED TREES SHALL HAVE PERMANENT IRRIGATION CONSISTING OF DRIP OR BUBBLERS.\n\n2. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL DEVELOP AND PROVIDE AN AS-BUILT DESIGN PLAN TO THE CITY AT THE TIME THE FINAL IRRIGATION INSPECTION IS PERFORMED;\na. UNLESS FISCAL SECURITY IS PROVIDED TO THE CITY FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE SYSTEM, IT MUST BE OPERATIONAL AT THE TIME OF THE FINAL LANDSCAPE INSPECTION.\n\n3. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL ALSO PROVIDE EXHIBITS TO BE PERMANENTLY INSTALLED INSIDE OR ATTACHED TO THE IRRIGATION CONTROLLER, INCLUDING:\na. A LAMINATED COPY OF THE WATER BUDGET CONTAINING ZONE NUMBERS, PRECIPITATION RATE, GALLONS PER MINUTE AND THE LOCATION OF THE ISOLATION VALVE; AND AN AS BUILT PLAN.\n\n4. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL PROVIDE A REPORT TO THE CITY ON A FORM PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER CERTIFYING COMPLIANCE WITH SUBSECTION 1. WHEN THE FINAL PLUMBING INSPECTION IS PERFORMED BY THE CITY.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778189064332,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR257C87QJE0FE8FDM37S3SF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This block is about irrigation notes, not electrical clearances. Let me look at the actual visual representation more carefully. Let me ask the vision tool to provide more specific information about what I can see regarding distances and specific tree locations.\n\nActually, I think I have enough information now to make my evaluations. Let me summarize what I've learned:\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Line Present:** An OHE line runs along the southern boundary of the property\n\n2. **Trees in Proximity to OHE Line:** The landscape plan shows trees (mitigation trees marked \"M\" and existing trees) directly adjacent to or overlapping the OHE line per vision analysis\n\n3. **No Utility Compatibility Documentation:** The plant lists (Sheet 35) do not identify which trees are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F UC column\n\n4. **No Clearance Dimensions:** The landscape plan does not show any dimensions or clearances between trees and the OHE line\n\n5. **No Austin Energy Approval:** No documented written approval from Austin Energy is included in the plans for trees in proximity to the OHE line\n\n6. **Pad-Mounted Equipment:** At least one tree appears very close to the electrical pad in the street yard area\n\n7. **Missing Mature Height Data:** The plant schedules show \"minimum\" planting heights (16' for Live Oak and Cedar Elm) but do not specify mature heights per ECM Appendix F\n\n**Now let me evaluate each checklist item systematically:**\n\nI need to be very careful here. The grouping file provides specific thresholds:\n- Distribution lines: 15 feet minimum for non-utility-compatible trees, 25 feet for large trees (40+ feet)\n- Transmission lines: 50 feet minimum for all trees, utility-compatible required within zone\n- Poles: 10 feet minimum for all trees\n- Pad-mounted: 10 feet minimum for all trees\n- Underground: 5 feet minimum for all trees\n- 20 feet for underground: root barriers required\n\n\n- The core problem is that documentation is missing on utility compatibility status, mature growth specifications from ECM Appendix F, clearance measurements, and Austin Energy sign-off. Without these critical elements, I cannot confirm compliance. The visual evidence suggests trees positioned too close to the OHE line, which points toward a potential violation. I'll need to assign statuses based on what can and cannot be verified from the available documentation.\n\nFor items showing trees near the OHE line without documented utility compatibility, I should apply a FAIL designation since the burden rests on the applicant to affirmatively demonstrate they meet the requirements.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed658f06-b65b-479d-b752-f47b92243df6","uuid":"258dd24c-edb5-4df9-a162-c4ac180c053f"}
{"level":30,"time":1778189065988,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR257C87QJE0FE8FDM37S3SF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough research of the site plan and supporting documents, I can now evaluate each checklist item. Let me provide my findings:\n\n## Summary of Key Findings\n\n**Electric Infrastructure Present:**\n- Overhead Electric (OHE) line running along southern property boundary\n- Multiple pad-mounted transformers on the site\n- Underground electric distribution lines serving the buildings\n- No transmission facilities (distribution-level infrastructure only)\n\n**Tree Planting Plan:**\n- 2 Live Oak (minimum 16' height at planting)\n- 10 Cedar Elm (minimum 16' height at planting)  \n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (minimum 8' height at planting)\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (minimum 10' height at planting)\n- Various shrubs and groundcovers\n\n**Critical Deficiencies:**\n1. Plant schedule does NOT identify utility compatibility status per ECM Appendix F UC column\n2. Landscape plan does NOT show mature heights from ECM Appendix F\n3. Landscape plan shows trees with canopies overlapping/adjacent to OHE line but NO clearance dimensions\n4. At least one tree is drawn extremely close to transformer pad in street yard area\n5. No dimensions or callouts verifying clearances from tree trunk to utility facilities\n6. No documented Austin Energy written approval for trees in proximity to electric facilities\n7. No root barrier specifications shown for trees near underground equipment\n\nNow let me provide the structured output for fail/not-verifiable findings:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed658f06-b65b-479d-b752-f47b92243df6","uuid":"5d435049-98bf-4eac-8540-0f51a3be927b"}
{"level":30,"time":1778189086910,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR257C87QJE0FE8FDM37S3SF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ch2yNVJ7aDwSHDitAGkkJ3","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where OHE line is located","Street yard area where trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows trees (mitigation trees and existing trees) located directly adjacent to or overlapping the OHE line along the southern boundary. Plant schedule does not identify utility-compatible status per ECM Appendix F UC column for any of the proposed trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Mexican Redbud). Without documented utility compatibility designation and without clearance dimensions on the plans, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan depicts mitigation trees (M) and existing trees positioned adjacent to the OHE line along the southern property boundary, with tree canopy circles overlapping the line symbol per vision analysis. Sheet 35 plant schedule lists proposed species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but provides no UC designation or reference to ECM Appendix F utility compatibility status.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires non-utility-compatible trees be at least 15 feet from distribution conductors. The plans show trees adjacent to the OHE line but do not document the trees' utility-compatible status. The burden of demonstrating compliance rests on the applicant; without the UC designation documented, compliance cannot be verified from available evidence.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where OHE line is located","Street yard areas where shade trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows shade trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm, each with minimum 16-foot planting specification) proposed near the OHE line on the southern boundary. However, plant schedule does not specify mature heights per ECM Appendix F, which is required to determine if trees qualify as 'large' (40+ feet mature height) subject to the 25-foot clearance requirement from distribution conductors. Mature height from ECM Appendix F cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule specifies Live Oak (100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' HT minimum) and Cedar Elm (100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' HT minimum), showing only minimum planting heights. Sheet 31 shows these trees positioned adjacent to the OHE line. ECM Appendix F mature height classifications are not referenced on any sheet.","reasoning":"Large tree prohibition (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) cannot be determined without the ECM Appendix F mature height designation. The 16-foot minimum planting specification does not establish the ultimate mature height. Without documented mature height from ECM Appendix F, it cannot be verified whether these trees will exceed the 40-foot threshold and be subject to the 25-foot clearance requirement.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Street yard area on western side where electrical transformer pad is located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 electrical design plan shows a pad-mounted transformer in the western street yard area (upstream of the main site entrance). Sheet 31 landscape plan shows a street yard tree (marked SY) in the same general area with the tree's canopy circle drawn extremely close to or overlapping the transformer pad. No clearance dimension is provided. Minimum 10-foot clearance from tree trunk to pad-mounted equipment cannot be verified from available evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows a rectangular electrical transformer pad symbol in the western street yard area. Sheet 31 vision analysis indicates a street yard tree (SY) with its canopy circle overlapping this pad location. No dimensions are labeled showing clearance between tree trunk center and equipment.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires 10-foot minimum clearance between trees and pad-mounted equipment. The plans show a tree in proximity to a pad but do not dimension the actual distance. Without a dimensioned clearance or explicit statement of compliance, the requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed tree planting areas, particularly near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) and plant schedule (Sheet 35) do not differentiate large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) from smaller species. The plant schedule shows only minimum planting specifications (16' for Live Oak and Cedar Elm) without reference to their ECM Appendix F mature height classifications. Without this designation, it is not possible to verify whether clearance requirements for large trees near overhead facilities are being met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule lists species with planting heights and caliper specifications but no mature height from ECM Appendix F. Sheet 31 landscape plan does not use callouts or symbols to indicate which trees are classified as large (40+ feet mature) versus standard size.","reasoning":"The grouping specifies that large tree prohibition (40+ feet mature per ECM Appendix F) requires clear differentiation on plans to verify compliance with 25-foot clearances from distribution conductors. Without this designation, large trees cannot be distinguished from smaller species, and compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary where OHE line runs parallel to property line","Street yard areas where trees are in proximity to utility facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While the landscape plan does show the OHE utility line and trees in relation to it (both are depicted on Sheet 31), the plan fails to demonstrate compliance because no clearance dimensions are provided between tree trunk centers and the conductor line. Trees shown with canopies overlapping the OHE line position lack any dimensioned clearance verification. Reviewer cannot verify clearance compliance from the presented evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows both the OHE line and trees on the same drawing. Vision analysis confirms trees are depicted adjacent to/overlapping the OHE line. However, no dimension lines, distances in feet, or callouts verifying clearance requirements are present anywhere on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement is that trees are shown on landscape plans in relation to overhead facilities 'with sufficient clarity to verify clearances.' Showing trees adjacent to a utility line without dimensioning the actual distances from tree trunk to conductor does not satisfy this standard. The plan fails to provide clearance verification dimensions required to demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed in proximity to overhead electric facilities and pad-mounted equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan shows trees positioned adjacent to or overlapping the OHE line along the southern boundary and near the transformer pad in the street yard, but no documented written approval from Austin Energy is included in the submitted plans or supplementary documents authorizing these tree placements within the restricted electrical clearance zones. Without such approval, trees in these proximity zones constitute a regulatory violation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan visually depicts trees adjacent to the OHE line and in proximity to transformer pads. Review of supplementary documents (Master Comment Report, Engineer's Summary Letter, site plan set) reveals no attached correspondence, approval letters, or documented written authorization from Austin Energy permitting the proposed tree locations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 exceptions section states that variations to planting distances and utility compatibility require explicit written approval from Austin Energy. The grouping file identifies this as the required documentation path for trees in prohibited zones. No such approval documentation is present in the submitted materials.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Grep"]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed658f06-b65b-479d-b752-f47b92243df6","uuid":"45c92bbe-f424-450c-9874-68adbc99ea72"}
