{"level":30,"time":1778189102534,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR258CA01FRAXT6HK9WG7XVV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've provided the structured output with my findings. Let me now provide a summary of my evaluation to the user explaining the key findings and which items passed, which failed, and which were not-verifiable.\n\nItems I marked as PASS (not included in structured output as per requirements):\n- EL-2.2 (N/A - no transmission lines)\n- EL-2.4 (N/A - no transmission lines)\n- EL-2.5 (N/A - no transmission easement)\n- EL-2.6 (N/A - no specific pole violations documented, though poles may be present)\n- EL-2.8 (N/A - but should probably be not-verifiable based on lack of documentation)\n- EL-2.9 (N/A - insufficient evidence of underground equipment proximity requiring root barriers)\n- EL-2.10 (PASS - species are identified on plant schedule)\n- EL-2.12 (N/A - no clearances dimensioned at all, so cannot evaluate measurement methodology)\n- EL-2.13 (N/A - no clearances dimensioned at all, so cannot evaluate measurement methodology)\n\nWait, I need to reconsider some of these. Let me review:\n\nEL-2.2: Transmission - Facts.md indicates distribution infrastructure, no transmission mentioned. Actually, looking back at the facts, it says \"5' Electric Easements (×2)\" which are plat-dedicated easements. These could potentially be associated with distribution lines. The OHE line shown is distribution-level based on the grouping file's description of the infrastructure type. So EL-2.2 should be N/A.\n\nEL-2.4: Same - N/A (no transmission)\n\nEL-2.5: Transmission easement - Facts.md lists dedicated easements but none labeled as \"transmission\" easement. Only electric easements (5' each). The grouping specifically notes transmission easements would have \"dedicated easements with special p