{"level":30,"time":1778189139824,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR259JZB2FZDJJDCQBZWAV3Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete - EL-2 Grouping (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines)\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for the **EL-2 grouping** covering tree placement requirements near overhead electric distribution and transmission lines. \n\n### **Key Findings Summary**\n\n**Critical Issues Identified:**\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Infrastructure Present:** An OHE (overhead electric) line runs along the southern property boundary. The landscape plan shows multiple mitigation trees and existing trees positioned directly adjacent to or overlapping this line.\n\n2. **No Utility Compatibility Documentation:** The plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists proposed trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but provides NO designation of which are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F UC column. \n\n3. **No Clearance Verification:** The landscape plan shows trees adjacent to the OHE line but provides NO dimensions, callouts, or clearance measurements verifying compliance with the required 15-foot minimum separation for non-utility-compatible trees.\n\n4. **Missing Austin Energy Approval:** No written approval from Austin Energy is included in the submitted plans or supplementary documents to authorize the proposed tree locations within electrical clearance zones.\n\n5. **Pad-Mounted Equipment:** At least one street yard tree is drawn extremely close to a transformer pad in the western street yard area, with no clearance verification.\n\n6. **Mature Height Documentation Missing:** The plant schedule shows only minimum planting specifications (16' for Live Oak and Cedar Elm) but does not reference ECM Appendix F mature heights needed to determine if trees exceed the 40-foot threshold for large tree prohibitions.\n\n### **Evaluation Results**\n\n**Fail Items: 2**\n- **EL-2.14:** Trees not shown with sufficient clearance dimensions to verify compliance\n- **EL-2.15:** No documented Austin Energy written approval for trees in restricted clearance zones\n\n**Not-Verifiable Items: 6**\n- **EL-2.1:** Utility-compatible status not designated for proposed trees\n- **EL-2.3:** Mature heights per ECM Appendix F not documented to verify large tree restrictions\n- **EL-2.6:** Clearance dimensions to utility poles not provided\n- **EL-2.7:** Clearance dimensions to pad-mounted equipment not provided\n- **EL-2.8:** Underground equipment locations not identified on landscape plan\n- **EL-2.9:** Root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment not provided\n- **EL-2.11:** Large trees (40+ feet) not differentiated on plans\n\n**Pass Items: 1**\n- **EL-2.10:** Plant species are properly identified on the plant schedule\n\n**N/A Items: 5**\n- **EL-2.2, EL-2.4:** No transmission lines present (distribution infrastructure only)\n- **EL-2.5:** No transmission easement boundaries identified\n- **EL-2.12, EL-2.13:** No clearances dimensioned on plans (requirement only applies when clearances are shown)\n\nThe structured findings have been provided with specific citations, sheet references, and detailed explanations of each deficiency."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed658f06-b65b-479d-b752-f47b92243df6","uuid":"4bfb71eb-d214-4be1-964e-e5a10077772f"}
