y where OHE line is located","Street yard areas where shade trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows shade trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm, each with minimum 16-foot planting specification) proposed near the OHE line on the southern boundary. However, plant schedule does not specify mature heights per ECM Appendix F, which is required to determine if trees qualify as 'large' (40+ feet mature height) subject to the 25-foot clearance requirement from distribution conductors. Mature height from ECM Appendix F cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule specifies Live Oak (100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' HT minimum) and Cedar Elm (100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' HT minimum), showing only minimum planting heights. Sheet 31 shows these trees positioned adjacent to the OHE line. ECM Appendix F mature height classifications are not referenced on any sheet.","reasoning":"Large tree prohibition (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) cannot be determined without the ECM Appendix F mature height designation. The 16-foot minimum planting specification does not establish the ultimate mature height. Without documented mature height from ECM Appendix F, it cannot be verified whether these trees will exceed the 40-foot threshold and be subject to the 25-foot clearance requirement.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line along southern and western property boundaries where utility poles are located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric poles are present along the OHE line (shown on Sheet 21 and Sheet 31). Trees are shown on the landscape plan in proximity to these utility areas. However, the landscape plan does not dimension the clearance distances between individual trees and specific poles. Without clearance dimensions, the 10-foot minimum separation requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 identifies utility poles along the OHE line marked with pole symbols. Sheet 31 shows trees adjacent to the line where poles exist. However, no dimensions or callouts on Sheet 31 specify distances between tree trunk centers and individual poles.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires minimum 10 feet lateral distance from tree trunks to utility poles. While poles and trees are both shown on the landscape plan, the lack of dimensioned clearances prevents verification of compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Street yard area on western side where electrical transformer pad is located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 electrical design plan shows a pad-mounted transformer in the western street yard area. Sheet 31 landscape plan shows a street yard tree (marked SY) in the same general area with the tree's canopy circle drawn extremely close to or overlapping the transformer pad. No clearance dimension is provided. Minimum 10-foot clearance from tree trunk to pad-mounted equipment cannot be verified from available evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows a rectangular electrical transformer pad symbol in the western street yard area. Sheet 31 vision analysis indicates a street yard tree (SY) with its canopy circle overlapping this pad location. No dimensions are labeled showing clearance between tree trunk center and equipment.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires 10-foot minimum clearance between trees and pad-mounted equipment. The plans show a tree in proximity to a pad but do not dimension the actual distance. Without a dimensioned clearance or explicit statement of compliance, the requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where underground electric lines and equipment are located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electric lines are shown on the landscape plan (marked as '- E -' on Sheet 31). However, the specific locations of underground electric equipment (pull boxes, vaults, buried transformers, etc.) are not clearly identified on the landscape plan. Without identified equipment locations and without dimensioned clearances, the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows underground electric line (E) entering from the western street boundary and routing through the site. Sheet 21 electrical design shows pull boxes and underground routing. However, Sheet 31 landscape plan does not specifically callout pull box locations or other underground equipment that would be subject to the 5-foot clearance requirement.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires 5-foot minimum lateral distance from tree trunks to underground electric equipment. The landscape plan must clearly identify such equipment locations to verify compliance. Without such identification and dimensioning, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where trees are proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electric equipment locations are not clearly identified on the landscape plan. Therefore, it cannot be determined which proposed trees fall within the 20-foot proximity zone requiring root barriers. Additionally, no root barrier specifications are shown on the landscape plan or in the landscape notes. Without identified equipment locations and without documented root barrier specifications, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electric routing and pull boxes, but these specific locations are not transferred to or dimensioned on Sheet 31 landscape plan. Sheet 35 landscape notes do not include root barrier specifications for trees near underground utilities. No callouts on Sheet 31 indicate where root barriers are required or provided.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires 4-foot deep root barriers positioned 5 feet from underground equipment for trees within 20 feet. The landscape plan must clearly identify which trees require this mitigation and must show the root barrier specifications. Without equipment location identification on the landscape plan and without root barrier details, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed tree planting areas, particularly near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) and plant schedule (Sheet 35) do not differentiate large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) from smaller species. The plant schedule shows only minimum planting specifications (16' for Live Oak and Cedar Elm) without reference to their ECM Appendix F mature height classifications. Without this designation, it is not possible to verify whether clearance requirements for large trees near overhead facilities are being met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule lists species with planting heights and caliper specifications but no mature height from ECM Appendix F. Sheet 31 landscape plan does not use callouts or symbols to indicate which trees are classified as large (40+ feet mature) versus standard size.","reasoning":"The grouping specifies that large tree prohibition (40+ feet mature per ECM Appendix F) requires clear differentiation on plans to verify compliance with 25-foot clearances from distribution conductors. Without this designation, large trees cannot be distinguished from smaller species, and compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary where OHE line runs parallel to property line","Street yard areas where trees are in proximity to utility facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While the landscape plan does show the OHE utility line and trees in relation to it (both are depicted on Sheet 31), the plan fails to demonstrate compliance because no clearance dimensions are provided between tree trunk centers and the conductor line. Trees shown with canopies overlapping the OHE line position lack any dimensioned clearance verification. Reviewer cannot verify clearance compliance from the presented evidence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows both the OHE line and trees on the same drawing. Vision analysis confirms trees are depicted adjacent to/overlapping the OHE line. However, no dimension lines, distances in feet, or callouts verifying clearance requirements are present anywhere on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement is that trees are shown on landscape plans in relation to overhead facilities 'with sufficient clarity to verify clearances.' Showing trees adjacent to a utility line without dimensioning the actual distances from tree trunk to conductor does not satisfy this standard. The plan fails to provide clearance verification dimensions required to demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Read"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed in proximity to overhead electric facilities and pad-mounted equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan shows trees positioned adjacent to or overlapping the OHE line along the southern boundary and near the transformer pad in the street yard, but no documented written approval from Austin Energy is included in the submitted plans or supplementary documents authorizing these tree placements within the restricted electrical clearance zones. Without such approval, trees in these proximity zones constitute a regulatory violation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan visually depicts trees adjacent to the OHE line and in proximity to transformer pads. Review of supplementary documents (Master Comment Report, Engineer's Summary Letter, site plan set) reveals no attached correspondence, approval letters, or documented written authorization from Austin Energy permitting the proposed tree locations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 exceptions section states that variations to planting distances and utility compatibility require explicit written approval from Austin Energy. The grouping file identifies this as the required documentation path for trees in prohibited zones. No such approval documentation is present in the submitted materials.","tools_used":["Read","mcp__conductor_tools__vision","Grep"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"96ae4e08-845b-4d60-8605-6a78c170bafe"}
