ion indicates most findings were flagged consistently across runs, with Comments 1-8 and 10-11 showing strong confidence levels.\n\nKey attention areas include obtaining necessary approvals from Austin Energy Design, confirming equipment specifications that affect clearances and drainage, verifying utility line locations, and conducting full vertical coordination. There's a critical flag around undisclosed easements requiring legal review and site plan updates. Tree species selection also needs coordination with landscape architecture.\n\nThe formatting review confirms all headlines stay within the 3-12 word range, summaries remain concise at 25-35 words, technical details are preserved without redundancy, citations are properly deduplicated, and zone nomenclature follows canonical standards. The consolidation is complete.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"420720f1-c8ef-4630-b41e-df044b1b2b62","uuid":"a7354594-2c18-4dd2-99c2-58a0523af98b"}
{"level":30,"time":1778189338668,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"13.json","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR25FHJZXAHAZA47136Y31CB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully synthesized 38 electrical infrastructure findings into **11 structured comments** (including 1 severity-0 notation), achieving a **3.5:1 consolidation ratio**. \n\n**Key patterns consolidated:**\n\n1. **Missing Design Specifications** (Comment 1) — Transformer pad detail sheets and dimensions\n2. **Building Clearances** (Comment 2) — 5-foot standard to buildings, balconies, windows, retaining walls, and fences\n3. **Access & Equipment Clearances** (Comment 3) — Hot-stick use area, vegetation setbacks, vertical clearances\n4. **Horizontal Utility Clearances** (Comment 4) — Water, wastewater, storm drain, gas, underground utilities, overhead lines\n5. **Vertical Utility Coordination** (Comment 5) — Cross-installation, inverts, depths\n6. **Equipment Specifications** (Comment 6) — Oil-filled vs. dry-type; drainage direction  \n7. **Property & Easements** (Comment 7) — **CRITICAL:** Undisclosed easements (Instruments 2010070731 & 2011021137) must be depicted; transformer easements required\n8. **Tree Compatibility** (Comment 8) — ECM Appendix F utility compatibility; root barriers\n9. **Site Circulation Protection** (Comment 9) — Sidewalk clearances, bollards, inter-pad spacing, fire lanes, hydrants, light poles, bicycle parking, stairwells\n10. **Niche Service** (Comment 10) — Conditional configuration details (35-foot clearance, 3-hour fire rating)\n11. **Fire Escapes** (Comment 11) — Severity 0 (not applicable — no fire escapes on site)\n\n**All 38 findings are accounted for**, with per-run comments preserved verbatim and all citations, sheet numbers, and locations retained. High-severity items (1-2, 4, 7) focus on critical code compliance gaps; medium-severity items flag missing documentation; low-severity items address conditional or administrative requirements."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"420720f1-c8ef-4630-b41e-df044b1b2b62","uuid":"b0789d74-83a8-4519-a18e-c7d8b12a02d9"}
{"level":30,"time":1778189338700,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"13.json","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":195842,"duration_api_ms":195714,"num_turns":4,"result":"---\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully synthesized 38 electrical infrastructure findings into **11 structured comments** (including 1 severity-0 notation), achieving a **3.5:1 consolidation ratio**. \n\n**Key patterns consolidated:**\n\n1. **Missing Design Specifications** (Comment 1) — Transformer pad detail sheets and dimensions\n2. **Building Clearances** (Comment 2) — 5-foot standard to buildings, balconies, windows, retaining walls, and fences\n3. **Access & Equipment Clearances** (Comment 3) — Hot-stick use area, vegetation setbacks, vertical clearances\n4. **Horizontal Utility Clearances** (Comment 4) — Water, wastewater, storm drain, gas, underground utilities, overhead lines\n5. **Vertical Utility Coordination** (Comment 5) — Cross-installation, inverts, depths\n6. **Equipment Specifications** (Comment 6) — Oil-filled vs. dry-type; drainage direction  \n7. **Property & Easements** (Comment 7) — **CRITICAL:** Undisclosed easements (Instruments 2010070731 & 2011021137) must be depicted; transformer easements required\n8. **Tree Compatibility** (Comment 8) — ECM Appendix F utility compatibility; root barriers\n9. **Site Circulation Protection** (Comment 9) — Sidewalk clearances, bollards, inter-pad spacing, fire lanes, hydrants, light poles, bicycle parking, stairwells\n10. **Niche Service** (Comment 10) — Conditional configuration details (35-foot clearance, 3-hour fire rating)\n11. **Fire Escapes** (Comment 11) — Severity 0 (not applicable — no fire escapes on site)\n\n**All 38 findings are accounted for**, with per-run comments preserved verbatim and all citations, sheet numbers, and locations retained. High-severity items (1-2, 4, 7) focus on critical code compliance gaps; medium-severity items flag missing documentation; low-severity items address conditional or administrative requirements.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"420720f1-c8ef-4630-b41e-df044b1b2b62","total_cost_usd":0.198217,"usage":{"input_tokens":2978,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50032,"cache_read_input_tokens":104090,"output_tokens":24458,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":50032},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2978,"outputTokens":24458,"cacheReadInputTokens":104090,"cacheCreationInputTokens":50032,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.198217,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"comments":[{"headline":"Missing Austin Energy transformer pad detail sheets","summary":"No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided or referenced on any plans. Transformer pad dimensions are not specified. Without pad details and equipment specifications, compliance with UCM § 1.18.0 cannot be verified.","sheets":[21],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Energy Design (consultation and detail approval)","attn":"Applicant must obtain AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets and confirm whether service is single-phase or three-phase. All four pads require detailed specifications.","details":[{"text":"No transformer pad dimensions (length × width) are shown on any submitted plan or detail sheet. Reference callouts to AE Design standard details are not present on electrical plan Sheet 21.","citation":"UCM § 1.5.2.6; UCM § 1.18.0","sourceId":"13:EL-13.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pad locations but provides no dimensions (length x width). No reference callouts or detail reference bubbles direct readers to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets. No specification of service type (single-phase or three-phase) is provided. Required transformer pad dimensions and AE Design detail references matching the specified service type are not documented."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No transformer pad dimensions are shown on any submitted plan or detail sheet, and no Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are included. Applicant must obtain from Austin Energy Design the transformer pad detail sheets corresponding to the specified service type (single-phase or three-phase) and provide: (1) dimensioned pad configuration details; (2) equipment specifications including transformer ratings and pad dimensions; (3) confirmation of compliance with AE Design requirements; (4) reference callouts on electrical plan sheet 21 to applicable AE Design standard details."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided or referenced. Transformer pad dimensions are not specified on the electrical design plan. The UCM § 1.5.2.6 and § 1.18.0 require that pad dimensions match AE Design-approved specifications for the proposed service type (single-phase or three-phase). Without these details, the adequacy and compliance of pad installation cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer clearances to buildings not dimensioned","summary":"No dimensional clearance documentation exists for transformer pads relative to buildings, retaining walls, balconies, fences, or windows/doors. Standard 5-foot clearances (or reduced 3-foot clearances to masonry with conditions) cannot be verified. Building elevation and cross-section details are not provided.","sheets":[9,21],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"Applicant must provide dimensioned clearances from all four transformer pads to each adjacent building element, and confirm whether reduced 3-foot clearances to masonry buildings are proposed (if so, conditions must be met and documented). Equipment type (oil-filled vs dry-type) affects window/door clearance rules.","details":[{"text":"No dimension lines show distance from transformer pads to building edges. Minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to adjacent building structures cannot be verified from submitted plans.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.1","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pad locations but provides no dimension lines or callout notes showing clearance distances from any transformer pad to adjacent buildings. No detail references or specifications provided. Minimum 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified from submitted plans."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad locations are identified on the electrical plan, but no dimensions are provided showing clearances to buildings. Applicant must provide dimensioned site plan showing minimum 5-foot clearance from edge of transformer pad to all building footprints and structures."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad locations shown on electrical plan but clearance distances to buildings are not dimensioned. Visual estimation from the 1\" = 20' scale suggests approximately 5-8 feet from building walls, but precise dimensions are required to verify compliance with the minimum 5-foot clearance requirement from building edges."}]},{"text":"No dimension lines measure clearance distances from transformer pads to retaining walls. 5-foot minimum clearance cannot be verified from submitted evidence.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.2","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows retaining walls around the property perimeter. Transformer pad locations are shown, but no dimension lines measure clearance distances from any transformer pad to adjacent retaining walls. The 5-foot minimum clearance from retaining walls cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are present on site but clearance distances from transformer pads are not dimensioned. Provide dimensioned plan showing minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to all retaining wall structures."}]},{"text":"No dimension lines show clearance distances from pads to adjacent balconies or building overhangs. Vertical elevations or cross-sections are not provided. 5-foot clearance to balconies cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.5","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"The site plan shows building footprints and transformer pad locations, but no vertical elevations or cross-sections are provided for the transformer pad areas showing whether balconies or building overhangs exist above or adjacent to any pad. Additionally, no dimension lines show clearance distances. Compliance cannot be verified from available evidence."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No cross-section drawings or building elevation details provided showing vertical clearances from transformer pads to building balconies, overhangs, or structures. Provide architectural cross-sections for each transformer location demonstrating minimum 5-foot lateral clearance from balconies/overhangs and confirmation that no structures cover pad areas."}]},{"text":"No building elevation sheets showing windows, doors, or ventilating ducts relative to transformer pad locations. Clearance dimensions from pads to these building openings are not provided. 12-foot horizontal clearance requirement (for oil-filled equipment with inadequate lateral separation) cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.6","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets showing window/door/duct locations relative to transformer pads were provided. No dimension lines show clearance distances from pads to windows, doors, or ventilating ducts. Specification of transformer equipment as oil-filled or dry-type was not provided. Compliance with the 12-foot horizontal clearance requirement for oil-filled equipment with inadequate lateral separation cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation drawings are not provided. Applicant must submit: (1) building elevation details showing all windows, doors, and ventilating ducts adjacent to transformer locations; (2) confirmation of oil-filled vs. dry-type equipment; (3) dimensional clearance analysis demonstrating 12-foot horizontal clearance when lateral separation is less than 5 feet or when openings are less than 12 feet from grade."}]},{"text":"No dimension lines identify which sides of pads have operators/controls (requiring 5-foot fence clearance) versus sides without (requiring 3-foot clearance). Fence clearances cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.3","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows wooden privacy fences around property perimeter and parking areas. No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pads to fence lines. No callouts identify which sides of transformer pads have operators/controls (requiring 5-foot clearance) versus sides without operators/controls (requiring 3-foot clearance). The required fence clearances cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"No documentation of whether reduced 3-foot clearances to brick/masonry buildings are proposed. If reduced clearances are intended, conditions (not in confined space, 10+ ft to windows/doors/ducts, 15+ ft vertical clearance, 3-hour fire rating) must be met and Austin Energy Design written approval must be provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.4","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any sheets. Therefore, it cannot be determined whether reduced 3-foot clearances (to brick/masonry buildings) were proposed, or whether the conditions for the reduction exception (not in confined space, 10 ft+ to windows/doors/ducts, 15 ft+ vertical clearance, 3-hour fire rating) were met. If reduced clearances were intended, evidence of Austin Energy Design written approval is not present in submitted documentation."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer pad access clearances and vegetation not documented","summary":"Transformer pad access door orientations are not identified on any plans. 10-foot hot-stick use area clearances and required vegetation setbacks (10 feet from access door, 5 feet from other sides) cannot be verified. No cross-sections show vertical clearances to overhead structures or building overhangs.","sheets":[9,21,31],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Energy Design (equipment orientation confirmation); City Arborist / Parks (vegetation management)","attn":"Applicant must obtain and reference AE Design-approved pad detail sheets showing access door orientation. Provide dimensioned site and landscape plans showing clearances from each pad's access door. Landscape plan must show all vegetation within 15 feet of each pad.","details":[{"text":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads but does not indicate which side is the access door. No dimension lines show clearance distances from the access door side to open areas or adjacent buildings. 10-foot hot-stick use area clearance requirement cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.10","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not indicate which side of each pad is the access door. No dimension lines show clearance distances from the access door side to open areas or adjacent buildings. The 10-foot hot-stick use area clearance requirement cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad equipment specifications, access door orientations, and clearance dimensions are not provided on the electrical plan. Applicant must provide: (1) Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets identifying access door location; (2) dimensioned site plan showing minimum 10-foot clearance from access door side to adjacent open areas or structures."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan but their orientation and access door locations are not indicated. Without knowing which side of each pad contains the access door (hot-stick use area), the required 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Landscape Plan shows vegetation but does not dimension clearance distances from shrubs/low-lying plants to transformer pads. Required 10-foot clearance from access door side and 5-foot clearance from other sides cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.14","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape Plan shows plantings and shrubs around the site. No dimension lines measure clearance distances from transformer pads to shrubs or low-lying vegetation. The 10-foot clearance from the access door side and 5-foot clearance from other sides cannot be verified. Additionally, transformer pad access door orientation is not identified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows vegetation areas but does not dimension shrub and low-lying vegetation clearances to transformer pads. Applicant must provide: (1) equipment detail sheets showing access door orientation on each transformer pad; (2) dimensioned landscape plan showing minimum 10-foot clearance from access door side and minimum 5-foot clearance from other sides to all proposed shrubs and low-lying vegetation."}]},{"text":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead structures, building overhangs, parking garage slabs, or enclosed areas above pads. Confined space configuration cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.31","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas adjacent to or above transformer pad locations. If such vertical obstructions exist, required clearance documentation is missing."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead structures, building overhangs, or parking garage slabs. Applicant must provide cross-section drawings for each transformer location (taken perpendicular to and through the transformer pad) showing vertical clearances to any overhead building elements, parking structures, or enclosed areas."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances through transformer pad locations are not provided in the plan set. Verification of clearances to overhead structures, building overhangs, parking garage ceilings, or enclosed areas above transformer locations cannot be made without profile/cross-section views."}]}]},{"headline":"Horizontal utility clearances not dimensioned","summary":"Dimension lines do not document required horizontal clearance distances from transformer pads to water lines (5 feet), wastewater lines (5 feet), storm drain lines (5 feet), gas lines (24-36 inches per pressure), underground utilities (12 inches), or overhead distribution conductors (7.5-15 feet). Utility coordination plan is not provided.","sheets":[12,19,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Water, Watershed Protection, Austin Energy (utility coordination and spacing approval)","attn":"Applicant must submit detailed utility coordination drawing (plan and cross-section views) showing all utilities with explicit horizontal (and vertical) dimensions relative to each transformer pad. Gas pressure specifications and overhead conductor locations must be confirmed.","details":[{"text":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and water lines on site but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances. 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from water lines cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.21","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and water lines on the site, but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances from transformer pads to water lines. The 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from water lines cannot be verified from available evidence."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Water lines are routed directly adjacent to transformer pad edges at multiple locations, providing insufficient clearance. Relocate water lines to maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from all transformer pad edges, or relocate transformer pads to maintain clearance. Provide dimensioned utility coordination plan showing all water lines at minimum 5 feet from transformer pad perimeters."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Water line routing is shown on the utility tap plan (Sheet 19) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) but the horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and water service lines are not dimensioned. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified without explicit dimensions."}]},{"text":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and wastewater lines but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances. 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from wastewater lines cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.22","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and wastewater lines on the site, but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances from transformer pads to wastewater lines. The 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from wastewater lines cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Wastewater line routes are shown but clearance dimensions to transformer pads are not provided. Applicant must provide dimensioned utility coordination plan showing minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from wastewater lines to all transformer pad edges."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Wastewater line routing is shown on utility plans and electrical plan but horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and wastewater service lines are not dimensioned. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and Sheet 12 shows storm drain routing but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances. 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from storm drains cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.23","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations and Sheet 12 shows storm drain routing on the site, but no dimension lines measure horizontal clearance distances from transformer pads to storm drain lines. The 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from storm drains cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Storm drain line routes are shown but clearance dimensions to transformer pads are not provided. Applicant must provide dimensioned utility coordination plan showing minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from storm drain lines to all transformer pad edges."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Storm drain line routing is shown on grading and drainage plans (Sheet 12) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) but horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and storm drain lines are not dimensioned. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad and underground utility routing but no dimension lines measure the 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from pads to other underground utilities. Compliance with UCM § 1.10.5.A separation requirements cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.A","sourceId":"13:EL-13.25","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and underground utility lines, but no dimension lines measure the 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities. Compliance with UCM § 1.10.5.A separation requirements cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility line routing is shown in plan view but specific horizontal and vertical clearance dimensions are not provided. Applicant must provide detailed utility coordination drawing showing all existing and proposed utilities with specific measurements (horizontal and vertical) demonstrating minimum 12-inch clearance from transformer pad and underground electrical infrastructure to all other utilities."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility routing (electrical, water, wastewater, storm drain, telephone) is shown on various plan sheets but the horizontal and vertical clearance distances between transformer pads and other underground utilities are not dimensioned. Minimum 12-inch clearance (horizontal and vertical) cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines at property boundaries but no dimension lines show distance from transformer pad locations to overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors. 15-foot radius clearance requirement cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.28","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines at property boundaries. No dimension lines show distances from transformer pad locations to overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors. The 15-foot radius clearance requirement (measured from conductors) cannot be verified from submitted evidence."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution primary and neutral conductor locations are not shown on the submitted electrical plan. The required 15-foot radius clearance (measured from the conductor centerline, not pole centerline) cannot be verified without identifying the specific overhead line locations and conductor positions."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines but no dimension lines identify them or measure sky-to-ground clearance from transformer pad locations. 7.5-foot minimum clearance from overhead distribution line conductors cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.27","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines labeled 'OHE' along property boundaries, but no transformer pads appear to be located under or directly adjacent to these lines. No 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance dimension lines are shown. If transformer pads are positioned within the 7.5-foot clearance area, this would require verification."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution line locations are not clearly identified on the electrical design plan. The required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution line conductors cannot be verified. The electrical notes reference consultation with Austin Energy Design regarding overhead lines but overhead line routing is not shown on the submitted plans."}]},{"text":"Grading and utility plans show gas infrastructure but horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and gas lines are not dimensioned. Gas pressure specifications are not provided. 24-inch (low-pressure) or 36-inch (high-pressure) minimum clearance cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.A","sourceId":"13:EL-13.24","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Grading and utility plans show gas infrastructure on the site but the horizontal clearance distances between transformer pads and gas lines are not dimensioned. The required minimum clearance (24 inches for low-pressure, 36 inches for high-pressure) cannot be verified without explicit dimensions or pressure specifications."}]}]},{"headline":"Vertical utility coordination and cross-installation not shown","summary":"No cross-section drawings or elevation views with invert elevations document whether transformer pads or Austin Energy underground facilities are located over or under other utility lines. No sections confirm that customer structures are not installed over AE underground facilities. Vertical coordination is shown only in plan view.","sheets":[19,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Water, Watershed Protection, Austin Energy (utility coordination and conflict resolution)","attn":"Applicant must provide detailed vertical utility coordination showing invert elevations, pipe depths, and cross-section drawings for all transformer pad locations and underground electrical routing relative to all other utilities.","details":[{"text":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and underground utility routing in plan view only. No cross-section drawings or elevation views with inverts/depths confirm whether pads or AE underground facilities are located over or under other utility lines. Vertical coordination cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.B","sourceId":"13:EL-13.26","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads and underground utility routing. No cross-section drawings or elevation views confirm whether transformer pads or Austin Energy underground facilities are located over or under other utility lines, or whether customer structures are installed over AE underground facilities. Compliance cannot be verified from available evidence."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility coordination shown in plan view only without vertical component (inverts, depths, cross-sections). Applicant must provide detailed vertical utility coordination showing all utilities with invert elevations, pipe depths, and cross-section drawings demonstrating that no transformer pads or underground electrical facilities are located over or under other utility lines, and that no building foundations or structures will be installed over electrical facilities."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Cross-installation of utilities (customer buildings/structures installed over or under AE underground facilities, or AE facilities installed over/under customer utilities) cannot be verified from the submitted plan set. Underground utility coordination details and cross-section drawings showing relative elevations are not provided."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines and transformer locations but no cross-section drawings confirm that customer structures (buildings, light poles, signs, antennas) are not installed under Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. Vertical clearance verification is not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.39","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines along property boundaries and transformer locations. No cross-section drawings or vertical clearance documentation confirms that customer structures (buildings, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks) are not installed under Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. Vertical clearance verification is not provided."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer equipment type and drainage not specified","summary":"Transformer specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type) are not documented on the electrical plan. Grading plan shows contours but does not confirm surface drainage direction relative to transformer pads or whether drainage slopes away from buildings if oil-filled equipment is proposed. Drainage compliance cannot be verified.","sheets":[11,21],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Energy Design (equipment type confirmation and grading approval)","attn":"Applicant must specify transformer equipment type (oil-filled or dry-type) in electrical plan notes. If oil-filled, provide detailed grading and drainage plan showing surface slopes directing liquid flow away from adjacent buildings.","details":[{"text":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical design plan or in notes. Grading plan shows surface contours and drainage arrows but does not explicitly confirm liquid drainage (if applicable) is directed away from buildings. Drainage requirement cannot be verified without equipment type specification.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1","sourceId":"13:EL-13.32","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type) are not documented on the electrical plan. Grading and drainage plans show contours but do not show surface flow direction relative to transformer pad locations, particularly whether drainage slopes toward or away from buildings. If oil-filled equipment is installed, proper grading to ensure liquid flow away from building cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Oil-filled vs. dry-type equipment not specified on electrical plan. Detailed grading around transformer pads not provided. Applicant must: (1) confirm whether equipment will be oil-filled or dry-type; (2) if oil-filled, provide detailed grading and drainage plan showing surface slopes around each transformer pad directing liquid flow away from adjacent buildings."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical design plan or in the electrical notes. The grading plan shows surface contours and drainage flow arrows but does not explicitly confirm that liquid drainage (if applicable for oil-filled equipment) is directed away from buildings. Without equipment type specification, the drainage requirement cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer pad property encumbrances and easement conflicts","summary":"Transformer pad locations are not dimensioned relative to easement boundaries or verified as 100% on private property. Critical undisclosed easements documented in facts.md (Instruments 2010070731 and 2011021137) are not depicted on site plan. Proposed transformer easements are not shown. Electrical routing is not confirmed on private property. Cross-department coordination required.","sheets":[2,9,21],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Property / Legal (easement documentation and title verification); Watershed Protection (drainage easement coordination); Austin Energy Design (transformer easement requirements)","attn":"CRITICAL: Per facts.md, two perpetual easements (Greenbelt Access 2010070731 and City Drainage 2011021137) covering ~0.44 acres in NE area must be added to site plan before approval. Applicant must also verify additional plat-dedicated easements (Cortez Heights, Trico Subdivision) and confirm no transformer pads or electrical routing conflict with them.","details":[{"text":"Transformer pad locations relative to easement boundaries are not clearly dimensioned. Facts.md identifies two critical undisclosed perpetual easements (Instruments 2010070731 — Greenbelt Access, 0.31 ac; 2011021137 — City Drainage, 0.13 ac) in NE area not depicted on site plan. Total ~0.44 acres must be shown before approval.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4; easement-specific regulations","sourceId":"13:EL-13.34","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Plat and Site Plans show easement callouts (drainage, water, wastewater, electrical). No explicit notation confirms whether any transformer pad is located within prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines). No Austin Energy Design written approval for pad placement in easements is documented."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad locations relative to easement boundaries are not clearly dimensioned or verified. Facts.md documents two critical undepicted easements in NE area that must be added to site plan before approval. Applicant must: (1) clearly show all easement boundaries on electrical plan with transformer locations dimensioned relative to easement edges; (2) confirm no transformer pads are located in drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements, or provide Austin Energy Design written approval for any proposed locations; (3) add missing greenbelt access easement and drainage easement to site plan exhibits."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pads must not be located in prohibited easements (drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines) without written Austin Energy Design approval. Transformer pad locations are not dimensioned relative to the documented easements. Facts.md identifies that two critical easements (Instruments 2010070731 and 2011021137) are not depicted on the site plan. Additional plat-dedicated easements (Cortez Heights and Trico Subdivision easements) are also not verified on the submitted site plan."}]},{"text":"Transformer easements (required for Austin Energy Design accessibility and maintenance) are not shown on electrical or site plans. Width and AE Design approval documentation are not provided. UCM § 1.10.3 requires transformer easements with width determined by AE Design on project-specific basis.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.35","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Easement callouts appear on plat and site plan boundary areas (drainage, water, electrical), but no specific transformer pad easement callouts or dimensions are shown on the electrical plan. Easement width adequate for Austin Energy accessibility requirements cannot be verified from submitted evidence."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No transformer easements are shown on any submitted plan sheet. Applicant must provide easement exhibit showing transformer easements of adequate width around all four transformer pad locations. Submit Austin Energy Design specifications for required easement width and coordinate with AE Design business unit for appropriate easement configuration and recording requirements."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on the electrical or site plans. The UCM § 1.10.3 and associated regulations require transformer easements around pads for Austin Energy Design accessibility and maintenance, with width determined by AE Design on a project-specific basis. No easement boundaries, widths, or AE Design approval documentation are provided in the submitted plans."}]},{"text":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to building service meters is shown but not dimensioned or verified to remain 100% on private property. Routing is not confirmed to be outside public right-of-way and utility easements.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.36","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Complete electrical routing from transformers to service meters is not clearly shown or verified to be 100% on private property. Applicant must provide detailed electrical routing plan with property boundary overlay showing the complete path from each transformer pad to its corresponding building service meter, confirming all routing remains on private property and outside public right-of-way and utility easements."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters must be 100% on private property. The routing is shown on the electrical plan but routing paths are not dimensioned or explicitly labeled to confirm they do not cross right-of-way, easements, or other properties."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows property lines and transformer pad locations but no dimension lines or callout notes specifically confirm that all transformer pads are located 100% on private property (not straddling property lines). Correlation to transformer positions requires explicit callouts not present on electrical plan.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.33","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows property lines and transformer pad locations. No dimension lines or callout notes specifically confirm that all transformer pads are located 100% on private property (not straddling property lines). Plat sheet shows property boundaries, but correlation to transformer pad positions requires explicit callouts not present on electrical plan."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Property lines are shown on the site and electrical plans, but transformer pad locations are not dimensioned or labeled to explicitly confirm they are 100% located on private property and not straddling property lines. Additionally, facts.md identifies critical undisclosed easements not depicted on the site plan that may affect the property availability for transformer pad installation."}]}]},{"headline":"Trees not confirmed utility-compatible and root barriers missing","summary":"Existing and proposed trees within 10-15 lateral feet of transformer pads are not confirmed as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F. Tree species cannot be positively identified. No root barrier details are provided for trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment. Root barriers require 4-foot depth and 5-foot offset per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","sheets":[30,31,32,37],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"City Arborist / Parks (tree species identification and utility compatibility); Landscape Architecture (root barrier design details)","attn":"Applicant must identify all trees within 20 feet of transformer pads by species. Provide ECM Appendix F utility-compatible designations ('UC' column) for each species. Provide root barrier detail sheets (4-foot depth, 5-foot offset) for all trees within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment.","details":[{"text":"Landscape Plan (Sheets 31-32) shows plantings and proposed tree locations but no dimension lines measure clearance distances from trees to transformer pads. Tree species are listed but verification that species within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F 'UC' column cannot be confirmed without dimensioned clearances.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4; ECM Appendix F","sourceId":"13:EL-13.13","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and Tree List (Sheet 32) identify proposed trees and plantings. Dimension lines from any trees to transformer pad locations are not provided. Tree species are listed, but verification that trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F 'UC' column cannot be confirmed without dimensioned clearances from trees to electrical equipment."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Landscape plan shows mitigation trees and landscaping areas but does not identify specific proposed tree species or provide utility-compatible designations per ECM Appendix F. Applicant must submit proposed planting schedule listing all tree species (botanical and common names) with verification that species within 10 lateral feet of transformer pads are ECM Appendix F utility-compatible ('UC' designation)."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing trees are located within 10-15 lateral feet of transformer pads. Transformer Pad 1 has a tree estimated at 10-15 feet distance; Transformer Pad 3 has a tree within 5-10 feet. The tree species cannot be positively identified or confirmed as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F from the submitted plans. Tree identification numbers are not clearly labeled on the electrical or site plan in proximity to transformer locations."}]},{"text":"Landscape Plan shows proposed trees and plantings but no dimension lines measure distances from trees to transformer pad locations or underground electrical equipment. No root barrier details or specifications are provided. 4-foot depth and 5-foot offset from equipment requirement cannot be verified for trees within 20 lateral feet.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.15","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape Plan shows proposed trees and plantings. No dimension lines measure distances from trees to transformer pad locations or underground electric equipment. No root barrier details or specifications are shown on landscape or detail sheets. If trees are located within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment, required root barrier specifications (4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No root barrier details are shown on landscape or construction detail sheets. Applicant must provide root barrier detail sheets showing minimum 4-foot depth and 5-foot offset from underground electrical equipment for all trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads and underground electrical routing."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer pad circulation and parking protection not documented","summary":"Multiple site circulation and protective clearance requirements are not dimensioned: sidewalk clearances (2 feet), bollard/parking protection (4-foot threshold), inter-pad clearances (5 feet), fire lane clearances (15 feet), fire hydrant clearances (5 feet), light pole clearances (5 feet), bicycle parking clearances (5 feet), and fire exit stairwell clearances (5 feet). Dimension lines are not provided for any of these elements.","sheets":[9,10,21,31],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Fire Department (fire lane and exit access coordination); Parks / Landscape (light poles and bicycle parking location coordination)","attn":"Applicant must provide dimensioned site plan showing all clearance requirements. Identify which internal driveways serve as fire lanes. Confirm whether transformer pads within 4 feet of parking areas — if so, provide bollard details (4-inch diameter galvanized rigid metal per AE Design specs).","details":[{"text":"Site plan shows sidewalk locations and transformer pad locations but no dimension lines measure distance from transformer pad edges to back of sidewalks. 2-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified from dimensioned evidence.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.7","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows sidewalk locations and transformer pad locations, but no dimension lines measure the distance from transformer pad edges to back of sidewalks. The 2-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified from dimensioned evidence."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sidewalk locations are shown on site plan but clearance distances to transformer pads are not dimensioned. Provide dimensioned plan showing minimum 2-foot clearance from back of sidewalk to transformer pad edges at all locations where sidewalks are adjacent to transformer pads."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer Pad 1 is located near a sidewalk easement on the western property edge. The plan indicates a 'Sidewalk Easement' and '5' Concrete Sidewalk' but the distance from the transformer pad to the back of the sidewalk is not dimensioned. The minimum 2-foot clearance from the back of sidewalk cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows transformer pads and parking areas but no specific dimension lines measure distances from pads to nearby parking spaces and drive aisles. If any pad is within 4 feet of parking/traffic, 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollard specifications and spacing cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.38","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows transformer pads and parking areas. Specific dimension lines measuring distances from each transformer pad to nearby parking spaces and drive aisles are not provided. No bollard details or protective barrier specifications are shown on the electrical plan or referenced in detail sheets. If any pad is located within 4 feet of parking/traffic areas, required 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal post specifications and spacing cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"West-central transformer pad is positioned between building and parking aisle. No dimensions are provided showing clearance to parking area. No bollards are detailed. Applicant must either: (1) provide dimensioned plan showing transformer pad is more than 4 feet from parking area edge, OR (2) provide AE Design equipment pad detail sheets with 4-inch diameter galvanized rigid metal bollard specifications and site plan showing bollard placement and spacing to allow equipment door opening."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"When transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle circulation routes, 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollards are required per AE Design specifications. No bollard specifications, details, or locations are shown on the electrical or site plans. Whether transformer pads are within the 4-foot threshold of parking cannot be definitively confirmed from the submitted plans."}]},{"text":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pads but no dimension lines measure distances between any pair of pads. 5-foot minimum clearance between transformer pads cannot be verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.20","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows four transformer pads, but no dimension lines measure distances between any pair of pads. The 5-foot minimum clearance between transformer pads cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Four transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan but no clearance dimensions are provided between any of them. Applicant must provide dimensioned plan showing minimum 5-foot clearance between each transformer pad pair."}]},{"text":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads but does not clearly identify all light pole locations or measure distances between pads and light poles. 5-foot minimum clearance from light poles cannot be verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.18","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not clearly identify all light pole locations or show dimension lines measuring distances between light poles and transformer pads. The 5-foot minimum clearance from light poles cannot be verified from available evidence."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Light pole locations are not specifically dimensioned relative to transformer pads on the site plan. Applicant must provide photometric plan or lighting detail sheets showing all light pole locations and dimensions demonstrating minimum 5-foot clearance to transformer pad edges."}]},{"text":"Fire Protection Plan shows fire lanes with dimensions but no dimension lines measure distances from transformer pad locations to fire lane boundaries. 15-foot minimum clearance from fire lanes cannot be verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.19","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire Protection Plan shows fire lanes with dimensions, but no dimension lines measure distances from transformer pad locations to the fire lane boundaries. The 15-foot minimum clearance from fire lanes cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire lanes are not specifically delineated or dimensioned on the fire protection plan relative to transformer pad locations. Applicant must identify which internal driveways are designated fire lanes and provide dimensioned plan showing minimum 15-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to fire lane boundaries."}]},{"text":"Fire Protection Plan identifies fire hydrant locations but no dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pads to fire hydrants. 5-foot minimum clearance cannot be verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.12","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire Protection Plan shows 3 fire hydrant locations (1 existing, 2 proposed). No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pads to fire hydrants. The 5-foot minimum clearance from fire hydrants cannot be verified from submitted evidence."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire hydrant location and transformer pad location are identified but clearance distance is not dimensioned. Provide dimensioned plan showing minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to fire hydrant structure."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows bicycle parking locations but no dimension lines measure clearance distances from transformer pad locations to bicycle parking areas. 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.17","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan and landscape plan show bicycle parking locations. No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pad locations to any bicycle parking areas. The 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Fire Protection Plan identifies fire exit requirements but no stairwells serving fire exits are explicitly labeled. No dimension lines show clearance distances from transformer pads to stairwell locations. 5-foot minimum clearance cannot be verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.8","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire Protection Plan identifies fire exit requirements. No stairwells are explicitly labeled on the site plan as serving fire exits. Dimension lines from transformer pads to any potential stairwell locations are not shown. The 5-foot minimum clearance from stairwells cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Niche service configuration specifications not documented","summary":"If transformer pads are located in niche service configuration (accessible from outside but within building footprint), required cross-section drawings and specifications are not provided. 35-foot vertical clearance inside niche and 3-hour fire wall rating with ventilation specifications are not documented. Niche configuration cannot be verified.","sheets":[9,21],"applicableArea":"Building Envelope","severity":1,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Architecture / Fire (niche fire rating and ventilation design); Austin Energy Design (configuration approval)","attn":"Conditional finding — only applicable if transformer pads are proposed in niche configuration. Applicant must confirm whether niche service is proposed. If yes, provide cross-sections showing 35-foot clearance and documentation of 3-hour fire wall rating and ventilation specifications.","details":[{"text":"No cross-section drawings or elevation views showing whether transformer pads are located in niches, vaults, or enclosed areas were provided. No documentation of 35-foot vertical clearance inside niche and niche entrance if applicable. Confined space configuration cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.11","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No cross-section drawings or elevation views showing whether any transformer pads are located in niches, vaults, or enclosed areas were provided. No documentation of 35-foot vertical clearance inside niche and niche entrance if applicable. Confined space configuration cannot be verified from submitted plans."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in areas with building overhangs, enclosed configurations, or notched-out areas adjacent to transformer locations. Provide cross-section drawings for any transformer location adjacent to building elements that might create a confined space configuration requiring 15-foot hot-stick clearance and 35-foot vertical clearance in niche."}]},{"text":"No niche service configuration is identified on submitted plans. No documentation of 3-hour fire wall rating, ventilation specifications, or Austin Energy Design consultation appears in any sheet or supplementary document. If niche service configuration is proposed, required fire rating and ventilation specifications are not demonstrated.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.30","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No niche service is identified on submitted plans. No documentation of 3-hour fire wall rating, ventilation specifications, or Austin Energy Design business unit consultation appears in any sheet or supplementary document. If a niche service configuration is proposed, required fire rating and ventilation specifications are not demonstrated."}]}]},{"headline":"Fire escape clearance requirement not applicable to project","summary":"Fire Protection Plan shows no fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes on any of the eight proposed buildings. 20-foot clearance requirement for oil-filled equipment from fire escapes is not applicable because the triggering condition (fire escapes present) does not exist on site.","sheets":[10],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":0,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows no fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes. No such features appear on the buildings. Requirement to maintain 20-foot clearance from oil-filled equipment is not triggered.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.9","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) shows no fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes. No such features appear on the buildings. Requirement to maintain 20-foot clearance from oil-filled equipment is not applicable as the triggering condition (fire escapes/stairs serving as fire exits) is not present."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"902bd2e1-82f8-4f8c-aea8-45cebee6af98"}
