{"level":30,"time":1778189428980,"pid":123,"hostname":"082c71e6-af9","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR25FSCW0HPK8XMENDD8W5V1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0127w1Mkx8jaB56kCLpcBhY9","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"comments":[{"headline":"Horizontal Sky-to-Ground Clearance Dimensions Missing","summary":"Dimension annotations showing the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric lines are not provided for buildings, structures, and site features. Without these dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","sheets":[4,9,11,21,31],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Applies across multiple site features (buildings, projections, fences, walkways, lighting, utilities). Surveyed conductor locations required to establish baseline for dimensional verification.","details":[{"text":"Building elevation sheets showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations and dimensioned clearances from outside conductor are not provided. The required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.1","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings do not have building elevation sheets showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations and dimensioned clearances from outside conductor. Without surveyed conductor location and elevation data, the required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on existing conditions survey and are shown on proposed site plan along western and southern property boundaries. However, no clearance dimension annotations are provided showing the horizontal sky-to-ground distance from the outside conductor to any building faces. Surveyed conductor locations and dimensions are required to verify 7.5-foot minimum clearance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric (OHE) line is shown on site plan (Sheet 9) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) running along the southern property boundary with utility poles visible, but no horizontal sky-to-ground clearance dimensions are provided for any buildings. Buildings 7 and 8 are identified as closest to the OHE line. Without dimension annotations showing the distance from the outside conductor to building walls, compliance with the 7.5-foot minimum horizontal clearance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Building elevation or section views are not provided showing projections (overhangs, balconies, roof details) and their clearances from overhead conductors. Clearance verification from the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground envelope cannot be assessed.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.3","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation or section views provided showing building projections (overhangs, balconies, roof details) and their clearances from overhead electric conductors. Clearance verification from both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial envelopes cannot be assessed."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets or section views are provided showing building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs) in relation to overhead electric conductors. Without these exhibits, the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for projections cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Driveways and pedestrian walkways shown on site plan lack section or plan view exhibits with dimension lines showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric distribution facilities.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.5","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows driveways and pedestrian walkways but provides no section or plan view exhibits showing 15-foot radial clearance dimensions from overhead electric distribution facilities to the edges of these elevated features or walkways."}]},{"text":"Fence locations shown on site and landscape plans lack dimension annotations demonstrating 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of overhead electric facilities.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.9","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fence locations are shown on site plan and landscape plan, but no dimension annotations demonstrate 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor of overhead electric facilities. Dimension lines are not provided from the conductor to fence faces."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Fences are proposed on site plan, and overhead electric lines exist. However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that fences maintain the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows wooden privacy fence (H.6 notation) located along the southern property boundary in the vicinity of the overhead electric (OHE) line. No clearance dimensions are provided showing that the fence maintains the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of the overhead electric facilities."}]},{"text":"Fire lanes and emergency access structures shown on site plan lack section views with clearance dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric facilities.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.16","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows fire lanes and emergency access routes (Sheet 10) but does not provide section views with clearance dimension annotations from outside conductor of overhead electric facilities showing both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained for emergency access structures."}]},{"text":"Trash receptacle and enclosure locations shown on site plan lack dimension annotations demonstrating 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric facilities when trash bins are raised during service.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.26","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Trash receptacles and enclosure areas are shown on site plan, but no dimension annotations demonstrate that trash areas maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric facilities when trash bins are raised during service."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Trash enclosure locations are shown on site plan. Overhead electric lines are present. However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that trash enclosures maintain the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance considering trash bin raised height during service."}]},{"text":"Electric easements are shown on plat and grading plan with recorded 5-foot dimensions, but dimension annotations do not demonstrate that items within easements maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.27","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Electric easements are shown on plat (Sheet 2) and grading plan (Sheet 11) with recorded 5' electric easement dimensions noted. However, the site plan does NOT provide clearance dimension annotations demonstrating that items within electric easements maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor as required."}]},{"text":"Water meter locations shown on electrical plan lack clearance dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of overhead electric service-drop conductors.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3; UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.28","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility tap plans (Sheets 19-20) show water and wastewater connections but do not show water meter locations or service drops with clearance dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor of overhead electric service-drop conductors."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Water meter locations are shown on the electrical design plan (Sheet 21). However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that water meters maintain the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric service-drop conductors."}]},{"text":"Photometric and landscape plans show decorative and site lighting fixtures but do not provide clearance verification dimensions from overhead electric lines showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearances.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.36","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Photometric plan and landscape plan show site lighting but do not provide clearance verification dimensions from overhead electric lines to decorative or site lighting fixtures showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances."}]}]},{"headline":"15-Foot Radial Clearance Dimensions Not Provided","summary":"Dimension annotations demonstrating the required 15-foot radial clearance from the outside conductor of distribution primary and neutral conductors are absent. This prevents verification that buildings, structures, and site features comply.","sheets":[9,11,22],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Radial clearance verification requires both surveyed conductor locations and three-dimensional dimensional exhibits. Multiple site features require demonstration of radial compliance.","details":[{"text":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines but provides no dimension annotations or clearance verification exhibits showing 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of distribution primary and neutral conductors to proposed buildings and site features.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.2","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines but provides no dimension annotations or clearance verification exhibits showing 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of distribution primary and neutral conductors to proposed buildings and site features."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution facilities are shown on site plan, but no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that customer facilities (buildings, structures) maintain the minimum 15-foot radial clearance from the outside conductor of primary and neutral conductors. Surveyed conductor locations are required."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution conductors are present on the southern boundary. The site plans do not provide clearance annotations showing that the minimum 15-foot radial clearance from the outside conductor is maintained. No dimension lines, radial clearance arcs, or verified distances are shown for any customer facilities (buildings, structures) relative to the distribution line."}]},{"text":"Driveways and pedestrian paths lack dimension annotations showing 15-foot radial clearance from overhead electric distribution facilities to edges of these features or walkways.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.5","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows driveways and pedestrian walkways but provides no section or plan view exhibits showing 15-foot radial clearance dimensions from overhead electric distribution facilities to the edges of these elevated features or walkways."}]},{"text":"Driveway posts and barriers shown near overhead lines lack section exhibits showing vertical and horizontal clearance verification dimensions from outermost electric line to barrier posts.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.13","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Driveway posts/barriers may exist near overhead lines, but no section exhibits showing vertical and horizontal clearance verification dimensions from outermost electric line to barrier posts are provided."}]}]},{"headline":"Building Elevation Sheets & Surveyed Conductor Data Missing","summary":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations, locations, and dimensions are provided. Registered surveyor-certified mid-span clearance verification data is absent. These are mandatory for vertical and three-dimensional clearance compliance verification.","sheets":[7,8,9,11,31],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Surveying firm must provide surveyed conductor locations and mid-span elevation data; coordination with electrical utility required.","attn":"Critical documentation gap. Surveyed elevation data from registered surveyor is explicitly required by UCM § 1.10.3 when vertical clearances may not meet minimums. This blocks clearance verification for multiple site features.","details":[{"text":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors with clearance dimensions to building faces and projections are included in the site plan set. Only architectural plan views are provided (Sheet 29) without elevation details.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.7","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan set that show surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors with clearance dimensions to building faces and projections. Only architectural plan views are provided (Sheet 29) without elevation details."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are included in the site plan package. Code requires registered surveyor data showing conductor elevations to verify that required clearances from buildings are met."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are included in the plan set. The electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and site plan (Sheet 9) show building locations and the overhead electric line, but neither includes elevation data for the conductors with dimension lines to verify required vertical clearances."}]},{"text":"Site plan provides plan-view exhibits only, lacking section and enlarged detail views with dimension lines showing clearances from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings and building projections (overhangs, awnings, decks, roofs).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.8","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Site plan shows buildings and overhead electric lines in plan view on multiple sheets but provides no section or enlarged plan detail views with dimension lines showing clearances from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings and building projections."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Section and plan view exhibits with dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to building edges and projections are not provided. Code requires dimensioned clearance exhibits showing the measurement from outside conductor to outermost extent of buildings and projections."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Plan and section view exhibits are absent. The site plan (Sheet 9) shows the overhead electric line and buildings in plan view only, with no dimension lines from the outside conductor to the outermost edges of buildings. No cross-sections, profile views, or enlarged details showing clearance dimensions from conductor to building faces are provided."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows two main driveways crossing overhead electric lines on southern boundary with no surveyed conductor elevation data or mid-span clearance documentation provided. Registered surveyor's mid-span clearance verification is required but absent.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.31","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Site plan shows two main driveways crossing overhead electric lines on southern boundary with no surveyed conductor elevation data or mid-span clearance documentation provided. Given the absence of any vertical clearance dimensions and the presence of OHE lines crossing driveways, a registered surveyor's mid-span clearance verification is required but not provided. UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires this documentation when vertical clearances may not meet minimums."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No registered surveyor data showing pole locations and mid-span clearances is provided in the site plan package. Code requires surveyor-certified mid-span clearance verification when existing overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 16-18 feet for driveways). Without this data, vertical clearances cannot be verified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric line is present on the southern boundary with buildings and driveways nearby. The clearances from site features to the overhead line appear marginal based on the site plan visual layout, but no registered surveyor data is provided showing pole locations and mid-span clearances. Without surveyed elevation data, compliance with vertical clearance requirements cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Buildings maintain setback from property lines where electric easements are recorded, but no surveyed clearance dimensions from outside conductor to building faces are provided to demonstrate both 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances as permanent requirements.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.6","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings maintain setback from property lines where electric easements are recorded, but no surveyed clearance dimensions from outside conductor to building faces are provided to demonstrate both 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained as permanent requirements per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric facilities exist in the Valley View Road right-of-way adjacent to the site. Buildings are proposed adjacent to this ROW, but no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate maintenance of the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from these ROW facilities."}]}]},{"headline":"Driveway Vertical Clearance Dimensions Missing","summary":"Driveways crossing or located beneath overhead electric lines lack vertical clearance dimension annotations from the lowest point of overhead facilities to finished driveway grades. Minimum clearances are 16 feet (parking without truck traffic) or 18 feet (areas with truck traffic).","sheets":[9,11,22],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Surveying/utilities coordination required for vertical clearance field verification and documentation.","attn":"Two main driveways cross overhead lines on southern boundary. Grading and section plans do not show vertical clearance margins. Mid-span surveyor verification is critical.","details":[{"text":"Two main site entrances (Type II driveways) cross the overhead electric line on the southern boundary. Grading plan and section views do not show vertical clearance dimensions from lowest point of overhead facilities to finished driveway grades. No mid-span clearance verification survey data is provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.18","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Two main site entrances (Type II Driveways) cross the overhead electric line on the southern boundary. Grading plan and section views do not show vertical clearance dimensions from lowest point of overhead facilities to finished driveway grades. No mid-span clearance verification survey data from registered surveyor is provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Driveways are proposed on the site plan, and overhead electric lines exist. However, no vertical clearance dimension annotations are provided showing the clearance from the lowest point of the overhead facilities to finished driveway grades. Code requires 16 feet minimum (parking without truck traffic) or 18 feet (areas with truck traffic). Mid-span clearance verification from registered surveyor is not provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Driveways are shown on the site plan in proximity to overhead electric facilities. Minimum 16-foot vertical clearance (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot vertical clearance (areas with truck traffic) is required, but no vertical clearance dimensions are provided. Grading plan shows finished floor elevations but not vertical clearance from driveways to the lowest point of overhead facilities."}]},{"text":"Vehicle parking areas are proposed on site plan beneath overhead electric lines. No vertical clearance dimension annotations show clearance from the lowest point of overhead facilities to parking areas. Code requires 12-18 feet depending on use.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.19","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Vehicle parking areas are proposed on site plan, and overhead electric lines are present. However, no vertical clearance dimension annotations are shown from the lowest point of overhead facilities to parking areas. Code requires compliance with clearance requirements (minimum 12-18 feet depending on use)."}]}]},{"headline":"No Clearance Dimensions From Outer Conductor on Any Plan Sheet","summary":"The site plan shows overhead electric facilities but provides zero clearance dimension annotations on any sheet. This is a fundamental documentation failure: dimensions must originate from the outside conductor, not pole centerline, per code.","sheets":[4,9,11,31],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"All utility clearance work must involve electrical utility coordination and surveying.","attn":"Critical administrative and technical deficiency. When dimensions are provided, they must be measured from the outside conductor, not pole centerline. On three-phase installations, the conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. No dimensions currently exist anywhere on the plans.","details":[{"text":"The site plan shows overhead electric facilities but provides NO clearance dimensions on any sheet. Where clearances must be annotated from the outside conductor to building edges, driveways, or other site features per UCM § 1.10.3, NO DIMENSIONS are provided. This is a fundamental documentation failure preventing any clearance verification.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.23","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"The site plan shows overhead electric facilities but provides NO clearance dimensions at all on any sheet. Where clearances should be annotated from the outside conductor to building edges, driveways, or other site features per UCM § 1.10.3 and the grouping guidance (dimensions must originate from outer conductor, not pole centerline), NO DIMENSIONS are provided. This is a fundamental documentation failure preventing any clearance verification."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electric lines and utility poles are shown on the site plan, but NO clearance dimensions are annotated on any sheets (site plan, grading plan, or other exhibits). When clearance dimensions are eventually provided, they must be measured from the outside conductor, not from pole centerline or pole structure. Code requires dimensions originating from conductor location."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any plan sheets. The site plan and landscape plan identify the overhead electric (OHE) line but provide zero dimension annotations measuring clearances from the outside conductor to any site features. Conductor may be several feet offset from pole center on three-phase installations. This project provides no dimensions at all."}]}]},{"headline":"Retaining Wall Clearance Documentation Incomplete","summary":"Retaining walls located near overhead electric lines lack both horizontal clearance dimension annotations and section view exhibits showing clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to the outermost edge of the walls.","sheets":[9,11,38,39],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"Concrete retaining wall identified along southern boundary near overhead electric line. Multiple wall locations shown on grading and detail plans. Specific wall sections must show clearance dimensions in cross-section views.","details":[{"text":"Retaining walls shown on grading plan and detail sheets, including walls adjacent to overhead electric lines, lack clearance dimensions from outermost electric line to wall faces. Measurement from conductor cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.14","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are shown on grading plan (Sheet 11) and detail sheets (Sheets 38-39), including walls adjacent to areas with overhead electric lines, but no clearance dimensions from outermost electric line to wall faces are dimensioned. Measurement from conductor (not pole) cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are shown on grading and wall plan sheets. Overhead electric lines are shown on existing conditions and site plan. However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that retaining walls maintain the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outermost electric line."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan indicates 'Concrete Retaining Wall' located along the southern boundary where the overhead electric (OHE) line runs. No clearance dimensions are provided showing that the retaining wall maintains the minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside electric line."}]},{"text":"Retaining wall detail sheets (38-39) show structural sections and dimensions but lack section view exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of retaining wall faces where overhead facilities exist.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.17","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Retaining wall detail sheets (38-39) show structural sections and dimensions but lack any section view exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of retaining wall faces where overhead electric facilities exist adjacent to wall locations."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Section exhibits are provided for retaining walls (Sheets 38-39), but they do not include dimension annotations showing clearance distances from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of the walls. Code requires dimensioned section exhibits demonstrating clearance compliance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining wall is shown on site plan along the southern boundary near overhead electric facilities, but section exhibits showing clearance dimensions from the outside electric conductor to the outermost edge of the wall are not provided on the wall detail sheets (Sheets 38-39)."}]}]},{"headline":"Pole Clearances & Guy Wire Issues Not Documented","summary":"Utility pole locations, guy wire anchor points, and required clearances to proposed site features (fences, driveways, sidewalks, lighting) are not clearly depicted or dimensioned. Guy wire anchor easements are not shown. Pole relocation or conversion notes are absent.","sheets":[2,4,9,31],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Utility company coordination required for pole relocation, conversion to self-supporting, and guy wire easement verification.","attn":"Down guy wires and anchors shown on existing conditions survey but not clearly identified on proposed plans. Crossing angle of overhead line relative to driveway alignment cannot be verified. Streetlight pole locations from adjacent properties not clearly dimensioned relative to proposed buildings.","details":[{"text":"Utility poles are shown on existing conditions survey and site plan, but no dimension annotations demonstrate that fence posts maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from electric poles.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.10","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility poles are shown on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) and site plan (Sheet 9), and fences are shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31), but no dimension annotations demonstrate that fence posts maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from electric poles."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing utility poles are shown on the existing conditions survey. Proposed fences are shown on site plan. However, no dimension annotations show the horizontal clearance distance from fence post locations to existing electric poles. Code requires minimum 10-foot clearance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Wooden privacy fence is shown on landscape plan near the southern boundary where overhead electric poles exist. The minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from fence posts to electric poles cannot be verified from the plans, as no dimension annotations showing distances from fence posts to pole locations are provided."}]},{"text":"Two main site driveways are immediately adjacent to overhead electric utility poles on the southern boundary. No dimension annotations show 30-foot minimum clearance from driveway edge to pole locations. Pole relocation notes are not provided.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.22","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Two main site driveways cross or are immediately adjacent to overhead electric utility poles and lines on the southern boundary (visible on Sheet 9 vision analysis). No dimension annotations show 30-foot minimum clearance from driveway edge to pole locations, and no pole relocation notes are provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing electric poles are shown on existing conditions survey. Proposed driveways are shown on site plan. However, no dimension annotations demonstrate the horizontal distance from driveway edges to existing poles, and no notes indicate whether poles will be relocated minimum 30 feet from driveway edges."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows overhead electric line crossing the property, but the angle of crossing relative to driveway alignment is not annotated. Cannot determine if crossings are perpendicular to driveway centerlines as required.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.32","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines cross the property and site driveways on plan view, but the angle of crossing relative to roadway alignment is not annotated or verified. Cannot determine if crossings are perpendicular to driveway centerlines as required."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines cross Valley View Road at the site property boundary. However, no angle dimension annotation demonstrates that the crossing is oriented at 90-degree angle to the road centerline as required."}]},{"text":"Existing conditions survey shows at least one down guy wire, but the site plan does not clearly identify all guy wire locations. No notes indicate whether conflicts with proposed accessible paths, driveways, and site features have been resolved through pole relocation or conversion.","citation":"UCM § 1.17.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.40","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows at least one down guy wire symbol at bottom-left corner (visible in vision analysis), but site plan and grading plan do not identify all guy wire locations or verify that proposed accessible paths, driveways, and site features do not conflict with guy anchor points. No pole relocation or conversion notes are provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows down guy wires (e.g., AT&T pole with guy wire shown). However, proposed site plan does not clearly depict existing down guy wire locations, and there are no notes indicating whether conflicts with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or site features have been identified and resolved through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles."}]},{"text":"Plat and grading plan do not show dedicated guy anchor easements with the required 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry point. Down guy anchors shown on existing conditions survey lack easement depiction.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.42","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows at least one down guy wire and anchor, but the plat (Sheet 2) and grading plan do not show dedicated guy anchor easements with the required 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry point as required by Austin Energy Transmission Engineering Standards."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Down guy anchors are visible on existing conditions survey (utilities shown with guy wires). However, no down guy anchor easements are depicted on the easement exhibits or site plan. Code requires dedicated easements 10 feet wide extending 5 feet past where down guy enters the ground. Without easement depiction, the requirement cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows sidewalk along Valley View Road western frontage but does not provide dimension annotations showing sidewalk clearance from existing utility poles at property line.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.25","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows sidewalk along Valley View Road (western frontage) but does not provide dimension annotations showing sidewalk clearance from existing utility poles at property line. Cannot verify that sidewalk is cleared from poles at each end of property."}]},{"text":"Existing conditions survey shows utility features but does not clearly identify or dimension streetlight pole locations adjacent to property with proposed building clearances.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.39","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utilities and existing features but does not clearly identify or dimension streetlight pole locations adjacent to property with proposed building clearances."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows fire lanes and potential lighting areas but does not provide photometric plan or explicit streetlight pole locations with clearance verification relative to overhead electric lines.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.24","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows fire lanes and potential lighting areas but does not provide photometric plan or explicit streetlight pole locations with clearance verification relative to overhead electric lines."}]}]},{"headline":"Service Infrastructure Details Missing or Incomplete","summary":"Meter working space clearances, transformer clearances, and service mast roof penetration details are not documented with required dimensional exhibits or working space verification. Underground service conversion pole locations are not shown.","sheets":[21,35],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Electrical service provider coordination required for service infrastructure final design and clearance verification.","attn":"Meter locations shown on electrical plan but no enlarged details showing 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom clearances. Transformers and service masts lack elevation/section detail exhibits.","details":[{"text":"Preliminary electrical design plan shows meter locations but does not provide enlarged meter area details showing clearance from obstructions (fences, walls, landscaping, building projections) required for meter access, installation, and working space (30-inch-wide front, 36-inch depth, 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9).","citation":"UCM § 1.9.3.1","sourceId":"1:EL-1.38","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows meter locations on site but does not provide enlarged meter area details showing clearance from obstructions (fences, walls, landscaping, building projections) that would conflict with meter access, installation, and required 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Meter locations are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21). However, no detailed site plan or meter area enlargement is provided showing working clearances around meter locations. Code requires 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9, free of obstructions including fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, and building projections."}]},{"text":"Preliminary electrical design plan shows transformer locations but does not provide section views with vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to top of transformer equipment showing 7.5-foot minimum vertical sky-to-ground clearance.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.43","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer locations on site but does not provide section views with vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to top of transformer equipment showing 7.5-foot minimum vertical sky-to-ground clearance."}]},{"text":"Preliminary electrical design plan shows electrical infrastructure but does not provide building elevation drawings showing service mast locations and roof clearance dimensions (3-foot minimum above roof, or 18-inch if mast within 4 feet of roof edge, for voltages ≤300V).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.47","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows electrical infrastructure but does not provide building elevation drawings showing service mast locations and roof clearance dimensions (3-foot minimum above roof, or 18-inch if mast within 4 feet of roof edge, for voltages ≤300V)."}]},{"text":"Preliminary electrical design plan shows underground service infrastructure but does not show any new power pole locations for underground service conversion or document clearances from new poles to existing poles if applicable.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.35","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground service infrastructure but does not show any new power pole locations for underground service conversion or document clearances from new poles to existing poles if applicable."}]}]},{"headline":"Water System Clearances Not Verified","summary":"Water meter locations and water line routing shown on utility plans lack clearance dimension annotations demonstrating compliance with overhead electric line separation and service drop clearance requirements.","sheets":[19,20,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Utility company and water department coordination required for final routing and clearance verification.","attn":"Water meter locations visible on electrical plan but no sections or dimensional exhibits verify 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from service drops. Water line routing beneath or adjacent to overhead distribution lines not dimensioned.","details":[{"text":"Utility tap plans showing water meter locations and service drops lack clearance dimension annotations demonstrating minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor of overhead electric service-drop conductors.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.29","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility tap plans show water line routing but do not provide dimension annotations or clearance notes demonstrating minimum clearance from proposed water lines to overhead electrical distribution facilities shown on site plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Water lines are shown on utility plans. Overhead distribution lines are shown on site plan. However, no clearance dimension annotations demonstrate that water lines maintain required clearances from overhead distribution facilities."}]},{"text":"Building foundations shown on site plan, some within or near 5-foot distance from property lines where electric facilities may be required in adjacent ROW or property, lack dimension annotations showing clearance space from property line to building foundation for necessary electric facility maintenance and access.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.30","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings 5-8 are shown near the eastern property boundary where electric facilities exist in adjacent ROW/easements. No clearance space verification is provided showing that building setbacks allow necessary clearance for electric facility installation and maintenance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building foundations are shown on site plan, some within or near 5-foot distance from property lines where electric facilities may be required in adjacent ROW or property. However, no dimension annotations show the clearance space from property line to building foundation to verify that adequate room exists for necessary electric facility maintenance and access."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility-Compatible Tree Species Not Verified","summary":"Landscape plan shows proposed tree plantings, including mitigation trees ('M' designation) near overhead electric lines. Tree species are not identified. Cannot verify that trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors are from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, UC column).","sheets":[31,32,35],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":1,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Landscape architect and arborist coordination required for species verification and clearance dimensioning.","attn":"Mitigation trees shown on landscape plan along southern boundary but species not identified on sheets. Trees must be verified as utility-compatible (generally mature height ≤20 feet) per ECM § 2.4.1.D and § 2.4.2.C. Lateral distances from tree locations to conductors not dimensioned.","details":[{"text":"Landscape plan shows proposed tree plantings within what appears to be 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors. Specific tree species are not identified on the landscape plan. Tree species verification against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible trees list (generally mature height ≤20 feet) cannot be performed. No clearance distance annotations are provided.","citation":"ECM § 2.4.1.D; ECM § 2.4.2.C; UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"1:EL-1.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed tree plantings but does not verify that trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors are from Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (ECM Appendix F, UC column), nor does it measure lateral distances from tree locations to conductors. Required clearance distances are not annotated."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Trees are proposed on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) within what appears to be 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors based on visual spacing and symbol overlap. However, the specific species of these proposed trees are not identified on the landscape plan. Tree species verification against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible trees list (generally mature height ≤20 feet) cannot be performed without this information."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows mitigation trees (designated 'M') located near the overhead electric (OHE) line on the southern boundary. The species of these trees and whether they are from the ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible Shade Trees list cannot be verified from the landscape plan. No clearance verification or species identification is provided for trees within the 10-foot lateral distance requirement from overhead distribution conductors."}]}]},{"headline":"Construction Safety & Notification Documentation Missing","summary":"No 48-hour notification requirement note is included on the cover sheet or general notes as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752. No construction staging plan or site logistics plan is provided showing equipment clearances from energized overhead lines.","sheets":[1,3,5],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Construction safety and site logistics plan must be coordinated with utility company and contractor. General notes on cover sheet are cross-departmental requirement.","attn":"Sheet 3 mentions pre-construction meeting with Andrew Perez 48 hours before construction, but the explicit 48-hour notification requirement is not stated on cover sheet or general notes as required by code. No construction staging or equipment operation zones defined relative to overhead lines.","details":[{"text":"Required note regarding 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage overhead lines is NOT included on the cover sheet or general notes. While Sheet 3 mentions a pre-construction safety meeting, UCM § 1.10.2 requires this notification requirement explicitly noted on cover sheet or general notes per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.46","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Required note regarding 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage overhead lines is NOT included on the cover sheet or general notes. While Sheet 3 (Electric Transmission Notes) mentions a pre-construction safety meeting with Andrew Perez 48 hours before construction, UCM § 1.10.2 requires this notification requirement to be explicitly noted on the cover sheet or general notes plan. The cover sheet (Sheet 1) lacks this required note."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on site and construction activities are proposed. However, no note is provided on the cover sheet or general notes requiring that the owner/contractor notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"The general notes on Sheet 3 do not include a required note stating that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. While Sheet 3 contains extensive Austin Energy requirements and Electric Transmission Notes, the specific 48-hour notification requirement for overhead distribution lines is not explicitly stated as a general note."}]},{"text":"No site logistics plan, construction phasing plan, or construction staging plan is provided showing construction staging areas, crane swing radius, material storage, or scaffold locations with 10-foot radial clearance verification from energized overhead lines as required by OSHA and UCM § 1.10.2.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.45","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 3 references construction sequence and staging notes. Sheet 5 shows erosion control plan. However, no site logistics plan or construction phasing plan is provided showing construction staging areas, crane swing radius, material storage, or scaffold locations with 10-foot radial clearance verification from energized overhead lines as required by OSHA and UCM § 1.10.2."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on and adjacent to the site. Construction activities are proposed. However, no construction staging plan, site logistics plan, or phasing plan is provided in the submitted site plan package showing construction staging area boundaries, crane swing radius, or material storage locations relative to overhead electric lines. Code requires 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines for construction activities."}]}]}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a7fd24c-676b-498c-9f16-8216c5e40215","uuid":"992b0de6-9630-4792-b9cb-b4b75658a8ff"}
